      "a": 1,
      "s": "JEE Main 2026 (Online) 2nd April Morning Shift. Correct option: B. Young's modulus $(Y)$ is defined as the ratio of longitudinal stress to longitudinal strain.\n\nLet $F$ be the force, $L$ the original length, $A$ the cross-sectional area, and $\\Delta L$ the extension.\n\n$$ Y = \\frac{\\text{Stress}}{\\text{Strain}} = \\frac{F/A}{\\Delta L/L} = \\frac{FL}{A\\Delta L} $$\n\nFor a wire of diameter $D$, the area $A = \\frac{\\pi D^2}{4}$.\n\nSubstituting this into the formula:\n\n$$ Y = \\frac{FL}{\\left(\\frac{\\pi D^2}{4}\\right)\\Delta L} = \\frac{4FL}{\\pi D^2\\Delta L} $$\n\nTo find the absolute error in $Y$, we need to find the relative error.\n\nSince $F$ and $\\pi$ are constants, the relative error in $Y$ is:\n\n$$ \\frac{\\Delta Y}{Y} = \\frac{\\Delta L_{\\text{scale}}}{L} + \\frac{2\\Delta D}{D} + \\frac{\\Delta (\\Delta L)}{\\Delta L} $$\n\nWhere $\\Delta L_{\\text{scale}}$, $\\Delta D$, and $\\Delta (\\Delta L)$ are the least counts of the respective measuring instruments.\n\nThe applied tensile force is $F = 100\\ \\text{N}$,\n\nThe length of wire is $L = 150\\ \\text{cm} = 1.5\\ \\text{m}$,\n\nThe diameter of wire is $D = 0.08\\ \\text{cm} = 8 \\times 10^{-4}\\ \\text{m}$,\n\nThe extension in the length of wire is $\\Delta L = 0.5\\ \\text{cm} = 5 \\times 10^{-3}\\ \\text{m}$.\n\n$$ Y = \\frac{4 \\times 100 \\times 1.5}{\\pi \\times (8 \\times 10^{-4})^2 \\times 5 \\times 10^{-3}} $$\n\n$$ Y = \\frac{600}{\\pi \\times 64 \\times 10^{-8} \\times 5 \\times 10^{-3}} = \\frac{600}{\\pi \\times 320 \\times 10^{-11}} = \\frac{6 \\times 10^{11}}{3.2\\pi} $$\n\n$$ Y \\approx 5.96 \\times 10^{10}\\ \\text{N/m}^2 $$\n\nSo, the error in measurement of Young’s modulus is $(\\Delta Y)$:\n\n$$ \\Delta Y = Y\\left[\\frac{0.1}{150} + 2\\left(\\frac{0.001}{0.08}\\right) + \\frac{0.001}{0.5}\\right] $$\n\n$$ \\Delta Y = Y\\left[0.00066 + 0.025 + 0.002\\right] = Y\\left[0.02766\\right] $$\n\n$$ \\Delta Y = (5.96 \\times 10^{10}) \\times 0.02766 \\approx 1.65 \\times 10^9\\ \\text{N/m}^2 $$\n\nTherefore, the value of $\\alpha$ is $1.65$. Thus, the correct option is (B).",
