      "a": 2,
      "s": "JEE Main 2026 (Online) 4th April Evening Shift. Correct option: C. The velocity of car $\\mathrm{A}, \\mathrm{V}_{\\mathrm{A}}=100 \\mathrm{~km} / \\mathrm{h}$\n\nThe velocity of car $\\mathrm{B}, \\mathrm{V}_{\\mathrm{B}}=80 \\mathrm{~km} / \\mathrm{h}$\n\nThe stone hits car $A$ with speed $5 \\mathrm{~m} / \\mathrm{s}$, i.e., relative speed with which the stone hits car $A, \\mathrm{v}_{\\mathrm{SA}}=5 \\mathrm{~m} / \\mathrm{s}$\n\nThe stone is thrown with speed v , i.e., the relative speed of the stone relative to car B is $\\mathrm{v}_{\\mathrm{SB}}=\\mathrm{v}$\n\nThe final speed is given in $\\mathrm{m} / \\mathrm{s}$, but we need to find the value of v in in $\\mathrm{km} / \\mathrm{h}$.\n\n$$ \\frac{1 \\mathrm{~m}}{\\mathrm{~s}}=\\frac{18}{5} \\mathrm{~km} / \\mathrm{h} $$\n\n$\\mathrm{v}_{\\mathrm{SA}}=5 \\times \\frac{18}{5}=18 \\mathrm{~km} / \\mathrm{h} \\ldots$ (i)\n\n[Diagram: JEE Main 2026 (Online) 4th April Evening Shift Physics - Motion in a Straight Line Question 2 English Explanation]\n\nWhen the person in car B throws the stone with speed v relative to the car, the actual velocity of the stone with respect to the ground $\\left(\\mathrm{V}_{\\mathrm{s}}\\right)$ is the sum of the car's velocity and the throw velocity:\n\n$$ v_{S B}=v_S-v_B=v \\Rightarrow v_s=v_B+v \\ldots (ii) $$\n\nThe stone hits car $A$ with a relative speed $v_{S A}$. The relative velocity of the stone with respect to car $A$ is:\n\n$$ \\mathrm{v}_{\\mathrm{SA}}=\\mathrm{v}_{\\mathrm{S}}-\\mathrm{v}_{\\mathrm{A}} .....(iii)$$\n\nSubstituting the expression for $\\mathrm{v}_{\\mathrm{s}}$ from equation (ii) :\n\n$$ v_{S A}=\\left(v_B+v\\right)-v_A $$\n\n$$\\Rightarrow $$ $$ \\mathrm{v}=\\mathrm{v}_{\\mathrm{sA}}+\\mathrm{v}_{\\mathrm{A}}-\\mathrm{v}_{\\mathrm{B}} $$\n\nSubstituting the values :\n\n$$ \\mathrm{v}=18+100-80 $$\n\n$$\\Rightarrow $$ $\\mathrm{v}=18+20$\n\n$$\\Rightarrow $$ $$ \\mathrm{v}=38 \\mathrm{~km} / \\mathrm{h} $$\n\nTherefore, the value of $v$ is $38 \\mathrm{~km} / \\mathrm{h}$.\n\nHence, the correct option is (C).",
      "source": "JEE Main 2026 (Online) 4th April Evening Shift | Motion in One Dimension | mnswhtf7",
      "pyq": true,
