      "s": "JEE Main 2015 (Offline). Correct option: A. Using $$h = ut + {1 \\over 2}g{t^2}$$\n\n$${y_1} = 10t - 5{t^2};\\,\\,{y_2} = 40t - 5{t^2}$$\n\n$$\\therefore$$ $$\\,\\,\\,\\,{y_2} - {y_1} = 30t\\,\\,\\,\\,$$ for $$\\,\\,\\,\\,t \\le 8s.$$\n\nCurve will be straight line when $$t \\le 8s.$$\n\nwhen stone 1 reaches the ground then $$\\,\\,\\,{y_1} = - 240m,\\,\\, and\\,\\, t = 8s$$\n\nfor $$\\,\\,\\,\\,t > 8s.$$\n\n$${y_2} - {y_1} = 40t + {1 \\over 2}g{t^2} - 240$$\n\nSo, it will be a parabolic curve till stone 2 reaches the ground. And parabola should opens upward as coefficient of t 2 is positive.",
