      "a": 3,
      "s": "JEE Main 2026 (Online) 4th April Evening Shift. Correct option: D. The mass of the body, $\\mathrm{m}=100 \\mathrm{~g}=0.1 \\mathrm{~kg}$\n\nThe constant force acting on the body, $\\vec{F}=(5 \\hat{\\imath}+10 \\hat{\\jmath}) N$\n\nThe time interval of motion, $\\mathrm{t}=2 \\mathrm{~s}$\n\nAs the body started from rest, so the initial velocity at $\\mathrm{t}=0, \\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{u}}=0$\n\nThe position at $\\mathrm{t}=2 \\mathrm{~s}, \\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{r}}=(2 \\mathrm{xi}+5 \\mathrm{y}) \\mathrm{j}) \\mathrm{m}$\n\nAccording to Newton's Second Law of Motion :\n\n$$ \\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{F}}=\\mathrm{m} \\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{a}} $$\n\n$$\\Rightarrow $$ $$ \\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{a}}=\\frac{\\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{F}}}{\\mathrm{~m}} $$\n\nSubstituting the values :\n\n$$ \\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{a}}=\\frac{5 \\hat{\\imath}+10 \\hat{\\jmath}}{0.1} $$\n\n$$\\Rightarrow $$ $$ \\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{a}}=(50 \\hat{\\imath}+100 \\hat{\\jmath}) \\mathrm{m} / \\mathrm{s}^2 $$\n\nFrom the second equation of motion for constant acceleration:\n\n$$ \\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{s}}=\\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{ut}}+\\frac{1}{2} \\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{a}} t^2 $$\n\nSince $\\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{u}}=0$ :\n\n$$ \\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{s}}=\\frac{1}{2} \\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{a}} \\mathrm{t}^2 $$\n\nSubstituting the acceleration and time :\n\n$$ \\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{s}}=\\frac{1}{2}(50 \\hat{\\imath}+100 \\hat{\\jmath})(2)^2 $$\n\n$$\\Rightarrow $$ $\\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{s}}=\\frac{1}{2}(50 \\hat{\\imath}+100 \\hat{\\jmath})(4)$\n\n$$\\Rightarrow $$ $\\vec{s}=2(50 \\hat{\\imath}+100 \\hat{\\jmath})$\n\n$$\\Rightarrow $$ $\\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{s}}=(100 i \\hat{\\imath}+200 \\hat{\\jmath}) \\mathrm{m}$\n\nOn comparing the calculated displacement with the given position $(2 x \\hat{i}+5 y \\hat{j})$ :\n\nFor the x -component: $2 \\mathrm{x}=100 \\Rightarrow \\mathrm{x}=50$\n\nFor the $y$-component: $5 y=200 \\Rightarrow y=40$\n\nSo, the required ratio is,\n\n$$ \\frac{x}{y}=\\frac{50}{40}=5: 4 $$\n\nTherefore, the ratio $\\mathrm{x}: \\mathrm{y}$ is $5: 4$.\n\nThus, the correct option is (D).",
      "source": "JEE Main 2026 (Online) 4th April Evening Shift | Motion in Two Dimensions | mnswhqph",
