      "a": 1,
      "s": "JEE Main 2026 (Online) 4th April Evening Shift. Correct option: B. Horizontal position of projectile is given as $\\mathrm{x}=24 \\mathrm{t}$\n\nVertical position of projectile is given as $\\mathrm{y}=43.6 \\mathrm{t}-4.9 \\mathrm{t}^2$\n\nVelocity is the rate of change of position with respect to time $\\left(\\vec{V}=\\frac{d \\vec{r}}{d t}\\right)$.\n\n[Diagram: JEE Main 2026 (Online) 4th April Evening Shift Physics - Motion in a Plane Question 2 English Explanation]\n\nFor the velocity component along horizontal, $\\left(\\mathrm{v}_{\\mathrm{x}}\\right)$ :\n\n$$ v_x=\\frac{d x}{d t}=\\frac{d}{d t}(24 t)=24 \\mathrm{~m} / \\mathrm{s} $$\n\nThe horizontal velocity remains constant throughout the motion.\n\nFor the velocity component along vertical, $\\left(\\mathrm{v}_{\\mathrm{y}}\\right)$ :\n\n$$ v_y=\\frac{d y}{d t}=\\frac{d}{d t}\\left(43.6 t-4.9 t^2\\right) $$\n\n$$\\Rightarrow $$ $\\mathrm{v}_{\\mathrm{y}}=43.6-(2 \\times 4.9) \\mathrm{t}$\n\n$$\\Rightarrow $$ $$ v_y=43.6-9.8 t $$\n\nSo, the velocities at $\\mathrm{t}=2 \\mathrm{~s}$ is,\n\n$$ \\mathrm{v}_{\\mathrm{x}}=24 \\mathrm{~m} / \\mathrm{s} $$\n\n$$\\Rightarrow $$ $$ \\mathrm{v}_{\\mathrm{y}}=43.6-9.8(2)=43.6-19.6=24 \\mathrm{~m} / \\mathrm{s} $$\n\nThe angle $\\theta$ that the velocity vector makes with the horizontal is given by\n\n$$ \\tan \\theta=\\frac{\\mathrm{v}_{\\mathrm{y}}}{\\mathrm{v}_{\\mathrm{x}}} $$\n\nSubstituting the values calculated for $\\mathrm{t}=2 \\mathrm{~s}$ :\n\n$$ \\tan \\theta=\\frac{24}{24} $$\n\n$$\\Rightarrow $$ $\\tan \\theta=1$\n\n$$\\Rightarrow $$ $$ \\theta=45^{\\circ} $$\n\nTherefore, the angle made by the projectile with the horizontal at $\\mathrm{t}=2 \\mathrm{~s}$ is $45^{\\circ}$.\n\nThus, the correct option is (B).",
      "source": "JEE Main 2026 (Online) 4th April Evening Shift | Motion in Two Dimensions | mnswhv5p",
