      "a": 1,
      "s": "JEE Main 2021 (Online) 1st September Evening Shift. Correct option: B. Here, two projectiles are projected at angles 42$$^\\circ$$ and 48$$^\\circ$$ with same initial velocity.\n\nAs we know the expression of range of projectile,\n\nRange $$ = {{{u^2}\\sin 2\\theta } \\over g}$$\n\nAT $$\\theta$$ 1 = 42$$^\\circ$$,\n\nRange, $${R_1} = {{{u^2}\\sin 2(42)^\\circ } \\over g} = {{0.99{u^2}} \\over g}$$\n\nAt $$\\theta$$ 2 = 48$$^\\circ$$\n\nRange, $${R_2} = {{{u^2}\\sin 2(48)^\\circ } \\over g} = {{0.99{u^2}} \\over g}$$\n\nThe range of the projectile is same for the two projectiles.\n\nTherefore, R 1 = R 2\n\nNow, as we know the expression of height of the projectile,\n\n$${H_{\\max }} = {{{u^2}\\sin \\theta } \\over {2g}}$$\n\nAt 42$$^\\circ$$, $${H_{\\max }} = {H_1} = {{{u^2}\\sin 42^\\circ } \\over {2g}} = {{0.669{u^2}} \\over {2g}}$$\n\nAt 48$$^\\circ$$, $${H_{\\max }} = {H_2} = {{{u^2}\\sin 48^\\circ } \\over {2g}} = {{0.743{u^2}} \\over {2g}}$$\n\nHigher the value of $$\\theta$$ higher the value of maximum height. Therefore, H 1 2 .",
