      "a": 0,
      "s": "JEE Main 2026 (Online) 5th April Morning Shift. Correct option: A. The masses $\\mathrm{m}_1$ and $\\mathrm{m}_2$ are on one side of the pulley, and $\\mathrm{m}_3$ is on the other.\n\nTotal mass on right side is $\\mathrm{M}_{\\mathrm{R}}=\\mathrm{m}_2+\\mathrm{m}_3=4+6=10 \\mathrm{~kg}$.\n\nTotal mass on right side is $\\mathrm{M}_{\\mathrm{L}}=\\mathrm{m}_1=4 \\mathrm{~kg}$.\n\n[Diagram: JEE Main 2026 (Online) 5th April Morning Shift Physics - Laws of Motion Question 2 English Explanation 1]\n\nSince $M_L < M_R$, the system will accelerate toward the right side. Let the acceleration be $a$.\n\nFor right side, $\\mathrm{m}_{\\mathrm{R}} \\mathrm{g}-\\mathrm{T}_1=\\mathrm{m}_{\\mathrm{R}} \\mathrm{a} \\Rightarrow 10 \\mathrm{~g}-\\mathrm{T}_1=10 \\mathrm{a}$\n\nFor left side, $\\mathrm{T}_1-\\mathrm{m}_{\\mathrm{L}} \\mathrm{g}=\\mathrm{m}_{\\mathrm{L}} \\mathrm{a} \\Rightarrow \\mathrm{T}_1-4 \\mathrm{~g}=4 \\mathrm{a} \\ldots$\n\nFrom both the equations,\n\n$$ \\mathrm{T}_1-4 \\mathrm{~g}=4\\left(\\frac{10 \\mathrm{~g}-\\mathrm{T}_1}{10}\\right) \\Rightarrow \\frac{10}{4}\\left(\\mathrm{~T}_1-40\\right)=100-\\mathrm{T}_1 $$\n\n$$\\Rightarrow $$ $\\frac{5 \\mathrm{~T}_1}{2}-100=100-\\mathrm{T}_1 \\Rightarrow \\frac{5 \\mathrm{~T}_1}{2}+\\mathrm{T}_1=200$\n\n$$\\Rightarrow \\frac{7 \\mathrm{~T}_1}{2}=200 \\Rightarrow \\mathrm{~T}_1=\\frac{400}{7} \\mathrm{~N} \\ldots (ii)$$\n\nPutting in equation (ii), we get the acceleration of the system;\n\n$$ \\mathrm{a}=\\frac{\\mathrm{T}_1-4 \\mathrm{~g}}{4}=\\frac{\\frac{400}{7}-40}{4}=\\frac{120}{7 \\times 4}=\\frac{30}{7} \\mathrm{~m} / \\mathrm{s}^2 \\ldots(iv) $$\n\nThe acceleration of whole system is $30 / 7 \\mathrm{~m} / \\mathrm{s}^2$,\n\nFor mass $\\mathrm{m}_3$;\n\n[Diagram: JEE Main 2026 (Online) 5th April Morning Shift Physics - Laws of Motion Question 2 English Explanation 2]\n\n$\\mathrm{m}_3 \\mathrm{~g}-\\mathrm{T}_2=\\mathrm{m}_3 \\mathrm{a} \\Rightarrow \\mathrm{T}_2=\\mathrm{m}_3(\\mathrm{~g}-\\mathrm{a})$\n\n$$ \\mathrm{T}_2=6\\left(10-\\frac{30}{7}\\right) \\mathrm{N}=6 \\times \\frac{40}{7}=\\frac{240}{7} \\ldots(\\mathrm{v}) $$\n\nSo, the ratio is $\\frac{\\mathrm{T}_1}{\\mathrm{~T}_2}$ is;\n\n$$ \\frac{\\mathrm{T}_1}{\\mathrm{~T}_2}=\\frac{400 / 7}{240 / 7}=\\frac{400}{240}=\\frac{5}{3} $$\n\nTherefore, the correct option is (A).",
      "source": "JEE Main 2026 (Online) 5th April Morning Shift | Laws of Motion | mnswhvew",
      "pyq": true,
      "exactPaperText": true,
