      "q": "A block is sliding down on an inclined plane of slope $\\theta$ and at an instant $t=0$ this block is given an upward momentum so that it starts moving up on the inclined surface with velocity $u$. The distance $(S)$ travelled by the block before its velocity become zero, is $\\_\\_\\_\\_$ .\n\n(g = gravitational acceleration)",
      "qHtml": "<p>A block is sliding down on an inclined plane of slope $\\theta$ and at an instant $t=0$ this block is given an upward momentum so that it starts moving up on the inclined surface with velocity $u$. The distance $(S)$ travelled by the block before its velocity become zero, is $\\_\\_\\_\\_$ .</p>\n<p>(g = gravitational acceleration)</p>",
