      "a": 2,
      "s": "JEE Main 2026 (Online) 6th April Evening Shift. Correct option: C. Work done (W) is defined as the integral of force (F) over a displacement (dx):\n\n$$ \\mathrm{W}=\\int_{\\mathrm{x}_{\\mathrm{i}}}^{\\mathrm{x}_{\\mathrm{f}}} \\mathrm{Fdx} $$\n\nFrom Newton's Second Law, $\\mathrm{F}=\\mathrm{ma}$, and acceleration $\\mathrm{a}=\\frac{\\mathrm{dv}}{\\mathrm{dt}}$.\n\nUsing the chain rule, $\\mathrm{a}=\\frac{\\mathrm{dv}}{\\mathrm{dx}} \\cdot \\frac{\\mathrm{dx}}{\\mathrm{dt}}=\\mathrm{v} \\frac{\\mathrm{dv}}{\\mathrm{dx}}$.\n\n$$ W=\\int_{x_i}^{x_f}\\left[m\\left(v \\frac{d v}{d x}\\right)\\right] d x $$\n\n$$\\Rightarrow $$ $W=\\int_{v_i}^{v_f} m v d v=m \\int_{v_i}^{v_f} v d v=m\\left[\\frac{v^2}{2}\\right]_{v_i}^{v_f}$\n\n$$\\Rightarrow $$ $\\mathrm{W}=\\frac{1}{2} \\mathrm{~m} \\mathrm{v}_{\\mathrm{f}}^2-\\frac{1}{2} \\mathrm{~m} \\mathrm{v}_{\\mathrm{i}}^2$\n\n$$\\Rightarrow $$ $$ \\mathrm{W}=\\Delta \\mathrm{K} . \\mathrm{E} . $$\n\nThe mass of the body is $\\mathrm{m}=1 \\mathrm{~kg}$\n\nThe velocity of body is given as function of position, $\\mathrm{v}=2 \\mathrm{x}^2$\n\nInitial position is $\\mathrm{x}_{\\mathrm{i}}=0 \\mathrm{~m}$\n\nFinal position is $\\mathrm{x}_{\\mathrm{f}}=5 \\mathrm{~m}$\n\nAt $\\mathrm{x}_{\\mathrm{i}}=0$ :\n\n$$ \\mathrm{v}_{\\mathrm{i}}=2(0)^2=0 \\mathrm{~m} / \\mathrm{s} $$\n\nAt $\\mathrm{x}_{\\mathrm{f}}=5$ :\n\n$$ v_f=2(5)^2=2(25)=50 \\mathrm{~m} / \\mathrm{s} $$\n\nOn substituting these values into the Work-Energy equation :\n\n$$ \\mathrm{W}=\\frac{1}{2} \\mathrm{~m}\\left(\\mathrm{v}_{\\mathrm{f}}^2-\\mathrm{v}_{\\mathrm{i}}^2\\right) $$\n\n$$\\Rightarrow $$ $\\mathrm{W}=\\frac{1}{2} \\times 1 \\times\\left(50^2-0^2\\right)$\n\n$$\\Rightarrow $$ $\\mathrm{W}=\\frac{1}{2} \\times(2500)$\n\n$$\\Rightarrow $$ $$ \\mathrm{W}=1250 \\mathrm{~J} $$\n\nTherefore, the work done by the body during displacement from $\\mathrm{x}=0$ to $\\mathrm{x}=5 \\mathrm{~m}$ is 1250 J .\n\nHence, the correct option is (C).",
