      "q": "The velocity at which 6 kg mass (shown in figure) strikes the ground when it is released from a height of 6 m above the ground is $\\_\\_\\_\\_$ $\\mathrm{m} / \\mathrm{s}$. Assume pulley is massless and string is light and inextensible. (Take $\\mathrm{g}=10 \\mathrm{~m} / \\mathrm{s}^2$ )\n\n[Diagram: JEE Main 2026 (Online) 6th April Evening Shift Physics - Work Power & Energy Question 5 English]",
      "qHtml": "<p>The velocity at which 6 kg mass (shown in figure) strikes the ground when it is released from a height of 6 m above the ground is $\\_\\_\\_\\_$ $\\mathrm{m} / \\mathrm{s}$. Assume pulley is massless and string is light and inextensible. (Take $\\mathrm{g}=10 \\mathrm{~m} / \\mathrm{s}^2$ )</p><img class=\"quiz-question-image\" src=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/image/6y3zli1mo4fpv2y/9e0021cb-81a5-42b5-9355-64909243bdc1/33773fa0-3b33-11f1-8c42-c7a7a182458c/file-6y3zli1mo4fpv2z.webp\" alt=\"JEE Main 2026 (Online) 6th April Evening Shift Physics - Work Power &amp; Energy Question 5 English\" loading=\"lazy\">",
