      "a": 0,
      "s": "JEE Main 2026 (Online) 6th April Evening Shift. Correct option: A. For the 6 kg mass $(\\mathrm{M})$ moving down and the 2 kg mass $(\\mathrm{m})$ moving up, let the acceleration of system is a and tension in the string is T .\n\n[Diagram: JEE Main 2026 (Online) 6th April Evening Shift Physics - Work Power & Energy Question 5 English Explanation]\n\nUsing Newton's second law ( $\\mathrm{F}=\\mathrm{ma}$ ) of motion for M\n\n$$\\mathrm{Mg}-\\mathrm{T}=\\mathrm{Ma} \\ldots (i) $$\n\nFor m ,\n\n$$ \\mathrm{T}-\\mathrm{mg}=\\mathrm{ma} \\ldots (ii)$$\n\nAdding the two equations :\n\n$$ (M-m) g=(M+m) a $$\n\n$$\\Rightarrow $$ $$ a=\\frac{(M-m)}{M+m} g $$\n\nSubstituting $\\mathrm{M}=6, \\mathrm{~m}=2$, and $\\mathrm{g}=10$ :\n\n$$ \\mathrm{a}=\\frac{6-2}{6+2} \\times 10=\\frac{4}{8} \\times 10=5 \\mathrm{~m} / \\mathrm{s}^2 $$\n\nUsing the kinematic equation for constant acceleration, starting from rest ( $u=0$ ) :\n\n$$ \\mathrm{v}^2=\\mathrm{u}^2+2 \\mathrm{as} $$\n\n$$\\Rightarrow $$ $$ \\mathrm{v}=\\sqrt{2 \\mathrm{as}} $$\n\nWhere s is the height $\\mathrm{h}=6 \\mathrm{~m}$.\n\n$$ v=\\sqrt{2 \\times 5 \\times 6} $$\n\n$$\\Rightarrow $$ $$ \\mathrm{v}=\\sqrt{60} \\approx 7.745 \\mathrm{~m} / \\mathrm{s} $$\n\nTherefore, the velocity is approximately $7.74 \\mathrm{~m} / \\mathrm{s}$.\n\nThe correct option is (A).",
