      "a": 1,
      "s": "JEE Main 2026 (Online) 2nd April Evening Shift. Correct option: B. Using the work-energy theorem, the work done by all forces acting on a body is equal to the change in its kinetic energy.\n\nThe ball falls from height $\\mathrm{h}=10 \\mathrm{~m}$ under gravity. And the ball enters the sand and travels a distance $\\mathrm{d}= 10 \\mathrm{~cm}=0.1 \\mathrm{~m}$ before coming to rest.\n\nLet m be the mass of the ball, h be the initial height, d be the penetration depth, and $\\mathrm{F}_{\\text {avg }}$ be the average resistive force exerted by the sand.\n\nThe total work done on the ball from the moment it is dropped until it stops is:\n\n$$ \\mathrm{W}_{\\text {total }}=\\mathrm{W}_{\\text {gravity }}+\\mathrm{W}_{\\text {sand }} $$\n\nSince the ball starts from rest at height $h$ and ends at rest after depth $d$, the total change in kinetic energy is zero $(\\Delta \\mathrm{K}=0)$.\n\n$$ \\mathrm{W}_{\\text {gravity }}+\\mathrm{W}_{\\text {sand }}=0 $$\n\nGravity acts over the entire vertical displacement ( $\\mathrm{h}+\\mathrm{d}$ ).\n\nSo, the work done by gravitational force is $\\mathrm{W}_{\\text {gravity }}=\\mathrm{mg}(\\mathrm{h}+\\mathrm{d})$\n\nThe resistive force $F_{\\text {avg }}$ acts upwards, opposite to the displacement $d$.\n\nSo, the work done by the sand is $\\mathrm{W}_{\\text {sand }}=-\\mathrm{F}_{\\text {avg }} \\cdot \\mathrm{d}$\n\nSubstituting these into the energy equation :\n\n$$ \\mathrm{mg}(\\mathrm{~h}+\\mathrm{d})-\\mathrm{F}_{\\mathrm{avg}} \\cdot \\mathrm{~d}=0 $$\n\n$$\\Rightarrow $$ $$ \\mathrm{F}_{\\mathrm{avg}}=\\frac{\\mathrm{mg}(\\mathrm{~h}+\\mathrm{d})}{\\mathrm{d}} $$\n\nThe mass of ball is $\\mathrm{m}=2 \\mathrm{~kg}$, the height of fall is $\\mathrm{h}=10 \\mathrm{~m}$, the distance of penetration in sand is $\\mathrm{d}=$ 0.1 m , and $\\mathrm{g}=10 \\mathrm{~m} / \\mathrm{s}^2$.\n\n$$ \\mathrm{F}_{\\mathrm{avg}}=\\frac{2 \\times 10 \\times(10+0.1)}{0.1} $$\n\n$$\\Rightarrow $$ $F_{a v g}=\\frac{20 \\times 10.1}{0.1}=20 \\times 101$\n\n$$\\Rightarrow $$ $$ \\mathrm{F}_{\\mathrm{avg}}=2020 \\mathrm{~N} $$\n\nTherefore, the average force exerted by sand on the ball is 2020 N .\n\nHence, the correct option is (B).",
      "source": "JEE Main 2026 (Online) 2nd April Evening Shift | Work, Power and Energy | mnrqzrmy",
