      "q": "A disc of radius $\\mathrm{R}$ and mass $\\mathrm{M}$ is rolling horizontally without slipping with speed $v$. It then moves up an inclined smooth surface as shown in figure. The maximum height that the disc can go up the incline is :\n\n[Diagram: JEE Main 2024 (Online) 1st February Evening Shift Physics - Rotational Motion Question 72 English]",
      "qHtml": "A disc of radius $\\mathrm{R}$ and mass $\\mathrm{M}$ is rolling horizontally without slipping with speed $v$. It then moves up an inclined smooth surface as shown in figure. The maximum height that the disc can go up the incline is :\n<br><br>\n<img class=\"quiz-question-image\" src=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/image/6y3zli1lsaqrkz2/1f522e79-a6b8-416b-b280-7f7235f61446/2f77d0e0-c524-11ee-94a9-d124b3795c4c/file-6y3zli1lsaqrkz3.png\" alt=\"JEE Main 2024 (Online) 1st February Evening Shift Physics - Rotational Motion Question 72 English\" loading=\"lazy\">",
