      "q": "The figure shows two solid discs with radius R and r respectively. If mass per unit area is same for both, what is the ratio of MI of bigger disc around axis AB (Which is $$ \\bot $$ to the plane of the disc and passing through its centre) of MI of smaller disc around one of its diameters lying on its plane? Given 'M' is the mass of the larger disc. (MI stands for moment of inertia)\n\n[Diagram: JEE Main 2021 (Online) 27th July Morning Shift Physics - Rotational Motion Question 129 English]",
      "qHtml": "The figure shows two solid discs with radius R and r respectively. If mass per unit area is same for both, what is the ratio of MI of bigger disc around axis AB (Which is $$ \\bot $$ to the plane of the disc and passing through its centre) of MI of smaller disc around one of its diameters lying on its plane? Given 'M' is the mass of the larger disc. (MI stands for moment of inertia)<br><br><img class=\"quiz-question-image\" src=\"https://imagex.cdn.examgoal.net/1ks0l0jpq/dbe8de78-67bb-44b1-ae0f-549738960cc6/11de2ee0-f6d6-11eb-b326-31a7780220e7/file-1ks0l0jpr.jpg\" alt=\"JEE Main 2021 (Online) 27th July Morning Shift Physics - Rotational Motion Question 129 English\" loading=\"lazy\">",
