      "q": "Net gravitational force at the center of a square is found to be $F_1$ when four particles having mass $M, 2 M, 3 M$ and $4 M$ are placed at the four corners of the square as shown in figure and it is $F_2$ when the positions of $3 M$ and $4 M$ are interchanged. The ratio $\\frac{F_1}{F_2}$ is $\\frac{\\alpha}{\\sqrt{5}}$. The value of $\\alpha$ is $\\_\\_\\_\\_$ .\n\n[Diagram: JEE Main 2026 (Online) 22nd January Morning Shift Physics - Gravitation Question 9 English]",
      "qHtml": "<p>Net gravitational force at the center of a square is found to be $F_1$ when four particles having mass $M, 2 M, 3 M$ and $4 M$ are placed at the four corners of the square as shown in figure and it is $F_2$ when the positions of $3 M$ and $4 M$ are interchanged. The ratio $\\frac{F_1}{F_2}$ is $\\frac{\\alpha}{\\sqrt{5}}$. The value of $\\alpha$ is $\\_\\_\\_\\_$ .</p><img class=\"quiz-question-image\" src=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/image/6y3zli1ml8ufoso/099e923f-cfde-46ff-8b13-508b64948735/3deacc80-023b-11f1-88dd-c7214e4b90e3/file-6y3zli1ml8ufosp.png\" alt=\"JEE Main 2026 (Online) 22nd January Morning Shift Physics - Gravitation Question 9 English\" loading=\"lazy\">",
