      "qHtml": "<p>A small point of mass $m$ is placed at a distance $2 R$ from the centre ' $O$ ' of a big uniform solid sphere of mass M and radius R . The gravitational force on ' m ' due to M is $\\mathrm{F}_1$. A spherical part of radius $\\mathrm{R} / 3$ is removed from the big sphere as shown in the figure and the gravitational force on m due to remaining part of $M$ is found to be $F_2$. The value of ratio $F_1: F_2$ is</p>\n<p><img class=\"quiz-question-image\" src=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/image/jaoe38c1m6qn0ktd/d0274187-1795-4fe4-8561-6a8da09a47ad/16ce8d10-e30d-11ef-8ccb-014d3311b56e/file-jaoe38c1m6qn0kte.png\" alt=\"JEE Main 2025 (Online) 22nd January Morning Shift Physics - Gravitation Question 22 English\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>",
