      "qHtml": "A person whose mass is 100 kg travels from Earth to Mars in a spaceship. Neglect all  other objects in sky and take acceleration due to gravity on the surface of the Earth and Mars as 10 m/s<sup>2</sup> and 4 m/s<sup>2</sup> respectively. Identify from the below figures, the curve that fits best for the weight of the passenger as a function of time.<br><br><img class=\"quiz-question-image\" src=\"https://imagex.cdn.examgoal.net/1krq8dqyt/45b88581-042e-41d6-a214-160991b7ca40/d3d0df50-f124-11eb-a221-f3b1f28d3393/file-1krq8dqyu.jpg\" alt=\"JEE Main 2021 (Online) 20th July Morning Shift Physics - Gravitation Question 128 English\" loading=\"lazy\">",
