      "a": 1,
      "s": "JEE Main 2026 (Online) 4th April Morning Shift. Correct option: B. When a uniform pressure (or stress) is applied to the surface of a fluid, it undergoes a decrease in volume.\n\nThe bulk modulus ( $\\beta$ ) is defined as the ratio of the volumetric stress (change in pressure, $\\Delta \\mathrm{P}$ ) to the volumetric strain (fractional change in volume, $\\frac{\\Delta \\mathrm{V}}{\\mathrm{V}}$ ).\n\n$$ \\beta=\\frac{\\Delta P}{\\Delta V / V} $$\n\n$$\\Rightarrow $$ $$ \\frac{\\Delta \\mathrm{V}}{\\mathrm{~V}}=\\frac{\\Delta \\mathrm{P}}{\\beta} $$\n\nIncrease in pressure is $\\Delta \\mathrm{P}=6.3 \\times 10^7 \\mathrm{~N} / \\mathrm{m}^2$\n\nBulk Modulus of water is $\\beta=2.1 \\times 10^9 \\mathrm{~N} / \\mathrm{m}^2$\n\nSubstituting the given values,\n\n$$ \\frac{\\Delta V}{V}=\\frac{6.3 \\times 10^7}{2.1 \\times 10^9} $$\n\n$$\\Rightarrow $$ $$ \\frac{\\Delta \\mathrm{V}}{\\mathrm{~V}}=3 \\times 10^{-2} $$\n\nThe percentage decrease in volume is $\\left(\\frac{\\Delta \\mathrm{V}}{\\mathrm{V}}\\right) \\times 100$\n\n$$ \\Delta \\%=\\left(3 \\times 10^{-2}\\right) \\times 100=3 \\% $$\n\nTherefore, the percentage decrease in the volume is $3 \\%$.\n\nThus, the correct option is (B).",
      "source": "JEE Main 2026 (Online) 4th April Morning Shift | Mechanical Properties of Solids | mnswhxia",
      "pyq": true,
      "exactPaperText": true,
      "pyqSourceSlug": "properties-of-matter"
