      "q": "A liquid drop of diameter 2 mm breaks into 512 droplets. The change in surface energy is $\\alpha \\times 10^{-6}$ J. The value of $\\alpha$ is _______. (Take surface tension of liquid = 0.08 N/m)",
      "qHtml": "<p>A liquid drop of diameter 2 mm breaks into 512 droplets. The change in surface energy is $\\alpha \\times 10^{-6}$ J. The value of $\\alpha$ is _______. (Take surface tension of liquid = 0.08 N/m)</p>",
      "o": [
        "10",
        "7",
        "8",
        "11"
      ],
      "oHtml": [
        "<p>10</p>",
        "<p>7</p>",
        "<p>8</p>",
        "<p>11</p>"
      ],
      "a": 1,
      "s": "JEE Main 2026 (Online) 2nd April Morning Shift. Correct option: B. Let $R$ be the radius of the big drop and $r$ be the radius of each small droplet. Since volume is conserved during the process:\n\nVolume of big drop $= 512 \\times$ Volume of one small droplet\n\n$$\\frac{4}{3}\\pi R^3 = 512 \\times \\left(\\frac{4}{3}\\pi r^3\\right)$$\n\n$$R^3 = 512\\,r^3$$\n\n$$R = (512)^{1/3}\\,r = 8r$$\n\n$$r = \\frac{R}{8}$$\n\nThe diameter of bigger drop is $D = 2\\ \\mathrm{mm}$, so $R = 1\\ \\mathrm{mm} = 10^{-3}\\ \\mathrm{m}$.\n\nThus, $r = \\frac{10^{-3}}{8}\\ \\mathrm{m}$.\n\nSurface energy is defined as surface tension $(T) \\times (A)$.\n\nInitial Surface Energy $U_i = T \\times (4\\pi R^2)$\n\nFinal Surface Energy $U_f = 512 \\times T \\times (4\\pi r^2)$\n\n$$\\Delta U = U_f - U_i = 4\\pi T\\left(512\\,r^2 - R^2\\right)$$\n\nSubstituting $r = \\frac{R}{8}$:\n\n$$\\Delta U = 4\\pi T\\left(512\\left(\\frac{R}{8}\\right)^2 - R^2\\right) = 4\\pi T\\left(\\frac{512R^2}{64} - R^2\\right)$$\n\n$$\\Delta U = 4\\pi T(8R^2 - R^2) = 4\\pi T(7R^2)$$\n\n$$\\Delta U = 28\\pi T R^2$$\n\nThe surface tension of liquid is $T = 0.08\\ \\mathrm{N/m}$ and $R = 10^{-3}\\ \\mathrm{m}$:\n\nPutting the values,\n\n$$\\Delta U = 28 \\times \\frac{22}{7} \\times 0.08 \\times (10^{-3})^2$$\n\n$$\\Delta U = 7.04 \\times 10^{-6}\\ \\mathrm{J} = \\alpha \\times 10^{-6}\\ \\mathrm{J}$$\n\n$$\\alpha \\approx 7$$\n\nThe value of $\\alpha$ is $7$. Therefore, the correct option is (B).",
