      "a": 2,
      "s": "JEE Main 2026 (Online) 2nd April Evening Shift. Correct option: C. Work done in increasing the size of a soap bubble is stored as surface energy.\n\nA soap bubble has two free surfaces (the inner and the outer air-liquid interfaces). The work done W is given by :\n\n$$ \\mathrm{W}=\\mathrm{T} \\times(2 \\times \\Delta \\mathrm{A}) $$\n\nWhere T is surface tension and $\\Delta \\mathrm{A}$ is the change in area of one surface\n\n$$ \\Delta A=\\left(4 \\pi R_2^2-4 \\pi R_1^2\\right) $$\n\nPutting the expression in work done,\n\n$$ \\mathrm{W}=2 \\mathrm{~T} \\times 4 \\pi\\left(\\mathrm{R}_2^2-\\mathrm{R}_1^2\\right)=8 \\pi \\mathrm{~T}\\left(\\mathrm{R}_2^2-\\mathrm{R}_1^2\\right) $$\n\nThe surface tension of soap bubble is $\\mathrm{T}=0.03 \\mathrm{~N} / \\mathrm{m}$\n\nThe initial diameter is $\\mathrm{D}_1=2 \\mathrm{~cm} \\Rightarrow \\mathrm{R}_1=1 \\mathrm{~cm}=1 \\times 10^{-2} \\mathrm{~m}$\n\nThe final diameter is $\\mathrm{D}_2=6 \\mathrm{~cm} \\Rightarrow \\mathrm{R}_2=3 \\mathrm{~cm}=3 \\times 10^{-2} \\mathrm{~m}$\n\nSubstitute the values into the expression for work done :\n\n$$ \\mathrm{W}=8 \\pi(0.03)\\left[\\left(3 \\times 10^{-2}\\right)^2-\\left(1 \\times 10^{-2}\\right)^2\\right] $$\n\n$$\\Rightarrow $$ $\\mathrm{W}=0.24 \\pi\\left[9 \\times 10^{-4}-1 \\times 10^{-4}\\right]$\n\n$$\\Rightarrow $$ $\\mathrm{W}=0.24 \\pi\\left[8 \\times 10^{-4}\\right]$\n\n$$\\Rightarrow $$ $\\mathrm{W}=1.92 \\pi \\times 10^{-4} \\mathrm{~J}=\\alpha \\pi \\times 10^{-4} \\mathrm{~J}$\n\n$$ \\Rightarrow \\alpha=1.92 $$\n\nTherefore, the value of $\\alpha$ is 1.92 .\n\nHence, the correct option is (C).",
      "source": "JEE Main 2026 (Online) 2nd April Evening Shift | Mechanical Properties of Fluids | mnrqw3xm",
      "pyq": true,
      "exactPaperText": true,
      "pyqSourceSlug": "properties-of-matter"
