      "a": 1,
      "s": "JEE Main 2026 (Online) 5th April Morning Shift. Correct option: B. Internal energy ( $U$ ) of an ideal gas depends only on temperature. The change in internal energy for any process is given by:\n\n$$ \\Delta \\mathrm{U}=\\mathrm{nC}_{\\mathrm{v}} \\Delta \\mathrm{~T}=\\mathrm{nC}_{\\mathrm{v}}\\left(\\mathrm{~T}_{\\mathrm{f}}-\\mathrm{T}_{\\mathrm{i}}\\right) $$\n\nAccording to Mayer's relation, $\\mathrm{C}_{\\mathrm{p}}-\\mathrm{C}_{\\mathrm{v}}=\\mathrm{R}$.\n\n$$ \\frac{C_p}{C_v}-1=\\frac{R}{C_v} $$\n\nSince $\\gamma=\\frac{\\mathrm{C}_{\\mathrm{p}}}{\\mathrm{C}_{\\mathrm{v}}}$, then $\\gamma-1=\\frac{\\mathrm{R}}{\\mathrm{C}_{\\mathrm{v}}} \\Rightarrow \\mathrm{C}_{\\mathrm{v}}=\\frac{\\mathrm{R}}{\\gamma-1}$.\n\nSubstituting $\\mathrm{C}_{\\mathrm{v}}$ back into the $\\Delta \\mathrm{U}$ equation:\n\n$$ \\Delta \\mathrm{U}=\\frac{\\mathrm{nR}}{\\gamma-1}\\left(\\mathrm{~T}_{\\mathrm{f}}-\\mathrm{T}_{\\mathrm{i}}\\right) $$\n\nThus, Statement I is true.\n\nFrom the law of equipartition of energy, the molar specific heat at constant volume is $C_v=\\frac{f}{2} R$, where $f$ is the degree of freedom.\n\nUsing $C_p=C_v+R=\\frac{f}{2} R+R=R\\left(1+\\frac{f}{2}\\right)$.\n\nThe ratio $\\gamma=\\frac{\\mathrm{C}_{\\mathrm{p}}}{\\mathrm{C}_{\\mathrm{v}}}=\\frac{\\mathrm{R}\\left(1+\\frac{\\mathrm{f}}{2}\\right)}{(\\mathrm{f} / 2) \\mathrm{R}}=\\frac{1+\\mathrm{f} / 2}{\\mathrm{f} / 2}=\\frac{2}{\\mathrm{f}}+1$.\n\nSo, $\\gamma=1+2$ f.\n\nThus, Statement II is true.\n\nStatement II is the definition of $\\gamma$ in terms of degrees of freedom, but Statement I is based on Mayer's relation which is the definition of $\\mathrm{C}_{\\mathrm{v}}$, i.e., not directly from the degrees of freedom.\n\nTherefore, both A and R are true but R is the correct explanation of A .\n\nThus, the correct option is (B).",
      "source": "JEE Main 2026 (Online) 5th April Morning Shift | Thermal Properties of Matter | mnswhv3w",
