      "a": 1,
      "s": "JEE Main 2026 (Online) 4th April Morning Shift. Correct option: B. The ideal gas law is given by: $\\mathrm{PV}=\\mathrm{nRT} \\Rightarrow \\mathrm{n}=\\frac{\\mathrm{PVR}}{\\mathrm{T}}$\n\nWhere R is the universal gas constant.\n\nFor the first gas : $\\mathrm{n}_1=\\frac{\\mathrm{P}_1 \\mathrm{~V}_1 \\mathrm{R}}{\\mathrm{T}_1}$\n\nFor the second gas : $\\mathrm{n}_2=\\frac{\\mathrm{P}_2 \\mathrm{~V}_2 \\mathrm{R}}{\\mathrm{T}_2}$\n\nWhen the gases are mixed, the total number of moles $n$ is the sum of the individual moles :\n\n$$ \\mathrm{n}=\\mathrm{n}_1+\\mathrm{n}_2 $$\n\nUsing the ideal gas law for the final mixture (pressure P , volume V , and temperature T ) :\n\n$$ \\frac{P V R}{T}=\\frac{P_1 V_1 R}{T_1}+\\frac{P_2 V_2 R}{T_2} $$\n\n$\\begin{gathered}\\frac{P V}{T}=\\frac{P_1 V_1}{T_1}+\\frac{P_2 V_2}{T_2} \\\\ \\frac{P V}{T}=\\frac{P_1 V_1 T_2+P_2 V_2 T_1}{T_1 T_2} \\\\ \\frac{T}{P V}=\\frac{T_1 T_2}{P_1 V_1 T_2+P_2 V_2 T_1} \\\\ T=\\frac{T_1 T_2 P V}{P_1 V_1 T_2+P_2 V_2 T_1}\\end{gathered}$\n\nTherefore, the temperature of the mixture of two gases is $\\frac{\\mathrm{T}_1 \\mathrm{~T}_2 \\mathrm{PV}}{\\mathrm{P}_1 \\mathrm{~V}_1 \\mathrm{~T}_2+\\mathrm{P}_2 \\mathrm{~V}_2 \\mathrm{~T}_1}$.\n\nThus, the correct option is (B).",
