      "q": "A flask contains Hydrogen and Argon in the ratio $2: 1$ by mass. The temperature of the mixture is $30^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C}$. The ratio of average kinetic energy per molecule of the two gases ( $\\mathrm{K}$ argon/K hydrogen) is :\n\n(Given: Atomic Weight of $\\mathrm{Ar}=39.9$ )",
      "qHtml": "A flask contains Hydrogen and Argon in the ratio $2: 1$ by mass. The temperature of the mixture is $30^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C}$. The ratio of average kinetic energy per molecule of the two gases ( $\\mathrm{K}$ argon/K hydrogen) is :\n<br><br>\n(Given: Atomic Weight of $\\mathrm{Ar}=39.9$ )",
