      "q": "An air bubble of volume $2.9 \\mathrm{~cm}^3$ rises from the bottom of a swimming pool of 5 m deep. At the bottom of the pool water temperature is $17^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C}$. The volume of the bubble when it reaches the surface, where the water temperature is $27^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C}$, is $\\_\\_\\_\\_$ $\\mathrm{cm}^3$.\n\n( $\\mathrm{g}=10 \\mathrm{~m} / \\mathrm{s}^2$, density of water $=10^3 \\mathrm{~kg} / \\mathrm{m}^3$, and 1 atm pressure is $10^5 \\mathrm{~Pa}$ )",
      "qHtml": "<p>An air bubble of volume $2.9 \\mathrm{~cm}^3$ rises from the bottom of a swimming pool of 5 m deep. At the bottom of the pool water temperature is $17^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C}$. The volume of the bubble when it reaches the surface, where the water temperature is $27^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C}$, is $\\_\\_\\_\\_$ $\\mathrm{cm}^3$.</p>\n<p>( $\\mathrm{g}=10 \\mathrm{~m} / \\mathrm{s}^2$, density of water $=10^3 \\mathrm{~kg} / \\mathrm{m}^3$, and 1 atm pressure is $10^5 \\mathrm{~Pa}$ )</p>",
