      "q": "The amplitude and phase of a wave that is formed by the superposition of two harmonic travelling waves, $y_1(x, t) = 4 \\sin (kx - \\omega t)$ and $y_2(x, t) = 2 \\sin (kx - \\omega t + \\frac{2\\pi}{3})$, are:\n(Take the angular frequency of initial waves same as $\\omega$)",
      "qHtml": "<p>The amplitude and phase of a wave that is formed by the superposition of two harmonic travelling waves, $y_1(x, t) = 4 \\sin (kx - \\omega t)$ and $y_2(x, t) = 2 \\sin (kx - \\omega t + \\frac{2\\pi}{3})$, are:</p> <p>(Take the angular frequency of initial waves same as $\\omega$)</p>",
