      "a": 3,
      "s": "JEE Main 2025 (Online) 7th April Evening Shift. Correct option: D. The equation for a wave traveling on a string is given by $ y = \\sin(20\\pi x + 10\\pi t) $, where $ x $ is the distance and $ t $ is the time in SI units. To find the minimum distance between two points having the same oscillating speed, we use the concept that this distance is half the wavelength $\\left(\\frac{\\lambda}{2}\\right)$.\n\nTo find the wavelength $\\lambda$:\n\n$ \\lambda = \\frac{2\\pi}{k} $\n\nHere, the wave number $ k = 20\\pi $. Thus,\n\n$ \\lambda = \\frac{2\\pi}{20\\pi} = \\frac{1}{10} \\text{ m} = 10 \\text{ cm} $\n\nThus, the minimum distance between two points having the same speed is:\n\n$ \\text{Distance} = \\frac{\\lambda}{2} = \\frac{10 \\text{ cm}}{2} = 5 \\text{ cm} $",
