      "q": "[Diagram: JEE Main 2025 (Online) 24th January Evening Shift Physics - Electrostatics Question 48 English]\n\nIn the first configuration (1) as shown in the figure, four identical charges $\\left(q_0\\right)$ are kept at the corners A, B, C and D of square of side length ' $a$ '. In the second configuration (2), the same charges are shifted to mid points $G, E, H$ and $F$, of the square. If $K=\\frac{1}{4 \\pi \\epsilon_0}$, the difference between the potential energies of configuration (2) and (1) is given by :",
      "qHtml": "<p><img class=\"quiz-question-image\" src=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/image/jaoe38c1m6uudmq7/07ea2b21-14b2-4251-b91e-ba87a75554c8/044dedf0-e55d-11ef-918b-9f97f398b68b/file-jaoe38c1m6uudmq8.png\" alt=\"JEE Main 2025 (Online) 24th January Evening Shift Physics - Electrostatics Question 48 English\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>\n<p>In the first configuration (1) as shown in the figure, four identical charges $\\left(q_0\\right)$ are kept at the corners A, B, C and D of square of side length ' $a$ '. In the second configuration (2), the same charges are shifted to mid points $G, E, H$ and $F$, of the square. If $K=\\frac{1}{4 \\pi \\epsilon_0}$, the difference between the potential energies of configuration (2) and (1) is given by :</p>",
