      "s": "JEE Main 2026 (Online) 8th April Evening Shift. Correct option: B. Coulomb's Law states that the force between two point charges is proportional to the product of the charges and inversely proportional to the square of the distance between them.\n\nIn vector form, the force $\\vec{F}_{21}$ exerted on charge $q_2$ by charge $q_1$ is:\n\n$$ \\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{F}}_{21}=\\frac{1}{4 \\pi \\epsilon_0} \\frac{\\mathrm{q}_1 \\mathrm{q}_2}{|\\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{r}}|^2} \\hat{\\mathrm{r}} $$\n\nWhere,\n\n$\\vec{r}=\\vec{r}_2-\\vec{r}_1$ is the position vector from $q_1$ to $q_2, \\hat{r}=\\frac{\\vec{r}}{|\\vec{r}|}$ is the unit vector and $\\frac{1}{4 \\pi \\epsilon_0}=9 \\times 10^9$\n\nSubstituting the unit vector, we get:\n\n$$ \\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{F}}_{21}=\\frac{1}{4 \\pi \\epsilon_0} \\frac{\\mathrm{q}_1 \\mathrm{q}_2}{|\\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{r}}|^3} \\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{r}} $$\n\nLet $\\vec{r}_1$ be the position of $q_1$ and $\\vec{r}_2$ be the position of $q_2$ :\n\n$$ \\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{r}}_1=2 \\hat{\\imath}+3 \\hat{\\jmath}+3 \\hat{\\mathrm{k}} $$\n\n$$ \\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{r}}_2=1 \\hat{\\imath}+1 \\hat{\\jmath}+1 \\hat{\\mathrm{k}} $$\n\nThe vector from $\\mathrm{q}_1$ to $\\mathrm{q}_2$ is :\n\n$$ \\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{r}}=\\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{r}}_2-\\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{r}}_1=(1-2) \\hat{\\mathrm{i}}+(1-3) \\hat{\\mathrm{j}}+(1-3) \\hat{\\mathrm{k}} $$\n\n$$\\Rightarrow $$ $$ \\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{r}}=-\\hat{\\imath}-2 \\hat{\\jmath}-2 \\hat{\\mathrm{k}} $$\n\nSo, the magnitude of position vector is,\n\n$$ |\\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{r}}|=\\sqrt{(-1)^2+(-2)^2+(-2)^2} $$\n\n$$\\Rightarrow $$ $$ |\\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{r}}|=\\sqrt{1+4+4}=\\sqrt{9}=3 \\mathrm{~m} $$\n\nSubstituting the values into the vector formula :\n\n$\\vec{F}=\\left(9 \\times 10^9\\right) \\frac{\\left(3 \\times 10^{-6}\\right)\\left(-4 \\times 10^{-6}\\right)}{3^3}(-\\hat{\\imath}-2 \\hat{\\jmath}-2 \\hat{k})$\n\n$$\\Rightarrow $$ $\\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{F}}=\\frac{9 \\times 3 \\times(-4) \\times 10^{-3}}{27}(-\\hat{\\imath}-2 \\hat{\\jmath}-2 \\hat{k})$\n\n$$\\Rightarrow $$ $\\vec{F}=\\frac{-108 \\times 10^{-3}}{27}(-\\hat{\\imath}-2 \\hat{\\jmath}-2 \\hat{k})$\n\n$$\\Rightarrow $$ $\\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{F}}=-4 \\times 10^{-3}(-\\hat{\\imath}-2 \\hat{\\jmath}-2 \\hat{\\mathrm{k}})$\n\n$$\\Rightarrow $$ $$ \\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{F}}=(4 \\hat{\\imath}+8 \\hat{\\jmath}+8 \\hat{\\mathrm{k}}) \\times 10^{-3} \\mathrm{~N} $$\n\nTherefore, the force on charge $\\mathrm{q}_2$ is $(4 \\hat{\\imath}+8 \\hat{\\jmath}+8 \\hat{\\mathrm{k}}) \\times 10^{-3} \\mathrm{~N}$.\n\nHence, the correct option is (B).",
