      "a": 3,
      "s": "JEE Main 2026 (Online) 2nd April Morning Shift. Correct option: D. When two conducting spheres are connected by a wire, charge flows from one to the other until they reach the same electrical potential.\n\nAt equilibrium, the potential (V) of both spheres must be equal.\n\n$$V_1 = V_2$$\n\nThe potential at the surface of a conducting sphere of radius R and charge Q is given by:\n\n$$V = \\frac{1}{4\\pi \\epsilon_0}\\frac{Q}{R}$$\n\nTherefore, for the two spheres:\n\n$$V_1 = V_2 \\Rightarrow \\frac{1}{4\\pi \\epsilon_0}\\frac{Q_1}{R_1} = \\frac{1}{4\\pi \\epsilon_0}\\frac{Q_2}{R_2}$$\n\n$$\\frac{Q_1}{R_1} = \\frac{Q_2}{R_2} \\Rightarrow \\frac{Q_1}{Q_2} = \\frac{R_1}{R_2}$$\n\nThe electric field (E) at the surface of a conducting sphere is given by:\n\n$$E = \\frac{1}{4\\pi \\epsilon_0}\\frac{Q}{R^2}$$\n\nSo, the ratio $\\frac{E_{S1}}{E_{S2}}$:\n\n$$\\frac{E_{S1}}{E_{S2}} = \\frac{\\frac{1}{4\\pi \\epsilon_0}\\frac{Q_1}{R_1^2}}{\\frac{1}{4\\pi \\epsilon_0}\\frac{Q_2}{R_2^2}}$$\n\n$$\\frac{E_{S1}}{E_{S2}} = \\left(\\frac{Q_1}{Q_2}\\right) \\times \\left(\\frac{R_2}{R_1}\\right)^2$$\n\nSubstituting the equilibrium condition $\\frac{Q_1}{Q_2} = \\frac{R_1}{R_2}$ into the electric field ratio:\n\n$$\\frac{E_{S1}}{E_{S2}} = \\left(\\frac{R_1}{R_2}\\right) \\times \\left(\\frac{R_2}{R_1}\\right)^2 = \\frac{R_2}{R_1}$$\n\nThe radii are given as $R_1 = 8\\ \\text{cm}$ and $R_2 = 18\\ \\text{cm}$.\n\n$$\\frac{E_{S1}}{E_{S2}} = \\frac{18}{8}$$\n\n$$\\frac{E_{S1}}{E_{S2}} = \\frac{9}{4}$$\n\nTherefore, the value of the ratio is $9/4$. Thus, the correct option is (D).",
      "source": "JEE Main 2026 (Online) 2nd April Morning Shift | Capacitance | mnrk9kzr",
      "pyq": true,
      "exactPaperText": true,
