      "q": "Electric field in a region is given by $\\vec{E}=A x \\hat{i}+B y \\hat{j}$, where $A=10 \\mathrm{~V} / \\mathrm{m}^2$ and $B=5 \\mathrm{~V} / \\mathrm{m}^2$. If the electric potential at a point $(10,20)$ is 500 V , then the electric potential at origin is $\\_\\_\\_\\_$ V.",
      "qHtml": "<p>Electric field in a region is given by $\\vec{E}=A x \\hat{i}+B y \\hat{j}$, where $A=10 \\mathrm{~V} / \\mathrm{m}^2$ and $B=5 \\mathrm{~V} / \\mathrm{m}^2$. If the electric potential at a point $(10,20)$ is 500 V , then the electric potential at origin is $\\_\\_\\_\\_$ V.</p>",
