      "s": "JEE Main 2026 (Online) 5th April Morning Shift. Correct option: A. [Diagram: JEE Main 2026 (Online) 5th April Morning Shift Physics - Current Electricity Question 2 English Explanation]\n\nUsing Kirchhoff's current law, the net accumulation of current at a junction is zero.\n\nSo, at junction $\\mathrm{A}, \\mathrm{I}_1-\\mathrm{I}_3-\\mathrm{I}_{\\mathrm{AD}}=0 \\Rightarrow \\mathrm{I}_{\\mathrm{AD}}=\\mathrm{I}_1-\\mathrm{I}_3$\n\nAnd at junction $\\mathrm{D}, \\mathrm{I}_{\\mathrm{AD}}+\\mathrm{I}_2-\\mathrm{I}_{\\mathrm{DB}}=0 \\Rightarrow \\mathrm{I}_1-\\mathrm{I}_3+\\mathrm{I}_2-\\mathrm{I}_{\\mathrm{DB}}=0 \\Rightarrow \\mathrm{I}_{\\mathrm{DB}}=\\mathrm{I}_1-\\mathrm{I}_3+\\mathrm{I}_2$\n\nApplying Kirchhoff's voltage law in closed loop I,\n\n$$ -4\\left(\\mathrm{I}_1-\\mathrm{I}_3\\right)-2\\left(\\mathrm{I}_1+\\mathrm{I}_2-\\mathrm{I}_3\\right)-\\mathrm{I}_1+10=0 $$\n\n$$ -7 \\mathrm{I}_1-2 \\mathrm{I}_2+6 \\mathrm{I}_3=-10 \\ldots (i) $$\n\nIn loop (II)\n\n$$ I_1+10-4 I_3-2\\left(I_3-I_2\\right)=0 $$\n\n$$ 2 \\mathrm{I}_2-6 \\mathrm{I}_3-\\mathrm{I}_1=-10 \\ldots \\text { (ii) } $$\n\nIn loop III,\n\n$$ -5-2\\left(\\mathrm{I}_3-\\mathrm{I}_2\\right)+2\\left(\\mathrm{I}_1+\\mathrm{I}_2-\\mathrm{I}_3\\right)=0 $$\n\n$$ 2 \\mathrm{I}_1+4 \\mathrm{I}_2-4 \\mathrm{I}_3=5 .....(iii) $$\n\nFrom equation (iii),\n\n$$ I_1=\\frac{5-4 I_2+4 I_3}{2} \\ldots (iv) $$\n\nOn substituting equation (iv) in equation (ii);\n\n$$ 2 \\mathrm{I}_2-6 \\mathrm{I}_3-\\frac{5-4 \\mathrm{I}_2+4 \\mathrm{I}_3}{2}=-10 $$\n\n$\\Rightarrow 4 \\mathrm{I}_2-12 \\mathrm{I}_3-5+4 \\mathrm{I}_2-4 \\mathrm{I}_3=-20$\n\n$\\Rightarrow 8 \\mathrm{I}_2-16 \\mathrm{I}_3=-15$\n\n$\\Rightarrow \\mathrm{I}_2-2 \\mathrm{I}_3=-\\frac{15}{8}$\n\n$$ \\Rightarrow \\mathrm{I}_2=2 \\mathrm{I}_3-\\frac{15}{8} \\ldots(\\mathrm{v}) $$\n\nOn substituting equation (v) in equation (iv),\n\n$$ \\mathrm{I}_1=\\frac{5-4\\left(2 \\mathrm{I}_3-\\frac{15}{8}\\right)}{2}=\\frac{5-8 \\mathrm{I}_3+\\frac{15}{2}+4 \\mathrm{I}_3}{2}=\\frac{\\frac{25}{2}-4 \\mathrm{I}_3}{2}=\\frac{25}{4}-2 \\mathrm{I}_3 $$\n\n$$\\Rightarrow $$ $$ \\begin{equation*} I_1=\\frac{25}{4}-2 I_3 \\ldots (vi) \\end{equation*} $$\n\nSubstituting equation (v) and (vi) in equation (i);\n\n$$ -7\\left(\\frac{25}{4}-2 \\mathrm{I}_3\\right)-2\\left(2 \\mathrm{I}_3-\\frac{15}{8}\\right)+6 \\mathrm{I}_3=-10 $$\n\n$\\begin{gathered}-\\frac{175}{4}+14 \\mathrm{I}_3-4 \\mathrm{I}_3+\\frac{15}{4}+6 \\mathrm{I}_3=-10 \\\\ \\frac{-175+15}{4}+16 \\mathrm{I}_3=-10 \\\\ \\frac{-160}{4}+16 \\mathrm{I}_3=-10 \\\\ -40+16 \\mathrm{I}_3=-10 \\\\ 16 \\mathrm{I}_3=30 \\Rightarrow \\mathrm{I}_3=\\frac{30}{16} \\mathrm{~A} \\\\ \\Rightarrow \\mathrm{I}_3=1.875 \\mathrm{~A}\\end{gathered}$\n\nFrom equation (v)\n\n$$ I_2=2\\left(\\frac{15}{8}\\right)-\\frac{15}{8}=\\frac{15}{8}=1.875 \\mathrm{~A} $$\n\nFrom equation (vi),\n\n$$ I_1=\\frac{25}{4}-2\\left(\\frac{15}{8}\\right)=\\frac{25}{4}-\\frac{15}{4}=\\frac{10}{4} \\mathrm{~A}=2.5 \\mathrm{~A} $$\n\nTherefore, the values of currents in the circuit are; $\\mathrm{I}_1=2.5 \\mathrm{~A}, \\mathrm{I}_2=1.875 \\mathrm{~A}, \\mathrm{I}_3=1.875 \\mathrm{~A}$.\n\nThus, the correct option is (A).",
