      "a": 0,
      "s": "JEE Main 2026 (Online) 4th April Morning Shift. Correct option: A. A voltmeter is a galvanometer with a high resistance connected in series. To increase the range of an existing voltmeter, we must add more resistance in series.\n\nLet the full-scale deflection current of the voltmeter be $\\mathrm{I}_{\\mathrm{g}}$.\n\n[Diagram: JEE Main 2026 (Online) 4th April Morning Shift Physics - Current Electricity Question 1 English Explanation 1]\n\nInitially, the voltmeter has a resistance x and measures up to $\\mathrm{V}_1=20 \\mathrm{~V}$.\n\nAccording to Ohm's Law ( $\\mathrm{V}=\\mathrm{IR}$ ):\n\n$$ 20=I_g \\cdot x \\Rightarrow I_g=\\frac{20}{x} $$\n\nTo measure a new maximum voltage $\\mathrm{V}_2=30 \\mathrm{~V}$, we connect an additional resistance R in series with the voltmeter.\n\n[Diagram: JEE Main 2026 (Online) 4th April Morning Shift Physics - Current Electricity Question 1 English Explanation 2]\n\nThe total resistance becomes $(x+R)$. The current required for full-scale deflection remains $I_g$ :\n\n$$ V_2=I_g(x+R) $$\n\nSubstituting $\\mathrm{V}_2=30$ and $\\mathrm{I}_{\\mathrm{g}}=20 \\mathrm{x}$ into the equation :\n\n$$ 30=\\left(\\frac{20}{x}\\right)(x+R) $$\n\n$$\\Rightarrow $$ $3=\\frac{2}{x}(x+R)$\n\n$$\\Rightarrow $$ $3 x=2(x+R)$\n\n$$\\Rightarrow $$ $3 x=2 x+2 R$\n\n$$\\Rightarrow $$ $$ x=2 R \\Rightarrow R=\\frac{x}{2} \\Omega $$\n\nThus, to increase the range to 30 V , a resistor of value $\\frac{x}{2} \\Omega$ must be connected in series with the voltmeter.\n\nHence, the correct option is (A).",
