      "a": 1,
      "s": "JEE Main 2026 (Online) 2nd April Evening Shift. Correct option: B. The bulb is rated at power $\\mathrm{P}=100 \\mathrm{~W}$ and the voltage rating is $\\mathrm{V}_{\\text {rated }}=200 \\mathrm{~V}$.\n\nUsing the power formula $\\mathrm{P}=\\frac{\\mathrm{V}^2}{\\mathrm{R}}$, the resistance of the bulb is,\n\n$$ \\mathrm{R}_{\\mathrm{b}}=\\frac{\\mathrm{V}_{\\mathrm{rated}}^2}{\\mathrm{P}} $$\n\n$$\\Rightarrow $$ $\\mathrm{R}_{\\mathrm{b}}=\\frac{(200)^2}{100}=\\frac{40000}{100}=400 \\Omega$\n\n[Diagram: JEE Main 2026 (Online) 2nd April Evening Shift Physics - Current Electricity Question 8 English Explanation]\n\nThe bulb $(400 \\Omega)$ is connected in parallel with the $400 \\Omega$ resistor. The equivalent resistance $\\left(\\mathrm{R}_{\\mathrm{p}}\\right)$ of two equal resistances in parallel is :\n\n$$ \\frac{1}{R_p}=\\frac{1}{400}+\\frac{1}{400}=\\frac{2}{400} $$\n\n$$\\Rightarrow $$ $$ \\mathrm{R}_{\\mathrm{p}}=200 \\Omega $$\n\nThis parallel combination is in series with the $200 \\Omega$ resistor.\n\n$$ \\mathrm{R}_{\\text {total }}=200+\\mathrm{R}_{\\mathrm{p}}=200+200=400 \\Omega $$\n\nSo, the total current in the circuit is $\\mathrm{i}=\\frac{\\mathrm{V}}{\\mathrm{R}_{\\text {total }}}=\\frac{100}{400}=\\frac{1}{4} \\mathrm{~A}$\n\nAs the bulb is in parallel with $400 \\Omega$ resistance, so the voltage drop across the bulb is same as across the parallel combination;\n\n$$ \\mathrm{V}_{\\mathrm{bulb}}=\\mathrm{iR}_{\\mathrm{p}}=\\frac{1}{4} \\times 200 \\mathrm{~V}=50 \\mathrm{~V} $$\n\nTherefore, the potential drop across the bulb is 50 V.\n\nHence, the correct option is (B).",
