      "qHtml": "<p>A current carrying rectangular loop PQRS is made of uniform wire. The length $P R=Q S=5 \\mathrm{~cm}$ and $P Q=R S=100 \\mathrm{~cm}$. If ammeter current reading changes from I to $2 I$, the ratio of magnetic forces per unit length on the wire $P Q$ due to wire $R S$ in the two cases respectively $\\left(f_{P Q}^I: f_{P Q}^{2 t}\\right)$ is:</p>\n<p><img class=\"quiz-question-image\" src=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/image/1ldr01a95/70e69e9a-3a3e-4000-8588-e333b977e824/bb25e190-a51d-11ed-8305-97c1292784a6/file-1ldr01a96.png\" alt=\"JEE Main 2023 (Online) 30th January Evening Shift Physics - Magnetic Effect of Current Question 96 English\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>",
