      "a": 1,
      "s": "JEE Main 2026 (Online) 4th April Morning Shift. Correct option: B. The ability of an optical instrument to distinguish between two closely spaced objects is defined by its resolving power.\n\nAccording to the Rayleigh criterion, for a circular aperture of diameter R , the minimum angular separation ( $\\Delta \\theta$ ) that can be resolved is given by the formula :\n\n$$ \\Delta \\theta=\\frac{1.22 \\lambda}{R} $$\n\nWhere $\\Delta \\theta$ is the angular resolution in radians, $\\lambda$ is the wavelength of the incident light and $R$ is the diameter of the objective lens or mirror.\n\nWe are given the wavelength of light as $\\lambda=500 \\mathrm{~nm}=500 \\times 10^{-9} \\mathrm{~m}=5 \\times 10^{-7} \\mathrm{~m}$\n\nAnd angular resolution as $\\Delta \\theta=5 \\times 10^{-7} \\mathrm{rad}$\n\n$$ \\mathrm{R}=\\frac{1.22 \\lambda}{\\Delta \\theta} $$\n\nSubstituting the values :\n\n$$ \\mathrm{R}=\\frac{1.22 \\times\\left(5 \\times 10^{-7}\\right)}{5 \\times 10^{-7}} $$\n\n$$\\Rightarrow $$ $\\mathrm{R}=1.22$ meters\n\n$$\\Rightarrow $$ $$ \\mathrm{R}=1.22 \\times 100 \\mathrm{~cm}=122 \\mathrm{~cm} $$\n\nTherefore, the value of R is 122 cm .\n\nThus, the correct option is (B).",
      "source": "JEE Main 2026 (Online) 4th April Morning Shift | Electromagnetic Waves | mnswhscd",
      "pyq": true,
      "exactPaperText": true,
      "pyqSourceSlug": "wave-optics"
