      "a": 0,
      "s": "JEE Main 2026 (Online) 5th April Morning Shift. Correct option: A. According to the lens maker's formula, the focal length (f) of a symmetric biconvex lens with radius of curvature R and refractive index $\\mu$ is :\n\n[Diagram: JEE Main 2026 (Online) 5th April Morning Shift Physics - Geometrical Optics Question 7 English Explanation 1]\n\n$$ \\frac{1}{f}=(\\mu-1)\\left(\\frac{1}{R}-\\frac{1}{-R}\\right)=\\frac{2(\\mu-1)}{R} $$\n\nWhen the lens is cut vertically, the new lens is plano-convex with one flat surface ( $\\mathrm{R}_2=\\infty$ ). Its focal length $\\left(f^{\\prime}\\right)$ is :\n\n[Diagram: JEE Main 2026 (Online) 5th April Morning Shift Physics - Geometrical Optics Question 7 English Explanation 2]\n\n$$ \\frac{1}{\\mathrm{f}^{\\prime}}=(\\mu-1)\\left(\\frac{1}{\\mathrm{R}}-\\frac{1}{\\infty}\\right)=\\frac{\\mu-1}{\\mathrm{R}} $$\n\nComparing the two equations, $\\frac{1}{\\mathrm{f}^{\\prime}}=\\frac{1}{2 \\mathrm{f}} \\Rightarrow \\mathrm{f}^{\\prime}=2 \\mathrm{f}$, i.e., the focal length of the objective lens doubles.\n\nThe total magnification ( M ) for a compound microscope is given by:\n\n$$ M=m_o \\times m_e \\approx \\frac{L}{f_o} \\times \\frac{D}{f_e} $$\n\nWhere L is the tube length, $\\mathrm{f}_{\\mathrm{o}}$ is the focal length of the objective, and $\\mathrm{f}_{\\mathrm{e}}$ is the focal length of the eyepiece.\n\nIt is given that magnification $(M)$ and the eyepiece $\\left(f_e\\right)$ remain constant. To keep $M$ the same while $f_o$ becomes $2 \\mathrm{f}_{\\mathrm{o}}$ :\n\n$$ M=\\frac{L}{f_o}=\\frac{L^{\\prime}}{2 f_o} $$\n\n$$\\Rightarrow $$ $$ \\mathrm{L}^{\\prime}=2 \\mathrm{~L} $$\n\nTherefore, the tube length has to be increased two times to keep the magnification of compound microscope unchanged.\n\nHence, the correct option is (A).",
