      "a": 1,
      "s": "JEE Main 2026 (Online) 4th April Morning Shift. Correct option: B. Using mirror formula,\n\n$$ \\frac{1}{f}=\\frac{1}{v}+\\frac{1}{u} $$\n\nWhere, the focal length is f , object distance is u , and image distance is v .\n\nAccording to the sign convention for a concave mirror:\n\nFocal length $\\mathrm{f}=-10 \\mathrm{~cm}$\n\nDistances measured in the direction of incident light are positive; opposite is negative.\n\nThe end of the rod closer to the mirror is at a distance of 20 cm from the pole.\n\n[Diagram: JEE Main 2026 (Online) 4th April Morning Shift Physics - Geometrical Optics Question 3 English Explanation]\n\n$$ \\mathrm{u}_1=-20 \\mathrm{~cm} $$\n\nUsing mirror formula for point A,\n\n$$ \\frac{1}{-10}=\\frac{1}{v_1}+\\frac{1}{-20} $$\n\n$$\\Rightarrow $$ $\\frac{1}{v_1}=\\frac{1}{20}-\\frac{1}{10}=\\frac{1-2}{20}=-\\frac{1}{20}$\n\n$$\\Rightarrow $$ $$ \\mathrm{v}_1=-20 \\mathrm{~cm} $$\n\nSince $\\mathrm{u}=2 \\mathrm{f}=\\mathrm{R}$ (the center of curvature), the image is formed at the same location ( $\\mathrm{v}=-20 \\mathrm{~cm}$ ).\n\nThe rod has a length of 10 cm and extends away from the mirror. Therefore, the far end $(\\mathrm{B})$ is at :\n\n$$ \\mathrm{u}_2=-(20+10)=-30 \\mathrm{~cm} $$\n\nUsing mirror formula for point B ,\n\n$$ \\frac{1}{-10}=\\frac{1}{v_2}+\\frac{1}{-30} $$\n\n$$\\Rightarrow $$ $\\frac{1}{v_2}=\\frac{1}{30}-\\frac{1}{10}=\\frac{1-3}{30}=-\\frac{2}{30}=-\\frac{1}{15}$\n\n$$\\Rightarrow $$ $$ \\mathrm{v}_2=-15 \\mathrm{~cm} $$\n\nThe length of the image is the magnitude of the difference between the two image positions:\n\nLength $=\\left|\\mathrm{v}_1-\\mathrm{v}_2\\right|$\n\nLength $=|-20-(-15)|=|-5|=5 \\mathrm{~cm}$\n\nTherefore, the length of image of the rod is 5 cm .\n\nThus, the correct option is (B).",
      "source": "JEE Main 2026 (Online) 4th April Morning Shift | Ray Optics | mnswhv8j",
      "pyq": true,
      "exactPaperText": true,
      "pyqSourceSlug": "geometrical-optics"
