      "a": 1,
      "s": "JEE Main 2026 (Online) 2nd April Morning Shift. Correct option: B. For a thin prism with a small prism angle (A), the angle of minimum deviation is given by,\n\n$$\\delta_m = (\\mu - 1)A$$\n\nWhere $\\mu$ is the refractive index of the glass, $\\mu = 1.5$:\n\nPutting the value of refractive index, $$\\delta_m = (1.5 - 1)A = 0.5A = \\frac{A}{2}$$\n\nAt the position of minimum deviation, the angle of incidence (i) is related to the prism angle (A) and the minimum deviation ($\\delta_m$) by\n\n$$i = \\frac{A + \\delta_m}{2}$$\n\nSubstituting the value of $$\\delta_m = \\frac{A}{2}$$\n\n$$i = \\frac{A + \\frac{A}{2}}{2} = \\frac{3A/2}{2} = \\frac{3A}{4}$$\n\nSo, the ratio of the incident angle (i) to the minimum deviation ($\\delta_m$) is,\n\n$$\\frac{i}{\\delta_m} = \\frac{3A/4}{A/2} = \\frac{6}{4} = \\frac{3}{2}$$\n\nTherefore, the ratio of the incident angle and minimum deviation is 3 : 2. Thus, the correct option is (B).",
