      "qHtml": "<p>A hemispherical vessel is completely filled with a liquid of refractive index $\\mu$. A small coin is kept at the lowest point $(\\mathrm{O})$ of the vessel as shown in figure. The minimum value of the refractive index of the liquid so that a person can see the coin from point E (at the level of the vessel) is _________.</p>\n<p><img class=\"quiz-question-image\" src=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/image/jaoe38c1m6w0v15p/c55fb6b0-5807-4864-96cf-798542192054/27a1a4d0-e603-11ef-80a5-67ab586ae463/file-jaoe38c1m6w0v15q.png\" alt=\"JEE Main 2025 (Online) 28th January Morning Shift Physics - Geometrical Optics Question 55 English\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>",
