      "q": "In a Young double slit experiment, the wavelength of incident light is $6000 \\mathop {\\rm{A}}\\limits^{\\rm{o}}$, the separation between slits $S_1$ and $S_2$ is 5 cm and the distance between slits plane and screen is 50 cm , as shown in the figure below. If the resultant intensity at $P$ is equal to the intensity due to individual slits, the path difference between interfering waves is $\\_\\_\\_\\_$ Å.\n\n[Diagram: JEE Main 2026 (Online) 6th April Evening Shift Physics - Wave Optics Question 10 English]",
      "qHtml": "<p>In a Young double slit experiment, the wavelength of incident light is $6000 \\mathop {\\rm{A}}\\limits^{\\rm{o}}$, the separation between slits $S_1$ and $S_2$ is 5 cm and the distance between slits plane and screen is 50 cm , as shown in the figure below. If the resultant intensity at $P$ is equal to the intensity due to individual slits, the path difference between interfering waves is $\\_\\_\\_\\_$ Å.</p><img class=\"quiz-question-image\" src=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/image/6y3zli1mnt2zskx/683291c4-7f8c-4caf-ad11-a04f8623fb0a/d1cd8e10-34f4-11f1-a0ba-554d230e3732/file-6y3zli1mnt2zsky.png\" alt=\"JEE Main 2026 (Online) 6th April Evening Shift Physics - Wave Optics Question 10 English\" loading=\"lazy\">",
