      "a": 0,
      "s": "JEE Main 2026 (Online) 5th April Evening Shift. Correct option: A. For two thin lenses in contact, the total power P is the sum of their individual powers :\n\n$$ \\mathrm{P}=\\mathrm{P}_1+\\mathrm{P}_2 $$\n\n[Diagram: JEE Main 2026 (Online) 5th April Evening Shift Physics - Geometrical Optics Question 6 English Explanation]\n\nThe power of lens is given as $P=\\frac{1}{f}$, where $f$ is the focal length of lens in meters.\n\n$$ \\frac{1}{F}=\\frac{1}{f_1}+\\frac{1}{f_2} $$\n\nFor a convex lens, the focal length is positive $\\Rightarrow \\mathrm{f}_1=+\\left|\\mathrm{f}_{\\text {convex }}\\right|$.\n\nFor a concave lens, the focal length is negative $\\Rightarrow f_2=-\\left|f_{\\text {concave }}\\right|$.\n\nSubstituting these into the formula of equivalent power:\n\n$$ \\frac{1}{F}=\\frac{1}{\\left|f_{\\text {convex }}\\right|}-\\frac{1}{\\left|f_{\\text {concave }}\\right|} $$\n\n$$\\Rightarrow $$ $$ \\frac{1}{F}=\\frac{\\left|f_{\\text {concave }}\\right|-\\left|f_{\\text {convex }}\\right|}{\\left|f_{\\text {convex }}\\right| \\cdot\\left|f_{\\text {concave }}\\right|} $$\n\nThe combination behaves as a concave lens if the equivalent focal length F is negative ( $\\mathrm{F}<0$ ).\n\nAs denominator of the expression is always positive in this case, so for the focal length (F) to be true, the numerator must be negative.\n\n$$ \\begin{gathered} \\left|\\mathrm{f}_{\\text {concave }}\\right|-\\left|\\mathrm{f}_{\\text {convex }}\\right|<0 \\\\ \\left|\\mathrm{f}_{\\text {convex }}\\right|>\\left|\\mathrm{f}_{\\text {concave }}\\right| \\end{gathered} $$\n\nConversely, it behaves as a convex lens if F is positive, which happens when\n\n$$ \\left|\\mathrm{f}_{\\text {concave }}\\right|>\\left|\\mathrm{f}_{\\text {convex }}\\right| . $$\n\nFor thin lenses in contact, the formula $\\frac{1}{\\mathrm{~F}}=\\frac{1}{\\mathrm{f}_1}+\\frac{1}{\\mathrm{f}_2}$ is independent of the order of the lenses. Therefore, interchanging them does not change the focal length.\n\nTherefore, the system behaves as a concave lens if $\\left|\\mathrm{f}_{\\text {convex }}\\right|>\\left|\\mathrm{f}_{\\text {concave }}\\right|$.\n\nThus, the correct option is (A).",
      "source": "JEE Main 2026 (Online) 5th April Evening Shift | Wave Optics | mnswhsk1",
