      "a": 1,
      "s": "JEE Main 2026 (Online) 5th April Morning Shift. Correct option: B. The refractive index is the ratio of the speed of light in a vacuum (c) to the speed of light in the medium (v).\n\n$$ \\mu=\\frac{c}{v} $$\n\nThe speed of light in vacuum is $\\mathrm{c}=3 \\times 10^8 \\mathrm{~m} / \\mathrm{s}$ and the speed of light in material of prism is given as $\\mathrm{v}= 2.12 \\times 10^8 \\mathrm{~m} / \\mathrm{s}$.\n\nSo, the refractive index of material of prism is;\n\n$$ \\mu=\\frac{3 \\times 10^8}{2.12 \\times 10^8} \\approx 1.414 \\approx \\sqrt{2} $$\n\nAs the prism is equilateral, so the angle of prism is $\\mathrm{A}=60^{\\circ}$.\n\nThe the angle of minimum deviation through prism is given as,\n\n$$ \\mu=\\frac{\\sin \\left(\\frac{A+\\delta_m}{2}\\right)}{\\sin \\left(\\frac{A}{2}\\right)} $$\n\nSubstituting the refractive index $\\mu=\\sqrt{2}$ and prism angle $\\mathrm{A}=60^{\\circ}$ :\n\n$$ \\sqrt{2}=\\frac{\\sin \\left(\\frac{60+\\delta_{\\mathrm{m}}}{2}\\right)}{\\sin \\left(\\frac{60}{2}\\right)} $$\n\n$$\\Rightarrow $$ $\\sqrt{2}=\\frac{\\sin \\left(\\frac{60+\\delta_m}{2}\\right)}{\\sin \\left(30^{\\circ}\\right)}$\n\n$$\\Rightarrow $$ $\\sqrt{2} \\times 0.5=\\sin \\left(\\frac{60+\\delta_m}{2}\\right)$\n\n$$\\Rightarrow $$ $\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}=\\sin \\left(\\frac{60+\\delta_m}{2}\\right) \\Rightarrow \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}=\\sin \\left(\\frac{60+\\delta_m}{2}\\right)=\\sin 45^{\\circ}$\n\n$$\\Rightarrow $$ $45^{\\circ}=\\frac{60+\\delta_{\\mathrm{m}}}{2}$\n\n$$\\Rightarrow $$ $$ 90^{\\circ}=60^{\\circ}+\\delta_{\\mathrm{m}} \\Rightarrow \\delta_{\\mathrm{m}}=30^{\\circ} $$\n\nTherefore, the correct option is (B).",
