      "a": 3,
      "s": "JEE Main 2026 (Online) 2nd April Evening Shift. Correct option: D. An equilateral prism has interior angles of $\\mathrm{A}=60^{\\circ}$.\n\nThe light ray enters the first face at a normal incidence (perpendicularly).\n\nAngle of incidence at the first face $\\mathrm{i}_1=0^{\\circ}$.\n\nBy Snell's Law $\\mathrm{n}_1 \\sin \\mathrm{i}_1=\\mathrm{n}_2 \\sin \\mathrm{r}_1$, the angle of refraction $\\mathrm{r}_1=0^{\\circ}$.\n\n[Diagram: JEE Main 2026 (Online) 2nd April Evening Shift Physics - Geometrical Optics Question 13 English Explanation]\n\nIn a prism, the relation between the apex angle $A$ and the internal angles is $A=r_1+r_2$.\n\n$$ 60^{\\circ}=0^{\\circ}+\\mathrm{i}_2 \\Rightarrow \\mathrm{i}_2=60^{\\circ} $$\n\nThe light ray strikes the painted face at an angle of $60^{\\circ}$ relative to the normal.\n\nFor TIR to occur at the interface between the prism ( $\\mathrm{n}_{\\text {prism }}=1.6$ ) and the paint ( $\\mathrm{n}_2$ ), the angle of incidence $\\mathrm{i}_2$ must be greater than or equal to the critical angle $\\theta_{\\mathrm{c}}$.\n\n$$ \\sin i_2 \\geq \\sin \\theta_c $$\n\nThe critical angle is defined by $\\sin \\theta_{\\mathrm{c}}=\\frac{\\mathrm{n}_{\\text {rarer }}}{\\mathrm{n}_{\\text {denser }}}=\\frac{\\mathrm{n}_2}{\\mathrm{n}_{\\text {prism }}}$\n\n$$ \\sin 60^{\\circ} \\geq \\frac{n_2}{1.6} $$\n\nSubstituting the value of $\\sin 60^{\\circ}=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}$ :\n\n$$ \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\geq \\frac{\\mathrm{n}_2}{1.6} $$\n\n$$\\Rightarrow $$ $\\mathrm{n}_2 \\leq \\frac{1.6 \\times \\sqrt{3}}{2}$\n\n$$\\Rightarrow $$ $\\mathrm{n}_2 \\leq 0.8 \\sqrt{3}$\n\n$$\\Rightarrow $$ $$ \\mathrm{n}_2 \\leq \\frac{4 \\sqrt{3}}{5} $$\n\nThe maximum value $\\mathrm{n}_2$ can take to ensure TIR is $\\frac{4 \\sqrt{3}}{5}$.\n\nHence, the correct option is (D).",
      "source": "JEE Main 2026 (Online) 2nd April Evening Shift | Wave Optics | mnrr7pl6",
      "pyq": true,
      "exactPaperText": true,
      "pyqSourceSlug": "geometrical-optics"
