      "a": 1,
      "s": "JEE Main 2026 (Online) 2nd April Morning Shift. Correct option: B. The energy of an incident photon is $E = \\frac{hc}{\\lambda}$, where $h$ is the Planck’s constant, $c$ is the speed of light in vacuum and $\\lambda$ is the wavelength of incident light.\n\nAccording to Einstein’s equation of photoelectric effect;\n\n$$\\frac{hc}{\\lambda} = \\phi + K_{\\max}$$\n\nWhere $\\phi$ is the work function is the minimum energy required to eject electron from the surface of metal, $\\left(\\phi = \\frac{hc}{\\lambda_0}\\right)$ and $K_{\\max} = eV_s$ ($V_s$ is the stopping potential).\n\nSo, $\\frac{hc}{\\lambda} = \\frac{hc}{\\lambda_0} + eV_s$\n\nCase 1: Wavelength is $\\lambda$, stopping potential is $3V_0$.\n\n$$\\frac{hc}{\\lambda} = \\frac{hc}{\\lambda_0} + e(3V_0) \\ldots (i)$$\n\nCase 2: Wavelength is $2\\lambda$, stopping potential is $V_0$.\n\n$$\\frac{hc}{2\\lambda} = \\frac{hc}{\\lambda_0} + eV_0$$\n\n$$\\Rightarrow 3\\left(\\frac{hc}{2\\lambda}\\right) = 3\\left(\\frac{hc}{\\lambda_0}\\right) + 3eV_0 \\ldots (ii)$$\n\nOn subtracting equation (i) from equation (ii):\n\n$$\\left(\\frac{3hc}{2\\lambda} - \\frac{hc}{\\lambda}\\right) = \\left(\\frac{3hc}{\\lambda_0} - \\frac{hc}{\\lambda_0}\\right) + (3eV_0 - 3eV_0)$$\n\n$$\\frac{hc}{2\\lambda} = \\frac{2hc}{\\lambda_0} \\rightarrow \\frac{1}{4\\lambda} = \\frac{1}{\\lambda_0} \\rightarrow \\lambda_0 = 4\\lambda$$\n\n$$\\Rightarrow \\alpha\\lambda = 4\\lambda \\Rightarrow \\alpha = 4$$\n\nTherefore, the value of $\\alpha$ is 4. Thus, the correct option is (B).",
      "source": "JEE Main 2026 (Online) 2nd April Morning Shift | Dual Nature of Matter | mnrkyc62",
