      "s": "JEE Main 2018 (Online) 15th April Morning Slot. Correct option: C. Energy required to remove e $$-$$ from singly ionized Helium atom\n\nE 1 = $${{13.6{z^2}} \\over {{n^2}}}$$ = $${{13.6 \\times {2^2}} \\over {{1^2}}}$$ = 54.4 eV.\n\nLet, E 2 = energy required to remove e $$-$$ from He $$-$$ atom\n\n$$\\therefore\\,\\,\\,\\,$$ According to q vertion.\n\nE 1 = 2.2 E 2\n\n$$\\therefore\\,\\,\\,\\,$$ E 2 = $${{54.4} \\over {2.2}}$$ = 24.72 eV\n\n$$\\therefore\\,\\,\\,\\,$$ Total energy required to ionize Helium atom completely\n\n= (54.4 + 24.72) eV\n\n= 79.12 eV",
