      "a": 1,
      "s": "JEE Main 2026 (Online) 2nd April Evening Shift. Correct option: B. The mass defect is the difference between the sum of the masses of the individual nucleons (protons and neutrons) and the actual mass of the nucleus.\n\nFor $\\text{Bi}_{83}^{209}$:\n\nNumber of protons (Z) $= 83$\n\nNumber of neutrons (N) $= A - Z = 209 - 83 = 126$\n\n$$\\Delta m = [Z \\ m_p + N \\ m_n] - M_{\\text{nucleus}}$$\n\n$$\\Delta m = [83 \\times 1.007825 + 126 \\times 1.008665] - 208.980388$$\n\n$$\\Delta m = [83.649475 + 127.09179] - 208.980388$$\n\n$$\\Delta m = 210.741265 - 208.980388 = 1.760877\\, \\text{u}$$\n\nUsing Einstein's mass-energy equivalence, the binding energy is:\n\n$$\\text{B.E.} = \\Delta m \\times 931 \\ \\text{MeV/u}$$\n\n$$\\text{B.E.} = 1.760877 \\times 931 \\approx 1639.376\\, \\text{MeV}$$\n\nThe binding energy per nucleon is the total binding energy divided by the mass number (A $= 209$).\n\n$$\\frac{\\text{B.E.}}{A} = \\frac{1639.376}{209} \\approx 7.8439 \\ \\text{MeV}$$\n\nTherefore, the binding energy per nucleon of $\\text{Bi}_{83}^{209}$ is $7.8439\\, \\text{MeV}$. Hence, the correct option is (B).",
