      "q": "Assuming in forward bias condition there is a voltage drop of 0.7 V across a silicon diode, the current through diode $D_1$ in the circuit is $\\_\\_\\_\\_$ mA .\n\n(Assume all diodes in the given circuit are identical)\n\n[Diagram: JEE Main 2026 (Online) 28th January Morning Shift Physics - Semiconductor Question 19 English]",
      "qHtml": "<p>Assuming in forward bias condition there is a voltage drop of 0.7 V across a silicon diode, the current through diode $D_1$ in the circuit is $\\_\\_\\_\\_$ mA .</p>\n<p>(Assume all diodes in the given circuit are identical)</p>\n\n<img class=\"quiz-question-image\" src=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/image/6y3zli1ml83cfof/f511ca24-624d-42ec-bf39-1113cb30c9a5/4cf58ef0-01d1-11f1-9078-a3f6a36b05f8/file-6y3zli1ml83cfog.png\" alt=\"JEE Main 2026 (Online) 28th January Morning Shift Physics - Semiconductor Question 19 English\" loading=\"lazy\">",
