      "q": "To measure the temperature coefficient of resistivity $\\alpha$ of a semiconductor, an electrical arrangement shown in the figure is prepared. The arm BC is made up of the semiconductor. The experiment is being conducted at $25^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C}$ and resistance of the semiconductor arm is $3 \\mathrm{~m} \\Omega$. Arm $\\mathrm{BC}$ is cooled at a constant rate of $2^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C} / \\mathrm{s}$. If the galvanometer $\\mathrm{G}$ shows no deflection after $10 \\mathrm{~s}$, then $\\alpha$ is :\n\n[Diagram: JEE Main 2024 (Online) 1st February Evening Shift Physics - Semiconductor Question 61 English]",
      "qHtml": "To measure the temperature coefficient of resistivity $\\alpha$ of a semiconductor, an electrical arrangement shown in the figure is prepared. The arm BC is made up of the semiconductor. The experiment is being conducted at $25^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C}$ and resistance of the semiconductor arm is $3 \\mathrm{~m} \\Omega$. Arm $\\mathrm{BC}$ is cooled at a constant rate of $2^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C} / \\mathrm{s}$. If the galvanometer $\\mathrm{G}$ shows no deflection after $10 \\mathrm{~s}$, then $\\alpha$ is :<br><br>\n<img class=\"quiz-question-image\" src=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/image/6y3zli1lsaqp7a4/862a4a97-dc65-47ce-8139-ed6a6955e295/ed45b5c0-c523-11ee-94a9-d124b3795c4c/file-6y3zli1lsaqp7a5.png\" alt=\"JEE Main 2024 (Online) 1st February Evening Shift Physics - Semiconductor Question 61 English\" loading=\"lazy\">",
