      "a": 3,
      "s": "JEE Main 2026 (Online) 5th April Morning Shift. Correct option: D. For a $10\\%$ by weight $(w/w)$ aqueous urea solution, let us take $100 \\, \\text{g}$ of solution.\n\nThen:\n\nMass of urea $= 10 \\, \\text{g}$\n\nMass of water $= 90 \\, \\text{g}$\n\nNow find the molar masses.\n\nUrea has formula $NH_2CONH_2$ or $CO(NH_2)_2$\n\n$$ M(\\text{urea}) = 12 + 16 + 2(14) + 4(1) = 60 \\, \\text{g mol}^{-1} $$\n\nMoles of urea:\n\n$$ n_{\\text{urea}} = \\frac{10}{60} = \\frac{1}{6} \\approx 0.167 $$\n\nMolar mass of water:\n\n$$ M(\\text{water}) = 2(1) + 16 = 18 \\, \\text{g mol}^{-1} $$\n\nMoles of water:\n\n$$ n_{\\text{water}} = \\frac{90}{18} = 5 $$\n\nNow, mole fraction of water is\n\n$$ X_{\\text{water}} = \\frac{n_{\\text{water}}}{n_{\\text{water}} + n_{\\text{urea}}} $$\n\n$$ X_{\\text{water}} = \\frac{5}{5 + \\frac{1}{6}} = \\frac{5}{\\frac{31}{6}} = \\frac{30}{31} $$\n\n$$ X_{\\text{water}} \\approx 0.967 $$\n\nSo, the correct answer is:\n\n$$ \\boxed{0.967} $$\n\nOption D",
