      "a": 3,
      "s": "JEE Main 2026 (Online) 4th April Evening Shift. Correct option: D. Let us find the total number of atoms in each case.\n\nWe only need to compare, so first calculate the number of moles of atoms in each sample.\n\n(A) 2 moles of cyclohexane\n\nCyclohexane has formula:\n\n$$ \\mathrm{C_6H_{12}} $$\n\nSo, one molecule of cyclohexane contains:\n\n$$ 6 + 12 = 18 \\text{ atoms} $$\n\nTherefore, in $2$ moles of cyclohexane, moles of atoms are:\n\n$$ 2 \\times 18 = 36 \\text{ moles of atoms} $$\n\n(B) 684 g of sucrose\n\nSucrose has formula:\n\n$$ \\mathrm{C_{12}H_{22}O_{11}} $$\n\nTotal atoms in one molecule:\n\n$$ 12 + 22 + 11 = 45 $$\n\nMolar mass of sucrose:\n\n$$ 12 \\times 12 + 22 \\times 1 + 11 \\times 16 $$\n\n$$ = 144 + 22 + 176 = 342 \\text{ g mol}^{-1} $$\n\nGiven mass $= 684$ g, so moles of sucrose:\n\n$$ \\frac{684}{342} = 2 \\text{ mol} $$\n\nHence, moles of atoms:\n\n$$ 2 \\times 45 = 90 \\text{ moles of atoms} $$\n\n(C) 90.8 L of dihydrogen at STP\n\nAt STP, $1$ mole of any gas occupies $22.4$ L.\n\nSo moles of $\\mathrm{H_2}$:\n\n$$ \\frac{90.8}{22.4} \\approx 4.05 \\text{ mol} $$\n\nEach molecule of $\\mathrm{H_2}$ has $2$ atoms.\n\nTherefore, moles of atoms:\n\n$$ 4.05 \\times 2 = 8.10 \\text{ moles of atoms} $$\n\nComparison\n\n(A) $= 36$ moles of atoms\n\n(B) $= 90$ moles of atoms\n\n(C) $= 8.10$ moles of atoms\n\nSo the correct order is:\n\n$$ \\mathrm{B} > \\mathrm{A} > \\mathrm{C} $$\n\nTherefore, the correct option is:\n\n$$ \\boxed{\\text{Option D}} $$",
