      "q": "For the given reaction;\nCaCO 3 + 2HCl -> CaCl 2 + H 2 O + CO 2\nIf 90 g CaCO 3 is added to 300 mL of HCl which contains 38.55% HCl by mass and has density 1.13 g mL -1 , then which of the following option is correct ?\nGiven molar mass of H, Cl, Ca and O are 1, 35.5, 40 and 16 g mol -1 respectively.",
      "qHtml": "<p>For the given reaction;</p><p>CaCO<sub>3</sub> + 2HCl &rarr; CaCl<sub>2</sub> + H<sub>2</sub>O + CO<sub>2</sub></p><p>If 90 g CaCO<sub>3</sub> is added to 300 mL of HCl which contains 38.55% HCl by mass and has density 1.13 g mL<sup>&minus;1</sup>, then which of the following option is <b>correct</b>?</p><p>Given molar mass of H, Cl, Ca and O are 1, 35.5, 40 and 16 g mol<sup>&minus;1</sup> respectively.</p>",
