      "q": "Given below are two statements:\n\nStatement I : According to Bohr's model of hydrogen atom, the angular momentum of an electron in a given stationary state is quantised.\n\nStatement II : The concept of electron in Bohr's orbit, violates the Heisenberg uncertainty principle.\n\nIn the light of the above statements, choose the most appropriate answer from the options given below:",
      "qHtml": "Given below are two statements:\n<br><br>\n<b>Statement I</b> : According to Bohr's model of hydrogen atom, the angular momentum of an electron in a given stationary state is quantised.\n<br><br>\n<b>Statement II</b> : The concept of electron in Bohr's orbit, violates the Heisenberg uncertainty principle.\n<br><br>\nIn the light of the above statements, choose the most appropriate answer from the options given below:",
