      "a": 3,
      "s": "JEE Main 2025 (Online) 24th January Evening Shift. Correct option: D. In group 14, the general trend is that ionization energy decreases down the group because atomic size increases.\n\nNow check each statement carefully.\n\nFor Statement (I):\n\nPb and Sn belong to the same group.\n\nUsually, ionization energy should decrease from Sn to Pb. But Pb shows slightly higher ionization energy than expected because of poor shielding by inner $d$ and $f$ electrons and relativistic effects. Due to this, the outer electrons of Pb are held more strongly.\n\nSo, the first ionization energy of Pb is slightly greater than that of Sn.\n\nStatement (I) is true.\n\nFor Statement (II):\n\nGe lies below Si in group 14. As atomic size increases from Si to Ge, the outer electron becomes easier to remove.\n\nHence, the first ionization energy of Ge is less than that of Si.\n\nSo, Statement (II) is false.\n\nTherefore, the correct option is:\n\n$$\\boxed{\\text{Option D}}$$\n\nStatement I is true but Statement II is false.",
      "source": "JEE Main 2025 (Online) 24th January Evening Shift | Periodic Classification | m6v42h50",
