      "q": "Bromine trifluoride autoionizes to form $\\mathrm{BrF}_2^{\\oplus}$ and $\\mathrm{BrF}_4^{\\ominus}$. The shapes of the cation and anion are respectively $\\_\\_\\_\\_$ and $\\_\\_\\_\\_$ .",
      "qHtml": "<p>Bromine trifluoride autoionizes to form $\\mathrm{BrF}_2^{\\oplus}$ and $\\mathrm{BrF}_4^{\\ominus}$. The shapes of the cation and anion are respectively $\\_\\_\\_\\_$ and $\\_\\_\\_\\_$ .</p>",
      "o": [
        "bent, square planar",
        "linear, square planar",
        "bent, see-saw",
        "linear, tetrahedral"
      ],
      "oHtml": [
        "<p>bent, square planar</p>",
        "<p>linear, square planar</p>",
        "<p>bent, see-saw</p>",
        "<p>linear, tetrahedral</p>"
      ],
      "a": 0,
      "s": "JEE Main 2026 (Online) 8th April Evening Shift. Correct option: A. First, let us recall the autoionization of bromine trifluoride:\n\n$ 2\\,\\mathrm{BrF_3} \\rightleftharpoons \\mathrm{BrF_2^+} + \\mathrm{BrF_4^-} $\n\nWe have to determine the shapes of the cation and the anion.\n\nCentral atom: Br\n\nValence electrons of Br = 7\n\nEach F contributes one bond → 2 Br–F bonds = 2 pairs of bonding electrons\n\nSo, total electrons around Br for shape determination:\n\n$ 7 - 2(\\text{by bonding}) - 1(\\text{positive charge}) = 4 $\n\nThese 4 electrons form 2 lone pairs on Br.\n\nHence, the total number of electron pairs around Br =\n\n2 (bonding) + 2 (lone pairs) = 4 electron domains.\n\nAccording to VSEPR theory:\n\n4 electron pairs → tetrahedral electron geometry\n\nWith 2 bonding and 2 lone pairs → bent shape\n\nThus, $\\mathrm{BrF_2^+}$ is bent .\n\nCentral atom: Br\n\nValence electrons of Br = 7\n\nEach F contributes one bond → 4 Br–F bonds = 4 pairs of bonding electrons\n\nAdditional one electron due to negative charge → +1\n\nHence total electrons on central bromine:\n\n$ 7 + 1 - 4 = 4 $\n\nwhich means 2 lone pairs on Br.\n\nThus, the total number of electron pairs =\n\n4 (bonding) + 2 (lone pairs) = 6 electron domains.\n\nAccording to VSEPR theory:\n\n6 electron domains → octahedral electron geometry\n\nWith 4 bonding and 2 lone pairs → square planar shape\n\nShapes are:\n\n$\\mathrm{BrF_2^+}$ → bent\n\n$\\mathrm{BrF_4^-}$ → square planar\n\nCorrect Option: A) bent, square planar",
