      "q": "The first and second ionization constants of a weak dibasic acid H 2 A are $8.1 \\times 10^{-8}$ and $1.0 \\times 10^{-13}$ respectively. 0.1 mol of H 2 A was dissolved in 1 L of 0.1 M HCl solution. The concentration of HA - in the resultant solution is:",
      "qHtml": "<p>The first and second ionization constants of a weak dibasic acid H<sub>2</sub>A are $8.1 \\times 10^{-8}$ and $1.0 \\times 10^{-13}$ respectively. 0.1 mol of H<sub>2</sub>A was dissolved in 1 L of 0.1 M HCl solution. The concentration of HA<sup>-</sup> in the resultant solution is:</p>",
