      "q": "At 25°C, 20.0 mL of 0.2 M weak monoprotic acid HX is titrated against 0.2 M NaOH. The pH of the solution (a) at the start of the titration (when NaOH has not been added) and (b) when 10 mL of NaOH is added respectively, are :\nGiven :\n$K_a = 5 \\times 10^{-4}$\n$\\mathrm{p}K_a = 3.3$\n$\\alpha \\ll 1$",
      "qHtml": "<p>At 25°C, 20.0 mL of 0.2 M weak monoprotic acid HX is titrated against 0.2 M NaOH. The pH of the solution (a) at the start of the titration (when NaOH has not been added) and (b) when 10 mL of NaOH is added respectively, are :</p><p>Given :<br>$K_a = 5 \\times 10^{-4}$<br>$\\mathrm{p}K_a = 3.3$<br>$\\alpha \\ll 1$</p>",
