      "s": "JEE Main 2025 (Online) 3rd April Evening Shift. Correct option: A. Hyperconjugation is considered a permanent effect because it does not rely on the presence of an external reagent to occur. Therefore, Statement I is false. However, Statement II is true; the presence of more alkyl groups results in more alpha hydrogen atoms ($\\alpha-\\mathrm{H}$), which enhances hyperconjugation. This increased hyperconjugation leads to greater stabilization of the carbocation.",
