      "s": "AIEEE 2011. Correct option: B. The formula between Mole fraction and Molality is\n$$$m = {{{X_{solute}}} \\over {{X_{solvent}}}} \\times {{1000} \\over {{M_{solvent}}}}$$$\n\n$$m$$ = molality, X solute = Mole fraction of solute, X solvent = Mole fraction of solvent, M solvent = Molar mass of solvent\n\nHere solute is methyl alcohol(CH 3 OH) and solvent is water(H 2 O). Here water is solvent because question says solution is aqueous.\n\nAssume mole fraction of methyl alcohol = X\n\nSo mole fraction of water = 1 - X\n\nand given molality (m) = 5.2\n\nM solvent = 18 (as molar mass of H 2 O = 18)\n\n$$\\therefore$$ 5.2 = $$ {X \\over {1 - X}} \\times {{1000} \\over {18}}$$\n\nby solving this we get,\n\nX = 0.086",
