      "s": "JEE Main 2018 (Offline). Correct option: A. [Diagram: JEE Main 2018 (Offline) Chemistry - Some Basic Concepts of Chemistry Question 226 English Explanation]\n\n$$\\therefore\\,\\,\\,$$ The ratio of no of atoms of C and H in one molecule of C x H y O z = 1 : 2\n\n$$\\therefore\\,\\,\\,$$ y = 2x\n\nIn one molecule of C x H y O z compound contain z atoms of oxygen.\n\nAccording to the question, no of atoms of oxygen required to burn C x H y completely should be twice of z atoms of oxygen.\n\nC x H y + (x + $${y \\over 4}$$) O 2 $$ \\to $$ HCO 2 + $${y \\over 2}$$ H 2 O\n\nNo. of O 2 molecules required = (x + $${y \\over 4}$$)\n\n$$\\therefore\\,\\,\\,$$ No. of O atoms required = 2 (x + $${y \\over 4}$$)\n\nAccording to question,\n\n$$2\\left( {x + {y \\over 4}} \\right) = 2z$$\n\n$$ \\Rightarrow \\,\\,\\,2\\left( {x + {{2x} \\over 4}} \\right) = 2z\\,\\,\\,$$ [ Putting y = 2x ]\n\n$$ \\Rightarrow \\,\\,\\,\\,{{3x} \\over 2} = z$$\n\n$$\\therefore\\,\\,\\,$$ x : y : z\n\n= x : 2x : $${{3x} \\over 2}$$\n\n= 2 : 4 : 3\n\n$$\\therefore\\,\\,\\,$$ Empirical formula = C 2 H 4 O 3",
