      "a": 2,
      "s": "JEE Main 2026 (Online) 4th April Evening Shift. Correct option: C. (A) A semi-permeable membrane (SPM) allows only solvent molecules (water) to pass through it. It does not allow ions to pass.\n\nSo, the solute ions from the two sides cannot come together. Therefore, no blue colour (due to mixing of ions) will appear on either side.\n\n(B) Because ions cannot cross the SPM, only solvent molecules can move from one side to the other depending on osmotic pressure.\n\n(C) A hypotonic solution is the one which has lower osmotic pressure (lower “effective” concentration of solute particles).\n\nWe use the NCERT relation for osmotic pressure:\n\nAs osmotic pressure $(\\pi)=i C R T$\n\n$$ \\begin{aligned} & \\mathrm{K}_4\\left[\\mathrm{Fe}(\\mathrm{CN})_6\\right] \\longrightarrow 4 \\mathrm{~K}^{+}+\\mathrm{Fe}(\\mathrm{CN})_6^{-4} \\quad(\\because i=5) \\\\ & \\mathrm{FeCl}_3 \\longrightarrow \\mathrm{Fe}^{+3}+\\mathrm{3Cl^-} \\quad(\\because i=4) \\\\ & \\text { for side } x: \\pi=5 \\mathrm{CRT}=0.5 \\mathrm{RT} \\quad(\\because c=0.1 \\mathrm{~m}) \\\\ &\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\, y: \\pi=0.4 R T \\quad(\\because c=0.1 \\mathrm{~m}) \\end{aligned} $$\n\neffective concentration of $x=\\dot{i} \\times C=0.5 \\mathrm{M}$\n\n$$ y=i \\times C=0.4 \\mathrm{~m} $$\n\nSince, effective concentration of $y$ is less than $x$. Hence, $y$ is hypotonic.\n\n(D) In reverse osmosis, pressure is applied on the side having higher osmotic pressure (here, side $x$). But this applied external pressure must be greater than the osmotic pressure difference between the two sides.\n\ni.e. P applied > $\\left(\\pi_x-\\pi_y\\right)$",
