      "a": 3,
      "s": "JEE Main 2026 (Online) 2nd April Morning Shift. Correct option: D. Given:\n\nMass of fluoroacetic acid $= 19.5 \\, \\text{g}$\n\nMolar mass $= 78 \\, \\text{g mol}^{-1}$\n\nMass of water $= 500 \\, \\text{g} = 0.5 \\, \\text{kg}$\n\nDepression in freezing point, $\\Delta T_f = 1^\\circ \\text{C} = 1 \\, \\text{K}$\n\n$K_f = 1.86 \\, \\text{K kg mol}^{-1}$\n\nWe have to find $K_a$ of fluoroacetic acid.\n\nFirst, calculate the number of moles of acid:\n\n$$ n = \\frac{19.5}{78} = 0.25 \\, \\text{mol} $$\n\nNow, molality of the solution:\n\n$$ m = \\frac{0.25}{0.5} = 0.5 \\, \\text{mol kg}^{-1} $$\n\nFor an electrolyte,\n\n$$ \\Delta T_f = i K_f m $$\n\nSo,\n\n$$ 1 = i \\times 1.86 \\times 0.5 $$\n\n$$ 1 = i \\times 0.93 $$\n\n$$ i = \\frac{1}{0.93} \\approx 1.075 $$\n\nFluoroacetic acid is a weak monoprotic acid:\n\n$$ \\text{HA} \\rightleftharpoons \\text{H}^+ + \\text{A}^- $$\n\nIf degree of dissociation is $\\alpha$, then for this type of acid:\n\n$$ i = 1 + \\alpha $$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$ \\alpha = i - 1 = 1.075 - 1 = 0.075 $$\n\nNow use Ostwald’s dilution law:\n\n$$ K_a = \\frac{C\\alpha^2}{1-\\alpha} $$\n\nGiven in the question, assume molarity and molality are same, so\n\n$$ C = 0.5 $$\n\nThus,\n\n$$ K_a = \\frac{0.5 \\times (0.075)^2}{1-0.075} $$\n\n$$ = \\frac{0.5 \\times 0.005625}{0.925} $$\n\n$$ = \\frac{0.0028125}{0.925} \\approx 3.04 \\times 10^{-3} $$\n\nSo,\n\n$$ K_a \\approx 3 \\times 10^{-3} $$\n\nHence, the correct option is:\n\n$$ \\boxed{3 \\times 10^{-3}} $$\n\nOption D.",
