      "a": 0,
      "s": "JEE Main 2026 (Online) 2nd April Evening Shift. Correct option: A. The given rate constant is $ k = 10^{-3} \\, \\text{M}^{-1} \\, \\text{s}^{-1} $.\n\nStep 1: Determining the order of reaction\n\nThe general unit of the rate constant is $ \\text{M}^{1-n} \\, \\text{s}^{-1} $, where $ n $ is the order of reaction.\n\nHere, the unit of $ k $ is $ \\text{M}^{-1} \\, \\text{s}^{-1} $.\n\nSo, $ 1 - n = -1 \\Rightarrow n = 2 $.\n\nHence, this is a second order reaction .\n\nStep 2: Expression for the rate\n\nThe rate law for a second order reaction is:\n\n$$ \\text{Rate} = k [A]^2 $$\n\nStep 3: Effect of changing concentration\n\nIf the concentration of $ A $ is made 4 times, that is, $ [A]' = 4[A] $, then\n\n$$ \\text{New rate} = k (4[A])^2 = 16k[A]^2 $$\n\nSo, the rate increases by 16 times.\n\nTherefore, statement (A) is correct.\n\nStep 4: Order of reaction\n\nAs we found $ n = 2 $, the reaction is second order.\n\nSo, statement (B) is correct.\n\nStep 5: Half-life relation\n\nFor a second order reaction, the half-life is inversely proportional to the initial concentration:\n\n$$ t_{1/2} = \\frac{1}{k[A]_0} $$\n\nHence, the half-life depends on concentration.\n\nSo, statement (C) is incorrect because it is true only for a first order reaction.\n\nStep 6: Example of reaction\n\nThe decomposition of $ \\mathrm{N_2O_5} $ is a first order reaction.\n\nThus, statement (D) is incorrect.\n\nStep 7: Graph type\n\nA straight-line graph of $ \\log \\frac{[R]_0}{[R]_t} $ versus $ t $ is valid only for first order reactions, not second order.\n\nTherefore, statement (E) is incorrect.\n\nFinal Answer: The correct statements are (A) and (B).",
      "source": "JEE Main 2026 (Online) 2nd April Evening Shift | Chemical Kinetics | mnrs7ldl",
      "pyq": true,
