      "q": "Correct statements regarding Arrhenius equation among the following are :\n\nA. Factor $e^{-\\mathrm{Ea} / \\mathrm{RT}}$ corresponds to fraction of molecules having kinetic energy less than Ea.\n\nB. At a given temperature, lower the Ea, faster is the reaction.\n\nC. Increase in temperature by about $10^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C}$ doubles the rate of reaction.\n\nD. Plot of $\\log \\mathrm{k}$ vs $\\frac{1}{\\mathrm{~T}}$ gives a straight line with slope $=-\\frac{\\mathrm{Ea}}{\\mathrm{R}}$.\n\nChoose the correct answer from the options given below :",
      "qHtml": "<p>Correct statements regarding Arrhenius equation among the following are :</p>\n<p>A. Factor $e^{-\\mathrm{Ea} / \\mathrm{RT}}$ corresponds to fraction of molecules having kinetic energy less than Ea.</p>\n<p>B. At a given temperature, lower the Ea, faster is the reaction.</p>\n<p>C. Increase in temperature by about $10^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C}$ doubles the rate of reaction.</p>\n<p>D. Plot of $\\log \\mathrm{k}$ vs $\\frac{1}{\\mathrm{~T}}$ gives a straight line with slope $=-\\frac{\\mathrm{Ea}}{\\mathrm{R}}$.</p>\n<p>Choose the correct answer from the options given below :</p>",
