      "s": "JEE Main 2026 (Online) 8th April Evening Shift. Correct option: A. $$ \\text { Coloured ions have unpaired electron. } $$\n\n$$ \\begin{aligned} &\\text { }\\\\ &\\begin{gathered} (i)\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\, T_i{ }^{+4}=4 s^{\\circ} 3 d^{\\circ} \\\\ n=0 \\end{gathered} \\end{aligned} $$\n\n$$ \\text { (ii) } V^{+2}=4 s^0 3 d^3 $$\n\n[Diagram: JEE Main 2026 (Online) 8th April Evening Shift Chemistry - d and f Block Elements Question 10 English Explanation 1]\n\n$$ n=3 $$\n\n$$ \\text { (iii) } \\mathrm{Mn}^{+2}=4 s^{\\circ} 3 d^5 $$\n\n[Diagram: JEE Main 2026 (Online) 8th April Evening Shift Chemistry - d and f Block Elements Question 10 English Explanation 2]\n\n$$ n=5 $$\n\n$$ \\text { (iv) } \\mathrm{Fe}^{+3}=4 \\mathrm{~s}^{\\circ} 3 \\mathrm{~d}^5 $$\n\n[Diagram: JEE Main 2026 (Online) 8th April Evening Shift Chemistry - d and f Block Elements Question 10 English Explanation 3]\n\n$$ n=5 $$\n\n$$ \\text { (v) } \\mathrm{Cr}^{+2}=4 \\mathrm{~s}^{\\circ} \\mathrm{3d}{ }^4 $$\n\n[Diagram: JEE Main 2026 (Online) 8th April Evening Shift Chemistry - d and f Block Elements Question 10 English Explanation 4]\n\n$$ n=4 $$\n\nThe absence of unpaired electron makes the element diamagnetic.\n\n$$ \\begin{aligned} & L a^{+3}=\\left[\\mathrm{Xe}\\right] 5 d^{\\circ} 6 s^{\\circ} \\\\ & 4 b^{+2}=\\left[\\mathrm{Xe}\\right] 4 f^{14} 6 s^{\\prime 4} \\\\ & L u^{+3}=\\left[\\mathrm{X}e\\right] 4 f^{14} 5 d^{\\circ} 6 s^{\\circ} \\\\ & C e^{+4}=\\left[\\mathrm{Xe}\\right] 4 f^{\\circ} 5 d^{\\circ} 6 s^{\\circ} \\\\ & A c^{+3}=\\left[Rn\\right] 6 d^{\\circ} 7 s^{\\circ} \\\\ & L_n^{+3}=\\left[Rn\\right] 5 f^{14} 6 d^{\\circ} 7 s^{\\circ} \\end{aligned} $$\n\nAns. (A)",
