      "a": 1,
      "s": "JEE Main 2026 (Online) 6th April Evening Shift. Correct option: B. Cr (Z = 24):\n\nGround state configuration:\n\n$$\\mathrm{Cr}: [\\mathrm{Ar}]\\,3d^5\\,4s^1$$\n\n(due to extra stability of half-filled $3d^5$ and $4s^1$ configuration)\n\nMn (Z = 25):\n\nGround state configuration:\n\n$$\\mathrm{Mn}: [\\mathrm{Ar}]\\,3d^5\\,4s^2$$\n\nFirst ionisation enthalpy, $\\Delta_i H_1$\n\nIn the first ionisation process:\n\nCr:\n\n$$\\mathrm{Cr} \\rightarrow \\mathrm{Cr}^+ + e^-$$\n\nAfter removal of one 4s electron:\n\n$$\\mathrm{Cr}^+: [\\mathrm{Ar}]\\,3d^5$$ (a very stable half-filled configuration)\n\nMn:\n\n$$\\mathrm{Mn} \\rightarrow \\mathrm{Mn}^+ + e^-$$\n\nAfter removal of one 4s electron:\n\n$$\\mathrm{Mn}^+: [\\mathrm{Ar}]\\,3d^5\\,4s^1$$ (not as stable as half-filled 3d⁵ only)\n\nBecause the resulting $\\mathrm{Cr}^+$ ion is particularly stable, less energy is required to form $\\mathrm{Cr}^+$ , i.e.\n\n$ \\Delta_i H_1(\\mathrm{Cr}) Thus,\n\nCorrect order for first ionisation enthalpy:\n\n$ \\Delta_i H_1: \\mathrm{Mn} > \\mathrm{Cr} $\n\n(Corresponds to option C .)\n\nSecond ionisation enthalpy, $\\Delta_i H_2$\n\nNow, let us remove the second electron.\n\nCr:\n\nFrom the already stable $\\mathrm{Cr}^+$ ($[Ar]\\,3d^5$):\n\n$$\\mathrm{Cr}^+ \\rightarrow \\mathrm{Cr}^{2+} + e^-$$\n\nAfter this, $\\mathrm{Cr}^{2+}$ becomes:\n\n$$[Ar]\\,3d^4$$ — less stable.\n\nTherefore, it requires a large amount of energy to remove this second electron.\n\nMn:\n\nFrom $\\mathrm{Mn}^+$ ($[Ar]\\,3d^5\\,4s^1$):\n\n$$\\mathrm{Mn}^+ \\rightarrow \\mathrm{Mn}^{2+} + e^-$$\n\nAfter this, $\\mathrm{Mn}^{2+}$ becomes:\n\n$$[Ar]\\,3d^5$$ — a stable half-filled configuration.\n\nThus, less energy is needed for the second ionisation.\n\nHence,\n\n$ \\Delta_i H_2(\\mathrm{Cr}) > \\Delta_i H_2(\\mathrm{Mn}) $\n\nwhich corresponds to option B .\n\nCombine results\n\n$\\Delta_i H_1$: Mn > Cr  → option C\n\n$\\Delta_i H_2$: Cr > Mn  → option B\n\nTherefore, the correct combination is:\n\n$ \\boxed{\\text{B and C only}} $\n\nFinal Answer: Option B",
      "source": "JEE Main 2026 (Online) 6th April Evening Shift | d & f Block | mnsik8zf",
      "pyq": true,
