      "s": "JEE Main 2026 (Online) 6th April Evening Shift. Correct option: D. $$ \\text { } \\begin{aligned}(A)\\,\\, & \\mathrm{NiCl}_4^{-2} \\\\ & \\mathrm{Ni}^{2+}=4 \\mathrm{~s}^0 3 \\mathrm{~d}^8 \\end{aligned} $$\n\n$$ \\text { Cl: weak field ligand, high spin complex. } $$\n\n[Diagram: JEE Main 2026 (Online) 6th April Evening Shift Chemistry - Coordination Compounds Question 11 English Explanation 1]\n\n$$ \\begin{aligned}(B) & \\mathrm{Ni}\\left(\\mathrm{NH}_3\\right)_6^{+2} \\\\ & \\mathrm{Ni}^{+2} = 4 \\mathrm{~s}^0 3 d^8 \\end{aligned} $$\n\n$\\mathrm{NH}_3$ : Weak field ligand, high spin complex.\n\n[Diagram: JEE Main 2026 (Online) 6th April Evening Shift Chemistry - Coordination Compounds Question 11 English Explanation 2]\n\n$$ \\begin{aligned} &\\text { }\\\\ &\\begin{aligned}(C)\\,\\, & \\mathrm{Ni}(\\mathrm{CO})_4 \\\\ & \\mathrm{Ni}^0=4 s^2 3 d^8 \\xrightarrow[\\text { d-system }]{\\text { converted }} 4 s^0 3 d^{10} \\end{aligned} \\end{aligned} $$\n\n[Diagram: JEE Main 2026 (Online) 6th April Evening Shift Chemistry - Coordination Compounds Question 11 English Explanation 3]\n\n$$ \\begin{aligned}(D)\\,\\, & \\mathrm{Ni}(\\mathrm{CN})_4^{-2} \\\\ & \\mathrm{Ni}^{+2}=4 \\mathrm{~s}^0 3 d^8 \\end{aligned} $$\n\nCN: strong field ligand, low spin complex\n\n[Diagram: JEE Main 2026 (Online) 6th April Evening Shift Chemistry - Coordination Compounds Question 11 English Explanation 4]",
      "source": "JEE Main 2026 (Online) 6th April Evening Shift | Coordination Compounds | mnsik908",
      "pyq": true,
      "exactPaperText": true,
