      "q": "Given below are two statements :\n\nStatement I : Hybridisation, shape and spin only magnetic moment of $\\mathrm{K}_3\\left[\\mathrm{Co}\\left(\\mathrm{CO}_3\\right)_3\\right]$ is $\\mathrm{sp}^3 \\mathrm{~d}^2$, octahedral and 4.9 BM respectively.\n\nStatement II : Geometry, hybridisation and spin only magnetic moment values $(B M)$ of the ions $\\left[\\mathrm{Ni}(\\mathrm{CN})_4\\right]^{2-},\\left[\\mathrm{MnBr}_4\\right]^{2-}$ and $\\left[\\mathrm{CoF}_6\\right]^{3-}$ respectively are square planar, tetrahedral, octahedral; $\\mathrm{dsp}^2, \\mathrm{sp}^3, \\mathrm{sp}^3 \\mathrm{~d}^2$ and $0,5.9,4.9$.\n\nIn the light of the above statements, choose the correct answer from the options given below",
      "qHtml": "<p>Given below are two statements :</p>\n<p><b><b>Statement I :</b></b> Hybridisation, shape and spin only magnetic moment of $\\mathrm{K}_3\\left[\\mathrm{Co}\\left(\\mathrm{CO}_3\\right)_3\\right]$ is $\\mathrm{sp}^3 \\mathrm{~d}^2$, octahedral and 4.9 BM respectively.</p>\n<p><b><b>Statement II :</b></b> Geometry, hybridisation and spin only magnetic moment values $(B M)$ of the ions $\\left[\\mathrm{Ni}(\\mathrm{CN})_4\\right]^{2-},\\left[\\mathrm{MnBr}_4\\right]^{2-}$ and $\\left[\\mathrm{CoF}_6\\right]^{3-}$ respectively are square planar, tetrahedral, octahedral; $\\mathrm{dsp}^2, \\mathrm{sp}^3, \\mathrm{sp}^3 \\mathrm{~d}^2$ and $0,5.9,4.9$.</p>\n<p>In the light of the above statements, choose the correct answer from the options given below</p>",
