      "s": "JEE Main 2022 (Online) 24th June Morning Shift. Correct option: C. [Diagram: JEE Main 2022 (Online) 24th June Morning Shift Chemistry - p-Block Elements Question 119 English Explanation]\n\nIt has two 3-centre-2-electron bonds and four\n2-centre-2-electron bonds.\n\nHence, all B–H bonds are not equivalent.\n\nIt is an electron deficient compound as the octet of\nboron is incomplete.\n\nHence, it can behave as a Lewis acid.\n\nIt can be synthesized from both BF 3 and NaBH 4\n\n$$2B{F_3} + 6NaH\\buildrel {450K} \\over\n\\longrightarrow {B_2}{H_6} + 6NaF$$\n\n$$2NaB{H_4} + {I_2} \\to {B_2}{H_6} + 2NaI + {H_2}$$\n\nIt is a non-planar molecule.\n\nHence, only Statements (C) and (D) are correct.",
