      "a": 0,
      "s": "JEE Main 2026 (Online) 4th April Morning Shift. Correct option: A. For a monoatomic anion $A^-$:\n\nNumber of electrons in $A^-$ $= 36$\n\nSince it is an anion with charge $-1$, the neutral atom $A$ must have one electron less.\n\nSo, number of electrons in neutral atom $A$:\n\n$$ 36 - 1 = 35 $$\n\nHence, atomic number of $A$ is $35$.\n\nThis element is bromine .\n\nNow, number of neutrons $= 45$\n\nSo, mass number:\n\n$$ \\text{Mass number} = \\text{protons} + \\text{neutrons} = 35 + 45 = 80 $$\n\nThus, atomic mass number is:\n\n$$ 80 $$\n\nNow let us find the group.\n\nBromine $(Z = 35)$ belongs to group 17 in the periodic table.\n\nAlso, bromine is a liquid at room temperature.\n\nSo, the correct answer is:\n\n$$ \\boxed{\\text{Option A: } 80,\\ 17,\\ \\text{liquid}} $$",
