      "a": 2,
      "s": "JEE Main 2026 (Online) 8th April Evening Shift. Correct option: C. Let us analyse both statements carefully using the concept of fractional distillation as given in NCERT.\n\nConcept:\n\nFractional distillation is a process used to separate a mixture of two or more liquids having different boiling points.\n\nThe liquid having a lower boiling point vaporises first.\n\nAs vapours rise through the fractionating column, they repeatedly condense and vaporise.\n\nThe temperature in the column gradually decreases from bottom to top.\n\nHence, vapours rising upwards become richer in the more volatile (lower boiling point) component.\n\nStatement I\n\n“Vapours of the liquid with higher boiling point condense before vapours of the liquid with lower boiling points in fractional distillation.”\n\nLiquids with higher boiling point are less volatile .\n\nThus, their vapours condense earlier (lower in the column) because they require a lower temperature difference to liquefy.\n\nTherefore, Statement I is true .\n\nStatement II\n\n“The vapours rising up in the fractionating column become richer in high boiling component of the mixture.”\n\nAs explained, the rising vapours become richer in the low boiling or more volatile component, not the high boiling one.\n\nTherefore, Statement II is false .\n\nCorrect Answer:\n\nOption C: Statement I is true but Statement II is false",
