      "q": "Given below are two statements:\n\nConsider the following reaction\n\n[Diagram: JEE Main 2025 (Online) 23rd January Evening Shift Chemistry - Aldehydes, Ketones and Carboxylic Acids Question 53 English 1]\n\nStatement (I): In the case of formaldehyde\n[Diagram: JEE Main 2025 (Online) 23rd January Evening Shift Chemistry - Aldehydes, Ketones and Carboxylic Acids Question 53 English 2]\nis about 2280, due to small substituents, hydration is faster.\n\nStatement (II) : In the case of trichloro acetaldehyde\n[Diagram: JEE Main 2025 (Online) 23rd January Evening Shift Chemistry - Aldehydes, Ketones and Carboxylic Acids Question 53 English 3]\nis about 2000 due to $-$I effect of $-$Cl .\n\nIn the light of the above statements, choose the correct answer from the options given below :",
