      "s": "JEE Main 2026 (Online) 2nd April Evening Shift. Correct option: C. The correct pair is:\n\n$$\\text{Amino acid (A) = Y, Hormone (B) = Thyroxine}$$\n\nSo, the correct option is:\n\n$$\\boxed{\\text{Option C}}$$\n\nReason:\n\nThe one-letter code $Y$ stands for tyrosine .\n\nThyroxine is an iodinated derivative of tyrosine .\n\nInsulin is a protein hormone , not an iodinated derivative of an amino acid.\n\nHence,\n\n$$\\boxed{Y \\rightarrow \\text{Thyroxine}}$$",
