      "qHtml": "<p>Consider the quadratic equation $\\left(n^2-2 n+2\\right) x^2-3 x+\\left(n^2-2 n+2\\right)^2=0, n \\in \\mathbf{R}$. Let $\\alpha$ be the minimum value of the product of its roots and $\\beta$ be the maximum value of the sum of its roots. Then the sum of the first six terms of the G.P., whose first term is $\\alpha$ and the common ratio is $\\frac{\\alpha}{\\beta}$, is :</p>",
