      "a": 1,
      "s": "JEE Main 2026 (Online) 5th April Morning Shift. Correct option: B. Given:\n\n$\\alpha,\\beta$ are roots of $x^2+ax+b=0$\n\n$\\beta-\\alpha=\\sqrt{11}$\n\n$\\beta^2-\\alpha^2=3i\\sqrt{11}$\n\nWe have to find $\\left(\\beta^3-\\alpha^3\\right)^2$.\n\nNow,\n\n$$ \\beta^2-\\alpha^2=(\\beta-\\alpha)(\\beta+\\alpha) $$\n\nSubstituting the given values,\n\n$$ 3i\\sqrt{11}=\\sqrt{11}(\\beta+\\alpha) $$\n\nSince $\\sqrt{11}\\neq 0$, we get\n\n$$ \\beta+\\alpha=3i $$\n\nNow use the identity\n\n$$ \\beta^3-\\alpha^3=(\\beta-\\alpha)(\\beta^2+\\alpha\\beta+\\alpha^2) $$\n\nSo first let us find $\\beta^2+\\alpha\\beta+\\alpha^2$.\n\nWe know\n\n$$ (\\beta+\\alpha)^2=\\beta^2+\\alpha^2+2\\alpha\\beta $$\n\nAlso,\n\n$$ \\alpha\\beta=\\frac{(\\alpha+\\beta)^2-(\\beta-\\alpha)^2}{4} $$\n\nSubstitute the values:\n\n$$ \\alpha+\\beta=3i,\\qquad \\beta-\\alpha=\\sqrt{11} $$\n\nThus,\n\n$$ \\alpha\\beta=\\frac{(3i)^2-(\\sqrt{11})^2}{4} =\\frac{-9-11}{4} =\\frac{-20}{4} =-5 $$\n\nNow,\n\n$$ \\alpha^2+\\beta^2=(\\alpha+\\beta)^2-2\\alpha\\beta $$\n\nSo,\n\n$$ \\alpha^2+\\beta^2=(3i)^2-2(-5)=-9+10=1 $$\n\nHence,\n\n$$ \\beta^2+\\alpha\\beta+\\alpha^2=1+(-5)=-4 $$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$ \\beta^3-\\alpha^3=(\\beta-\\alpha)(\\beta^2+\\alpha\\beta+\\alpha^2) =\\sqrt{11}\\cdot(-4) =-4\\sqrt{11} $$\n\nNow square it:\n\n$$ \\left(\\beta^3-\\alpha^3\\right)^2=\\left(-4\\sqrt{11}\\right)^2=16\\cdot 11=176 $$\n\nSo the correct answer is:\n\n$$ \\boxed{176} $$\n\nHence, Option B is correct.",
