      "s": "JEE Main 2026 (Online) 4th April Evening Shift. Correct option: D. Solve the quadratic equation first:\n\n$$ z^2+4z+16=0 $$\n\nUsing the quadratic formula,\n\n$$ z=\\frac{-4\\pm\\sqrt{16-64}}{2} =\\frac{-4\\pm\\sqrt{-48}}{2} =\\frac{-4\\pm 4\\sqrt{3}i}{2} =-2\\pm 2\\sqrt{3}i $$\n\nSo the set is\n\n$$ S=\\{-2+2\\sqrt{3}i,\\,-2-2\\sqrt{3}i\\} $$\n\nNow we need to find\n\n$$ \\sum_{z\\in S}|z+\\sqrt{3}i|^2 $$\n\nThat is,\n\n$$ |-2+2\\sqrt{3}i+\\sqrt{3}i|^2 + |-2-2\\sqrt{3}i+\\sqrt{3}i|^2 $$\n\nSimplify each term:\n\nFor $z=-2+2\\sqrt{3}i$,\n\n$$ z+\\sqrt{3}i=-2+3\\sqrt{3}i $$\n\nHence,\n\n$$ |-2+3\\sqrt{3}i|^2=(-2)^2+(3\\sqrt{3})^2=4+27=31 $$\n\nFor $z=-2-2\\sqrt{3}i$,\n\n$$ z+\\sqrt{3}i=-2-\\sqrt{3}i $$\n\nHence,\n\n$$ |-2-\\sqrt{3}i|^2=(-2)^2+(-\\sqrt{3})^2=4+3=7 $$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$ \\sum_{z\\in S}|z+\\sqrt{3}i|^2=31+7=38 $$\n\nSo the correct answer is:\n\n$$ \\boxed{38} $$\n\nOption D",
