      "a": 2,
      "s": "JEE Main 2026 (Online) 5th April Morning Shift. Correct option: C. Given\n\n$$ 3\\sin^2 x + 12\\cos x - 3 = p,\\qquad x\\in \\mathbb{R} $$\n\nWe need all integral values of $p$ for which this equation has at least one real solution.\n\nNow use the identity\n\n$$ \\sin^2 x = 1 - \\cos^2 x $$\n\nSo,\n\n$$ 3(1-\\cos^2 x)+12\\cos x-3 = p $$\n\nSimplifying,\n\n$$ 3 - 3\\cos^2 x + 12\\cos x - 3 = p $$\n\n$$ -3\\cos^2 x + 12\\cos x = p $$\n\nLet\n\n$$ t = \\cos x $$\n\nThen\n\n$$ -1 \\le t \\le 1 $$\n\nSo we have\n\n$$ p = -3t^2 + 12t $$\n\nNow we need the range of\n\n$$ f(t) = -3t^2 + 12t,\\qquad -1 \\le t \\le 1 $$\n\nThis is a downward opening parabola.\n\nFind its values at the endpoints:\n\n$$ f(-1) = -3(1) + 12(-1) = -3 - 12 = -15 $$\n\n$$ f(1) = -3(1) + 12(1) = -3 + 12 = 9 $$\n\nAlso,\n\n$$ f'(t) = -6t + 12 $$\n\nFor $-1 \\le t \\le 1$, we have\n\n$$ -6t + 12 > 0 $$\n\nso $f(t)$ is increasing on $[-1,1]$.\n\nHence the range of $p$ is\n\n$$ -15 \\le p \\le 9 $$\n\nTherefore all integral values of $p$ are\n\n$$ -15,-14,-13,\\dots,9 $$\n\nThis is an AP with first term $-15$, last term $9$.\n\nNumber of terms:\n\n$$ n = 9-(-15)+1 = 25 $$\n\nSum:\n\n$$ S = \\frac{n}{2}(a+l) = \\frac{25}{2}(-15+9) = \\frac{25}{2}(-6) = -75 $$\n\nHence, the required sum is\n\n$$ \\boxed{-75} $$\n\nSo, the correct option is:\n\n$$ \\boxed{\\text{Option C}} $$",
