      "s": "JEE Main 2026 (Online) 2nd April Morning Shift. Correct option: D. $ 50\\left(\\frac{2x}{1+3i}-\\frac{y}{1-2i}\\right)=31+17i $\n\nWe need to find $10(x-3y)$.\n\nFirst, simplify the fractions by rationalising the denominators.\n\n$ \\frac{2x}{1+3i}=\\frac{2x(1-3i)}{(1+3i)(1-3i)} $\n\n$ =\\frac{2x(1-3i)}{1+9}=\\frac{2x(1-3i)}{10} $\n\n$ =\\frac{x}{5}(1-3i) $\n\nSimilarly,\n\n$ \\frac{y}{1-2i}=\\frac{y(1+2i)}{(1-2i)(1+2i)} $\n\n$ =\\frac{y(1+2i)}{1+4}=\\frac{y(1+2i)}{5} $\n\nNow substitute into the given equation:\n\n$ 50\\left(\\frac{x}{5}(1-3i)-\\frac{y}{5}(1+2i)\\right)=31+17i $\n\nTake $\\frac{1}{5}$ common inside:\n\n$ 50\\cdot \\frac{1}{5}\\left[x(1-3i)-y(1+2i)\\right]=31+17i $\n\n$ 10\\left[x(1-3i)-y(1+2i)\\right]=31+17i $\n\nExpand:\n\n$ 10\\left[x-3xi-y-2yi\\right]=31+17i $\n\n$ 10\\left[(x-y)+(-3x-2y)i\\right]=31+17i $\n\nSo,\n\n$ 10(x-y)+10(-3x-2y)i=31+17i $\n\nNow compare real and imaginary parts:\n\n$ 10(x-y)=31 $\n\n$ 10(-3x-2y)=17 $\n\nThus,\n\n$ x-y=\\frac{31}{10} $\n\n$ -3x-2y=\\frac{17}{10} $\n\nNow solve these equations.\n\nFrom the first equation,\n\n$ x=y+\\frac{31}{10} $\n\nSubstitute into the second:\n\n$ -3\\left(y+\\frac{31}{10}\\right)-2y=\\frac{17}{10} $\n\n$ -3y-\\frac{93}{10}-2y=\\frac{17}{10} $\n\n$ -5y=\\frac{17}{10}+\\frac{93}{10} $\n\n$ -5y=\\frac{110}{10}=11 $\n\n$ y=-\\frac{11}{5} $\n\nThen\n\n$ x=y+\\frac{31}{10}=-\\frac{11}{5}+\\frac{31}{10} $\n\n$ x=-\\frac{22}{10}+\\frac{31}{10}=\\frac{9}{10} $\n\nNow find:\n\n$ 10(x-3y)=10\\left(\\frac{9}{10}-3\\left(-\\frac{11}{5}\\right)\\right) $\n\n$ =10\\left(\\frac{9}{10}+\\frac{33}{5}\\right) $\n\n$ =10\\left(\\frac{9}{10}+\\frac{66}{10}\\right) $\n\n$ =10\\cdot \\frac{75}{10}=75 $\n\nTherefore, the value of $10(x-3y)$ is\n\n$ \\boxed{75} $\n\nSo, the correct option is $\\boxed{\\text{D}}$.",
