      "q": "Let $\\alpha, \\beta$ be the roots of the equation $x^2 - 3x + r = 0$, and $\\frac{\\alpha}{2}, 2\\beta$ be the roots of the equation $x^2 + 3x + r = 0$.\nIf the roots of the equation $x^2 + 6x = m$ are $2\\alpha + \\beta + 2r$ and $\\alpha - 2\\beta - \\frac{r}{2}$, then $m$ is equal to :",
      "qHtml": "<p>Let $\\alpha, \\beta$ be the roots of the equation $x^2 - 3x + r = 0$, and $\\frac{\\alpha}{2}, 2\\beta$ be the roots of the equation $x^2 + 3x + r = 0$.</p><p>If the roots of the equation $x^2 + 6x = m$ are $2\\alpha + \\beta + 2r$ and $\\alpha - 2\\beta - \\frac{r}{2}$, then $m$ is equal to :</p>",
