      "s": "JEE Main 2025 (Online) 4th April Morning Shift. Correct option: A. $$\\begin{aligned}\n& x^2+4 x-n=0 \\text { has integer roots } \\\\\n& \\Rightarrow x=\\frac{-4 \\pm \\sqrt{16+4 n}}{2}=-2 \\pm \\sqrt{4+n}\n\\end{aligned}$$\n\nFor $x$ to be integer $4+n$ must be perfect squares\n\n$$\\begin{aligned}\n& n \\in[20,100] \\\\\n& n+4 \\in[24,104]=S\n\\end{aligned}$$\n\n$\\left\\{25,36, \\ldots 10^2\\right\\} \\in S \\Rightarrow 5^2, 6^2, \\ldots 10^2 \\Rightarrow 6$ values of $n$",
