      "s": "JEE Main 2026 (Online) 5th April Morning Shift. Correct option: B. Let\n\n$A$ = event that the letter came from ANANTPUR\n\n$K$ = event that the letter came from KANPUR\n\n$B$ = event that on the envelope, the two visible consecutive letters are AN\n\nWe have to find:\n\n$$ P(A \\mid B) $$\n\nUsing Bayes’ theorem,\n\n$$ P(A \\mid B)=\\frac{P(A)\\,P(B\\mid A)}{P(A)\\,P(B\\mid A)+P(K)\\,P(B\\mid K)} $$\n\nSince the letter is known to have come either from ANANTPUR or KANPUR, and no other information is given, we take\n\n$$ P(A)=P(K)=\\frac{1}{2} $$\n\nSo,\n\n$$ P(A \\mid B)=\\frac{P(B\\mid A)}{P(B\\mid A)+P(B\\mid K)} $$\n\nNow we find these probabilities.\n\n1. Probability of seeing AN in ANANTPUR\n\nWord: ANANTPUR\n\nIts consecutive pairs are:\n\n$$ AN,\\ NA,\\ AN,\\ NT,\\ TP,\\ PU,\\ UR $$\n\nThere are $7$ consecutive pairs in all, and AN occurs $2$ times.\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$ P(B\\mid A)=\\frac{2}{7} $$\n\n2. Probability of seeing AN in KANPUR\n\nWord: KANPUR\n\nIts consecutive pairs are:\n\n$$ KA,\\ AN,\\ NP,\\ PU,\\ UR $$\n\nThere are $5$ consecutive pairs in all, and AN occurs $1$ time.\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$ P(B\\mid K)=\\frac{1}{5} $$\n\n3. Apply Bayes’ theorem\n\n$$ P(A \\mid B)=\\frac{\\frac{2}{7}}{\\frac{2}{7}+\\frac{1}{5}} $$\n\nTake LCM:\n\n$$ \\frac{2}{7}+\\frac{1}{5}=\\frac{10+7}{35}=\\frac{17}{35} $$\n\nSo,\n\n$$ P(A \\mid B)=\\frac{\\frac{2}{7}}{\\frac{17}{35}} =\\frac{2}{7}\\cdot\\frac{35}{17} =\\frac{10}{17} $$\n\nTherefore, the required probability is\n\n$$ \\boxed{\\frac{10}{17}} $$\n\nSo, the correct option is B .",
