      "s": "JEE Main 2026 (Online) 6th April Evening Shift. Correct option: C. We want every pair drawn to have one blue and one green . Since there are 6 blue and 6 green balls, we will draw a total of 6 pairs.\n\nFor each pair to be mixed (one of each colour), we must match the 6 blue balls with the 6 green balls in pairs. The number of such “good” pairings is counted by choosing and matching one ball of one colour with one ball of the other colour.\n\nThe total number of ways to split 12 balls into 6 pairs (without caring about the order of drawing inside a pair) is counted separately. The required probability is:\n\nProbability $=\\frac{\\lfloor 6 \\times\\lfloor 6}{\\left(\\frac{12}{\\left(\\lfloor 2)^6\\lfloor 6\\right.}\\right) \\times\\lfloor 6}=\\frac{16}{231}$\n\nSo, the probability that each drawn pair consists of one blue and one green ball is $\\frac{16}{231}$.",
