      "s": "JEE Main 2026 (Online) 6th April Morning Shift. Correct option: A. [Diagram: JEE Main 2026 (Online) 6th April Morning Shift Mathematics - Parabola Question 4 English Explanation]\n\n$\\begin{aligned} & \\text{For the parabola } y^2=12x,\\ \\text{we have } 4a=12 \\Rightarrow a=3. \\\\\\\\ & \\text{So, the parametric point on } y^2=4ax \\text{ is } (at^2,2at). \\\\\\\\ & \\text{Let the ordinate (}y\\text{-coordinate) of }P \\text{ be in ratio }1:2 \\text{ with }Q. \\\\\\\\ & \\text{So we take }P(3t^2,6t)\\ \\text{and}\\ Q\\big(3(2t)^2,6(2t)\\big)=\\left(12t^2,12t\\right). \\\\\\\\ & \\text{Now find }PQ: \\\\\\\\ & PQ=\\sqrt{(12t^2-3t^2)^2+(12t-6t)^2} \\\\\\\\ & \\quad=\\sqrt{(9t^2)^2+(6t)^2}=\\sqrt{81t^4+36t^2}. \\\\\\\\ & \\text{Given }PQ=3\\sqrt{13}\\Rightarrow PQ^2=117. \\\\\\\\ & \\text{So, }81t^4+36t^2=117 \\\\\\\\ & \\Rightarrow 9t^4+4t^2-13=0 \\\\\\\\ & \\Rightarrow (t^2-1)(9t^2+13)=0. \\\\\\\\ & \\text{Since }t^2\\ge 0,\\ 9t^2+13\\ne 0,\\ \\text{so }t^2=1 \\Rightarrow t=1. \\\\\\\\ & \\text{Hence }P(3,6),\\ Q(12,12). \\\\\\\\ & \\text{Focus of }y^2=12x\\text{ is }S(a,0)=(3,0). \\\\\\\\ & \\text{Slope of }QS=\\frac{12-0}{12-3}=\\frac{12}{9}=\\frac{4}{3}. \\\\\\\\ & \\text{Line }PS \\text{ is vertical since }P(3,6)\\text{ and }S(3,0)\\text{ have same }x. \\\\\\\\ & \\text{So the angle }\\alpha \\text{ at the focus is the angle between }QS \\text{ and the vertical.} \\\\\\\\ & \\text{If slope of }QS \\text{ is }\\frac{4}{3},\\ \\text{then the angle it makes with the vertical has} \\\\\\\\ & \\tan\\alpha=\\frac{3}{4}. \\\\\\\\ & \\Rightarrow \\sin\\alpha=\\frac{3}{5}. \\end{aligned}$",
