      "s": "JEE Main 2026 (Online) 5th April Evening Shift. Correct option: B. For the parabola\n\n$$ y^2=8x $$\n\nwe compare it with the standard form\n\n$$ y^2=4ax $$\n\nSo,\n\n$$ 4a=8 \\implies a=2 $$\n\nHence:\n\nfocus $S=(2,0)$\n\ndirectrix is\n\n$$ x=-2 $$\n\nSince the directrix cuts the $x$-axis at point $A$, we get\n\n$$ A=(-2,0) $$\n\nNow let $B(\\alpha,\\beta)$ be a point on the parabola such that the slope of $AB$ is $\\dfrac35$.\n\nThe slope of $AB$ is\n\n$$ \\frac{\\beta-0}{\\alpha-(-2)}=\\frac{\\beta}{\\alpha+2} $$\n\nGiven this is $\\dfrac35$, so\n\n$$ \\frac{\\beta}{\\alpha+2}=\\frac35 $$\n\nThus,\n\n$$ 5\\beta=3(\\alpha+2) \\tag{1} $$\n\nAlso, since $B$ lies on the parabola $y^2=8x$,\n\n$$ \\beta^2=8\\alpha \\tag{2} $$\n\nNow substitute from (1). From (1),\n\n$$ \\beta=\\frac{3(\\alpha+2)}{5} $$\n\nPut into (2):\n\n$$ \\left(\\frac{3(\\alpha+2)}{5}\\right)^2=8\\alpha $$\n\n$$ \\frac{9(\\alpha+2)^2}{25}=8\\alpha $$\n\n$$ 9(\\alpha+2)^2=200\\alpha $$\n\n$$ 9(\\alpha^2+4\\alpha+4)=200\\alpha $$\n\n$$ 9\\alpha^2+36\\alpha+36=200\\alpha $$\n\n$$ 9\\alpha^2-164\\alpha+36=0 $$\n\nNow solve:\n\n$$ 9\\alpha^2-164\\alpha+36=0 $$\n\nDiscriminant:\n\n$$ D=164^2-4\\cdot 9\\cdot 36=26896-1296=25600 $$\n\n$$ \\sqrt D=160 $$\n\nSo,\n\n$$ \\alpha=\\frac{164\\pm 160}{18} $$\n\nHence,\n\n$$ \\alpha=\\frac{324}{18}=18 \\quad \\text{or} \\quad \\alpha=\\frac{4}{18}=\\frac29 $$\n\nGiven $\\alpha>1$, we take\n\n$$ \\alpha=18 $$\n\nThen from $\\beta^2=8\\alpha$,\n\n$$ \\beta^2=144 \\implies \\beta=\\pm 12 $$\n\nSince slope is $\\dfrac35>0$, $\\beta$ must be positive. Therefore\n\n$$ B=(18,12) $$\n\nNow $BC$ is a focal chord of the parabola.\n\nFor parabola $y^2=4ax$, a point in parametric form is\n\n$$ (at^2,\\,2at) $$\n\nHere $a=2$, so point is\n\n$$ (2t^2,\\,4t) $$\n\nFor point $B=(18,12)$,\n\n$$ 2t^2=18 \\implies t^2=9 \\implies t=3 $$\n\nand\n\n$$ 4t=12 \\implies t=3 $$\n\nSo $B$ corresponds to parameter $t=3$.\n\nIf $BC$ is a focal chord, then the other endpoint corresponds to parameter $-\\dfrac1t$.\n\nThus for $t=3$, point $C$ corresponds to parameter $-\\dfrac13$.\n\nSo,\n\n$$ C=\\left(2\\left(\\frac{1}{9}\\right),\\,4\\left(-\\frac13\\right)\\right) =\\left(\\frac29,\\,-\\frac43\\right) $$\n\nNow find area of $\\triangle ABC$.\n\nCoordinates are:\n\n$$ A=(-2,0),\\quad B=(18,12),\\quad C=\\left(\\frac29,-\\frac43\\right) $$\n\nUsing determinant formula,\n\n$$ \\text{Area} = \\frac12\\left| x_1(y_2-y_3)+x_2(y_3-y_1)+x_3(y_1-y_2) \\right| $$\n\nSo,\n\n$$ \\text{Area} = \\frac12\\left[ -2\\left(12+\\frac43\\right) +18\\left(-\\frac43\\right) +\\frac29(0-12) \\right] \\Bigg| $$\n\nNow simplify:\n\n$$ 12+\\frac43=\\frac{40}{3} $$\n\nSo,\n\n$$ -2\\cdot \\frac{40}{3}=-\\frac{80}{3} $$\n\nAlso,\n\n$$ 18\\cdot \\left(-\\frac43\\right)=-24 $$\n\nand\n\n$$ \\frac29(-12)=-\\frac{24}{9}=-\\frac83 $$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$ \\text{Area} = \\frac12\\left|-\\frac{80}{3}-24-\\frac83\\right| $$\n\n$$ = \\frac12\\left|-\\frac{88}{3}-24\\right| = \\frac12\\left|-\\frac{88}{3}-\\frac{72}{3}\\right| $$\n\n$$ = \\frac12\\left|-\\frac{160}{3}\\right| = \\frac{80}{3} $$\n\nHence,\n\n$$ 6\\times \\text{Area} = 6\\cdot \\frac{80}{3}=160 $$\n\nTherefore, the required answer is\n\n$$ \\boxed{160} $$\n\nSo, the correct option is B .",
