      "s": "JEE Main 2026 (Online) 2nd April Morning Shift. Correct option: D. Since $a $$ \\frac{x^2}{a^2}+\\frac{y^2}{b^2}=1, $$\n\nwe use the eccentricity formula\n\n$$ e=\\sqrt{1-\\frac{a^2}{b^2}}. $$\n\nGiven\n\n$$ e=\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{3}, $$\n\nso\n\n$$ e^2=\\frac{5}{9}. $$\n\nHence,\n\n$$ 1-\\frac{a^2}{b^2}=\\frac{5}{9} $$\n\nwhich gives\n\n$$ \\frac{a^2}{b^2}=1-\\frac{5}{9}=\\frac{4}{9}. $$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$ a^2=\\frac{4}{9}b^2. $$\n\nNow the ellipse passes through $(4,3)$, so it satisfies the equation:\n\n$$ \\frac{4^2}{a^2}+\\frac{3^2}{b^2}=1. $$\n\nThat is,\n\n$$ \\frac{16}{a^2}+\\frac{9}{b^2}=1. $$\n\nSubstitute $a^2=\\frac{4}{9}b^2$:\n\n$$ \\frac{16}{\\frac{4}{9}b^2}+\\frac{9}{b^2}=1. $$\n\nSimplifying,\n\n$$ 16\\cdot \\frac{9}{4b^2}+\\frac{9}{b^2}=1 $$\n\n$$ \\frac{36}{b^2}+\\frac{9}{b^2}=1 $$\n\n$$ \\frac{45}{b^2}=1 $$\n\nso\n\n$$ b^2=45. $$\n\nThen\n\n$$ a^2=\\frac{4}{9}\\cdot 45=20. $$\n\nFor an ellipse with major axis along the $y$-axis, the length of latus rectum is\n\n$$ \\frac{2a^2}{b}. $$\n\nSo,\n\n$$ \\text{Length of latus rectum}=\\frac{2\\cdot 20}{\\sqrt{45}} =\\frac{40}{3\\sqrt{5}}. $$\n\nRationalising,\n\n$$ \\frac{40}{3\\sqrt{5}}\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{\\sqrt{5}} =\\frac{8\\sqrt{5}}{3}. $$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is\n\n$$ \\boxed{\\frac{8\\sqrt{5}}{3}} $$\n\nSo, Option D is correct.",
