      "s": "JEE Main 2026 (Online) 6th April Morning Shift. Correct option: A. For the hyperbola\n\n$$ \\frac{x^2}{a^2}-\\frac{y^2}{b^2}=1 $$\n\nwe are given that it passes through the point $(6,4\\sqrt{3})$.\n\nSo, substituting $x=6$ and $y=4\\sqrt{3}$:\n\n$$ \\frac{36}{a^2}-\\frac{(4\\sqrt{3})^2}{b^2}=1 $$\n\nSince\n\n$$ (4\\sqrt{3})^2=48 $$\n\nwe get\n\n$$ \\frac{36}{a^2}-\\frac{48}{b^2}=1 \\qquad ...(1) $$\n\nNow for the hyperbola\n\n$$ \\frac{x^2}{a^2}-\\frac{y^2}{b^2}=1 $$\n\nits eccentricity is\n\n$$ e=\\sqrt{1+\\frac{b^2}{a^2}} $$\n\nSo,\n\n$$ e^2=1+\\frac{b^2}{a^2} $$\n\nGiven:\n\n$$ 15(e^2+1)=34e $$\n\nSubstitute $e^2=1+\\frac{b^2}{a^2}$ if needed, but first solve this equation in $e$:\n\n$$ 15e^2-34e+15=0 $$\n\nFactorising:\n\n$$ 15e^2-25e-9e+15=0 $$\n\n$$ 5e(3e-5)-3(3e-5)=0 $$\n\n$$ (3e-5)(5e-3)=0 $$\n\nSo,\n\n$$ e=\\frac{5}{3} \\quad \\text{or} \\quad e=\\frac{3}{5} $$\n\nBut for a hyperbola, $e>1$, hence\n\n$$ e=\\frac{5}{3} $$\n\nNow,\n\n$$ e^2=1+\\frac{b^2}{a^2} $$\n\nSo,\n\n$$ \\frac{25}{9}=1+\\frac{b^2}{a^2} $$\n\n$$ \\frac{b^2}{a^2}=\\frac{25}{9}-1=\\frac{16}{9} $$\n\nThus,\n\n$$ b^2=\\frac{16}{9}a^2 $$\n\nSubstitute this in equation $(1)$:\n\n$$ \\frac{36}{a^2}-\\frac{48}{\\frac{16}{9}a^2}=1 $$\n\nNow,\n\n$$ \\frac{48}{\\frac{16}{9}a^2}=48\\cdot \\frac{9}{16a^2}=\\frac{27}{a^2} $$\n\nSo,\n\n$$ \\frac{36}{a^2}-\\frac{27}{a^2}=1 $$\n\n$$ \\frac{9}{a^2}=1 $$\n\nHence,\n\n$$ a^2=9 $$\n\nThen,\n\n$$ b^2=\\frac{16}{9}\\cdot 9=16 $$\n\nNow consider the second hyperbola:\n\n$$ \\frac{x^2}{b^2}-\\frac{y^2}{2(a^2+1)}=1 $$\n\nSubstitute $a^2=9$ and $b^2=16$:\n\n$$ \\frac{x^2}{16}-\\frac{y^2}{2(9+1)}=1 $$\n\n$$ \\frac{x^2}{16}-\\frac{y^2}{20}=1 $$\n\nFor a hyperbola of the form\n\n$$ \\frac{x^2}{A^2}-\\frac{y^2}{B^2}=1 $$\n\nthe length of the latus rectum is\n\n$$ \\frac{2B^2}{A} $$\n\nHere,\n\n$$ A^2=16 \\Rightarrow A=4, \\qquad B^2=20 $$\n\nTherefore, length of latus rectum\n\n$$ =\\frac{2\\cdot 20}{4}=10 $$\n\nHence, the required answer is\n\n$$ \\boxed{10} $$\n\nSo, the correct option is A .",
