      "s": "JEE Main 2026 (Online) 5th April Evening Shift. Correct option: C. For a hyperbola, the eccentricity $e>1$.\n\nWe are given:\n\n$$ 6e^2-11e+3=0 $$\n\nSolve this quadratic:\n\n$$ 6e^2-9e-2e+3=0 $$\n\n$$ 3e(2e-3)-1(2e-3)=0 $$\n\n$$ (2e-3)(3e-1)=0 $$\n\nSo,\n\n$$ e=\\frac{3}{2}\\quad \\text{or}\\quad e=\\frac{1}{3} $$\n\nSince for a hyperbola $e>1$, we take\n\n$$ e=\\frac{3}{2} $$\n\nNow the foci are $(3,5)$ and $(3,-4)$.\n\nThese lie on the vertical line $x=3$, so the transverse axis is vertical.\n\nThe distance between the foci is\n\n$$ |5-(-4)|=9 $$\n\nHence,\n\n$$ 2c=9 \\Rightarrow c=\\frac{9}{2} $$\n\nFor a hyperbola,\n\n$$ e=\\frac{c}{a} $$\n\nSo,\n\n$$ a=\\frac{c}{e} =\\frac{\\frac{9}{2}}{\\frac{3}{2}} =3 $$\n\nNow use the relation\n\n$$ c^2=a^2+b^2 $$\n\nThus,\n\n$$ b^2=c^2-a^2 =\\left(\\frac{9}{2}\\right)^2-3^2 =\\frac{81}{4}-9 =\\frac{81-36}{4} =\\frac{45}{4} $$\n\nLength of latus rectum of a hyperbola is\n\n$$ \\frac{2b^2}{a} $$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$ \\text{Length of latus rectum} =\\frac{2\\cdot \\frac{45}{4}}{3} =\\frac{45}{6} =\\frac{15}{2} $$\n\nHence, the correct answer is\n\n$$ \\boxed{\\frac{15}{2}} $$\n\nSo, Option C is correct.",
