      "s": "JEE Main 2026 (Online) 8th April Evening Shift. Correct option: B. Since the ellipse has its major axis along the $y$-axis, the denominator under $y^2$ must be bigger than the denominator under $x^2$.\n\nSo we need\n\n$$f(3a+15) > f\\left(a^2+7a+3\\right).$$\n\nGiven that $f$ is a strictly decreasing positive function, a bigger function value happens when the input is smaller. So,\n\n$$3a+15 Bring all terms to one side:\n\n$$a^2+7a+3-3a-15>0$$\n\n$$a^2+4a-12>0.$$\n\nComplete the square:\n\n$$a^2+4a-12=(a+2)^2-16.$$\n\nSo the inequality becomes\n\n$$(a+2)^2-16>0 \\;\\Rightarrow\\; (a+2)^2>16.$$\n\nTaking square roots,\n\n$$|a+2|>4 \\;\\Rightarrow\\; a+2>4 \\text{ or } a+2 So,\n\n$$a>2 \\text{ or } a That means the allowed values are\n\n$$a \\in \\mathbf{R}-[-6,2].$$\n\nHence, $\\alpha=-6$ and $\\beta=2$. Therefore,\n\n$$\\alpha^2+\\beta^2=(-6)^2+(2)^2=36+4=40.$$",
