      "q": "Let the point P be the vertex of the parabola $y=x^2-6 x+12$. If a line passing through the point P intersects the circle $x^2+y^2-2 x-4 y+3=0$ at the points R and S , then the maximum value of $(\\mathrm{PR}+\\mathrm{PS})^2$ is :",
      "qHtml": "<p>Let the point P be the vertex of the parabola $y=x^2-6 x+12$. If a line passing through the point P intersects the circle $x^2+y^2-2 x-4 y+3=0$ at the points R and S , then the maximum value of $(\\mathrm{PR}+\\mathrm{PS})^2$ is :</p>",
