      "s": "JEE Main 2026 (Online) 5th April Evening Shift. Correct option: A. The given variable $X$ takes values\n\n$$ 0,0,2,6,12,20,\\ldots,n(n-1) $$\n\nwith corresponding frequencies\n\n$$ {}^nC_0,{}^nC_1,{}^nC_2,{}^nC_3,{}^nC_4,{}^nC_5,\\ldots,{}^nC_n $$\n\nWe notice that the values of $X$ follow the pattern\n\n$$ X=r(r-1), \\quad r=0,1,2,\\ldots,n $$\n\nand the corresponding frequency is\n\n$$ {}^nC_r $$\n\nSo this is a discrete frequency distribution with:\n\nvariate value $x_r=r(r-1)$\n\nfrequency $f_r={}^nC_r$\n\nStep 1: Use the formula for mean\n\nMean is given by\n\n$$ \\bar X=\\frac{\\sum f_r x_r}{\\sum f_r} $$\n\nSo,\n\n$$ \\bar X=\\frac{\\sum_{r=0}^n {}^nC_r \\, r(r-1)}{\\sum_{r=0}^n {}^nC_r} $$\n\nGiven mean $=60$, so\n\n$$ \\frac{\\sum_{r=0}^n {}^nC_r \\, r(r-1)}{\\sum_{r=0}^n {}^nC_r}=60 $$\n\nNow use standard binomial identities:\n\n$$ \\sum_{r=0}^n {}^nC_r = 2^n $$\n\nand\n\n$$ \\sum_{r=0}^n r(r-1)\\,{}^nC_r = n(n-1)2^{n-2} $$\n\nHence,\n\n$$ \\bar X=\\frac{n(n-1)2^{n-2}}{2^n} =\\frac{n(n-1)}{4} $$\n\nGiven this is $60$:\n\n$$ \\frac{n(n-1)}{4}=60 $$\n\n$$ n(n-1)=240 $$\n\n$$ n^2-n-240=0 $$\n\n$$ (n-16)(n+15)=0 $$\n\nSo,\n\n$$ n=16 $$\n\nStep 2: Write the values and frequencies for $n=16$\n\nNow total frequency is\n\n$$ N=\\sum_{r=0}^{16} {}^{16}C_r = 2^{16}=65536 $$\n\nTo find the median, we need the value of $X$ whose cumulative frequency just exceeds $\\dfrac{N}{2}$.\n\n$$ \\frac{N}{2}=32768 $$\n\nNow frequencies are:\n\n$$ {}^{16}C_0,{}^{16}C_1,{}^{16}C_2,\\ldots,{}^{16}C_{16} $$\n\nUsing symmetry of binomial coefficients:\n\n$$ {}^{16}C_0+{}^{16}C_1+\\cdots+{}^{16}C_7 = \\frac{1}{2}\\left(2^{16}-{}^{16}C_8\\right) $$\n\nSince\n\n$$ {}^{16}C_8=12870 $$\n\nwe get\n\n$$ {}^{16}C_0+{}^{16}C_1+\\cdots+{}^{16}C_7 = \\frac{65536-12870}{2} =26333 $$\n\nNow add ${}^{16}C_8$:\n\n$$ 26333+12870=39203 $$\n\nSo the cumulative frequency crosses $32768$ at $r=8$.\n\nHence the median corresponds to\n\n$$ X=8(8-1)=56 $$\n\nFinal Answer\n\n$$ \\boxed{56} $$\n\nSo, the correct option is A .",
