      "a": 3,
      "s": "JEE Main 2026 (Online) 4th April Morning Shift. Correct option: D. Given\n\n$$ A=\\begin{bmatrix} 1 & 1 & 2\\\\ -2 & 0 & 1\\\\ 1 & 3 & 5 \\end{bmatrix} $$\n\nWe have to find the sum of all elements of\n\n$$ \\operatorname{adj}\\left(\\operatorname{adj}\\left(2(\\operatorname{adj}A)^{-1}\\right)\\right) $$\n\n$$ \\det A= 1\\begin{vmatrix} 0 & 1\\\\ 3 & 5 \\end{vmatrix} -1\\begin{vmatrix} -2 & 1\\\\ 1 & 5 \\end{vmatrix} +2\\begin{vmatrix} -2 & 0\\\\ 1 & 3 \\end{vmatrix} $$\n\n$$ =1(0\\cdot 5-1\\cdot 3)-1((-2)\\cdot 5-1\\cdot 1)+2((-2)\\cdot 3-0\\cdot 1) $$\n\n$$ =-3-(-11)+2(-6) $$\n\n$$ =-3+11-12=-4 $$\n\nSo,\n\n$$ \\det A=-4 $$\n\nFor an $n\\times n$ matrix,\n\n$$ \\det(\\operatorname{adj}A)=(\\det A)^{n-1} $$\n\nSince $A$ is $3\\times 3$,\n\n$$ \\det(\\operatorname{adj}A)=(\\det A)^2=(-4)^2=16 $$\n\nNow let\n\n$$ B=2(\\operatorname{adj}A)^{-1} $$\n\nWe need $\\operatorname{adj}(\\operatorname{adj}B)$.\n\nFor a $3\\times 3$ matrix, the property is:\n\n$$ \\operatorname{adj}(\\operatorname{adj}B)=(\\det B)\\,B $$\n\nSince\n\n$$ B=2(\\operatorname{adj}A)^{-1} $$\n\nand for a $3\\times 3$ matrix,\n\n$$ \\det(2M)=2^3\\det(M)=8\\det(M) $$\n\ntherefore,\n\n$$ \\det B=8\\det\\left((\\operatorname{adj}A)^{-1}\\right) $$\n\nAlso,\n\n$$ \\det\\left((\\operatorname{adj}A)^{-1}\\right)=\\frac{1}{\\det(\\operatorname{adj}A)}=\\frac{1}{16} $$\n\nHence,\n\n$$ \\det B=8\\cdot \\frac{1}{16}=\\frac{1}{2} $$\n\nSo,\n\n$$ \\operatorname{adj}(\\operatorname{adj}B)=(\\det B)B=\\frac12\\,B $$\n\nBut\n\n$$ B=2(\\operatorname{adj}A)^{-1} $$\n\nThus,\n\n$$ \\operatorname{adj}(\\operatorname{adj}B)=\\frac12 \\cdot 2(\\operatorname{adj}A)^{-1}=(\\operatorname{adj}A)^{-1} $$\n\nSo the required matrix is simply\n\n$$ (\\operatorname{adj}A)^{-1} $$\n\nWe know,\n\n$$ \\operatorname{adj}A=(\\det A)A^{-1} $$\n\nHence,\n\n$$ (\\operatorname{adj}A)^{-1}=\\frac{1}{\\det A}A $$\n\nSince $\\det A=-4$,\n\n$$ (\\operatorname{adj}A)^{-1}=\\frac{1}{-4}A=-\\frac14 A $$\n\nTherefore the required matrix is\n\n$$ -\\frac14 A $$\n\nFirst find the sum of elements of $A$:\n\n$$ 1+1+2-2+0+1+1+3+5=12 $$\n\nTherefore sum of elements of $-\\frac14 A$ is\n\n$$ -\\frac14 \\cdot 12=-3 $$\n\nFinal Answer\n\n$$ \\boxed{-3} $$\n\nSo, the correct option is D .",
