      "s": "JEE Main 2026 (Online) 6th April Evening Shift. Correct option: C. Given\n\n$$ \\vec{a} = 2\\hat{i} + 3\\hat{j} + 3\\hat{k}, \\qquad \\vec{b} = 6\\hat{i} + 3\\hat{j} + 3\\hat{k} $$\n\nWe need the square of the area of the triangle whose adjacent sides are\n\n$$ 2\\vec{a} + 3\\vec{b} \\quad \\text{and} \\quad \\vec{a} - \\vec{b} $$\n\nFor two adjacent sides $\\vec{u}$ and $\\vec{v}$, area of triangle is\n\n$$ \\frac{1}{2} |\\vec{u} \\times \\vec{v}| $$\n\nSo, square of the area is\n\n$$ \\left( \\frac{1}{2} |\\vec{u} \\times \\vec{v}| \\right)^2 = \\frac{1}{4} |\\vec{u} \\times \\vec{v}|^2 $$\n\nLet\n\n$$ \\vec{u} = 2\\vec{a} + 3\\vec{b}, \\qquad \\vec{v} = \\vec{a} - \\vec{b} $$\n\nFirst find $\\vec{u}$:\n\n$$ 2\\vec{a} = 2(2\\hat{i}+3\\hat{j}+3\\hat{k}) = 4\\hat{i}+6\\hat{j}+6\\hat{k} $$\n\n$$ 3\\vec{b} = 3(6\\hat{i}+3\\hat{j}+3\\hat{k}) = 18\\hat{i}+9\\hat{j}+9\\hat{k} $$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$ \\vec{u} = 2\\vec{a}+3\\vec{b} = 22\\hat{i}+15\\hat{j}+15\\hat{k} $$\n\nNow find $\\vec{v}$:\n\n$$ \\vec{v} = \\vec{a}-\\vec{b} = (2-6)\\hat{i} + (3-3)\\hat{j} + (3-3)\\hat{k} = -4\\hat{i} $$\n\nNow compute $\\vec{u} \\times \\vec{v}$:\n\n$$ \\vec{u} \\times \\vec{v} = \\begin{vmatrix} \\hat{i} & \\hat{j} & \\hat{k} \\\\ 22 & 15 & 15 \\\\ -4 & 0 & 0 \\end{vmatrix} $$\n\nExpanding,\n\n$$ \\vec{u} \\times \\vec{v} = \\hat{i}(15\\cdot 0 - 15\\cdot 0) - \\hat{j}(22\\cdot 0 - 15\\cdot (-4)) + \\hat{k}(22\\cdot 0 - 15\\cdot (-4)) $$\n\n$$ = 0\\hat{i} - 60\\hat{j} + 60\\hat{k} $$\n\nSo,\n\n$$ |\\vec{u} \\times \\vec{v}|^2 = 0^2 + (-60)^2 + 60^2 = 3600 + 3600 = 7200 $$\n\nHence square of the area of the triangle is\n\n$$ \\frac{1}{4} \\times 7200 = 1800 $$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is\n\n$$ \\boxed{1800} $$\n\nSo, Option C is correct.",
