      "qHtml": "<p>Two adjacent sides of a parallelogram PQRS are given by $\\overrightarrow{PQ} = \\hat{j} + \\hat{k}$ and $\\overrightarrow{PS} = \\hat{i} - \\hat{j}$. If the side PS is rotated about the point P by an acute angle $\\alpha$ in the plane of the parallelogram so that it becomes perpendicular to the side PQ, then $\\sin^2\\left(\\frac{5\\alpha}{2}\\right) - \\sin^2\\left(\\frac{\\alpha}{2}\\right)$ is equal to:</p>",
