      "s": "JEE Main 2024 (Online) 1st February Evening Shift. Correct option: D. $f(x)=\\left\\{\\begin{array}{l}x-1, x \\text { is even, } \\\\ 2 x, \\quad x \\text { is odd, }\\end{array} x \\in \\mathbf{N}\\right.$\n\nLet $a$ is odd\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n& \\Rightarrow f(a)=2 a \\\\\\\\\n& \\Rightarrow f(f(a))=2 a-1 \\\\\\\\\n& \\Rightarrow f(f(f(a)))=2(2 a-1)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$2(2 a-1)=21$ Not possible for any $a \\in N$\n\nLet $a$ is even\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n& \\Rightarrow f(a)=a-1 \\\\\\\\\n& \\Rightarrow f(f(a))=2(a-1) \\\\\\\\\n& \\Rightarrow f(f(f(a)))=2(a-1)-1=2 a-3 \\\\\\\\\n& 2 a-3=21 \\quad \\Rightarrow a=12\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n& \\lim _{x \\rightarrow 12^{-}}\\left(\\frac{|x|^3}{2}-\\left[\\frac{x}{12}\\right]\\right) \\\\\\\\\n& =\\lim _{x \\rightarrow 12^{-}} \\frac{|x|^3}{12}-\\lim _{x \\rightarrow 12^{-}}\\left[\\frac{x}{12}\\right] \\\\\\\\\n& =144-0=144 .\n\\end{aligned}\n$$",
