      "a": 1,
      "s": "JEE Main 2026 (Online) 5th April Evening Shift. Correct option: B. Let us define a new function $h(x)$ taking the difference between $f(x)$ and $g(x)$.\n\n$$h(x) = f(x) - g(x)$$\n\nDifferentiating this function twice with respect to $x$, we get:\n\n$$h^{\\prime \\prime}(x) = f^{\\prime \\prime}(x) - g^{\\prime \\prime}(x)$$\n\nWe are given that $f^{\\prime \\prime}(x) = g^{\\prime \\prime}(x)$ for all $x \\in \\mathbf{R}$. Therefore, their difference is zero:\n\n$$h^{\\prime \\prime}(x) = 0$$\n\nNow, let us integrate both sides with respect to $x$ to find $h^{\\prime}(x)$:\n\n$$h^{\\prime}(x) = \\int 0 \\,dx = c_1$$\n\nwhere $c_1$ is a constant of integration.\n\nWe are given the values of the first derivatives at $x = 1$. Let us simplify them:\n\n$$f^{\\prime}(1) = 4$$\n\n$$2g^{\\prime}(1) = 4 \\implies g^{\\prime}(1) = 2$$\n\nUsing these values, we can find the exact value of $h^{\\prime}(1)$:\n\n$$h^{\\prime}(1) = f^{\\prime}(1) - g^{\\prime}(1) = 4 - 2 = 2$$\n\nSince $h^{\\prime}(x) = c_1$ for all values of $x$, it follows that:\n\n$$c_1 = 2$$\n\nSubstituting this back, we get our first derivative equation:\n\n$$h^{\\prime}(x) = 2$$\n\nNext, we need the original function $h(x)$. We find it by integrating $h^{\\prime}(x)$ with respect to $x$:\n\n$$h(x) = \\int 2 \\,dx = 2x + c_2$$\n\nwhere $c_2$ is another constant of integration.\n\nWe are given the values of the functions at $x = 2$. Let us simplify these values as well:\n\n$$g(2) = 9$$\n\n$$3f(2) = 9 \\implies f(2) = 3$$\n\nUsing these values, we can find the value of $h(2)$:\n\n$$h(2) = f(2) - g(2) = 3 - 9 = -6$$\n\nNow, substitute $x = 2$ and $h(2) = -6$ into our integrated equation for $h(x)$:\n\n$$h(2) = 2(2) + c_2$$\n\n$$-6 = 4 + c_2$$\n\n$$c_2 = -6 - 4$$\n\n$$c_2 = -10$$\n\nSubstituting the value of $c_2$ back into the equation for $h(x)$, we have the completed function rule:\n\n$$h(x) = 2x - 10$$\n\nThe question asks for the value of $f(25) - g(25)$, which is represented directly by $h(25)$. Let us substitute $x = 25$ into our function $h(x)$:\n\n$$h(25) = 2(25) - 10$$\n\n$$h(25) = 50 - 10$$\n\n$$h(25) = 40$$\n\nTherefore, $f(25) - g(25) = 40$.\n\nThe correct answer is Option B.",
