      "s": "JEE Main 2026 (Online) 2nd April Morning Shift. Correct option: B. $\\therefore$ Denominator $=0$ at $x=2$\n\n$\\Rightarrow$ Numerator $=0$ at $x=2$\n\n$$2^3-5(2)^2+a(2)+b=0$$\n\n$$\\Rightarrow 2a+b=12 \\quad \\ldots (1)$$\n\n$$\\therefore \\; m=\\lim\\limits_{x\\rightarrow 2}\\frac{\\dfrac{\\sin\\left(x^3-5x^2+ax+b\\right)}{x^3-5x^2+ax+b}\\cdot \\left(x^3-5x^2+ax+b\\right)}{\\left(\\dfrac{x-1-1}{\\sqrt{x-1}+1}\\right)\\cdot \\dfrac{\\log_e\\left(1+(x-2)\\right)}{x-2}\\cdot (x-2)}$$\n\n$$\\Rightarrow m=\\lim\\limits_{x\\rightarrow 2} 2\\left(\\frac{x^3-5x^2+ax+b}{(x-2)^2}\\right)$$\n\n$$\\Rightarrow m=\\lim\\limits_{x\\rightarrow 2} 2\\left(\\frac{3x^2-10x+a}{2(x-2)}\\right)$$\n\n$\\therefore$ Denominator $=0$ at $x=2$\n\n$\\Rightarrow$ Numerator $=0$ at $x=2$\n\n$$\\Rightarrow 3(2)^2-10(2)+a=0 \\rightarrow a=8$$\n\nput $a=8$ in (1), we get $b=-4$\n\n$$\\therefore \\; m=\\lim\\limits_{x\\rightarrow 2} 2\\left(\\frac{6x-10}{2}\\right) \\rightarrow m=2$$\n\n$\\therefore \\; a+b+m=6$",
      "source": "JEE Main 2026 (Online) 2nd April Morning Shift | Continuity and Differentiability | mnrj3xt1",
