      "q": "Let $f: \\mathbb{R} \\rightarrow \\mathbb{R}$ be a differentiable function such that $f\\left(\\frac{x+y}{3}\\right)=\\frac{f(x)+f(y)}{3}$ for all $x, y \\in \\mathbb{R}$, and $f^{\\prime}(0)=3$. Then the minimum value of the function $g(x)=3+e^x f(x)$, is:",
      "qHtml": "<p>Let $f: \\mathbb{R} \\rightarrow \\mathbb{R}$ be a differentiable function such that $f\\left(\\frac{x+y}{3}\\right)=\\frac{f(x)+f(y)}{3}$ for all $x, y \\in \\mathbb{R}$, and $f^{\\prime}(0)=3$. Then the minimum value of the function $g(x)=3+e^x f(x)$, is:</p>",
