      "q": "Consider the following three statements for the function $f:(0, \\infty) \\rightarrow \\mathbb{R}$ defined by $f(x)=\\left|\\log _e x\\right|-|x-1|$ :\n\n(I) $f$ is differentiable at all $x>0$.\n\n(II) $f$ is increasing in $(0,1)$.\n\n(III) $f$ is decreasing in $(1, \\infty)$.\n\nThen.",
      "qHtml": "<p>Consider the following three statements for the function $f:(0, \\infty) \\rightarrow \\mathbb{R}$ defined by $f(x)=\\left|\\log _e x\\right|-|x-1|$ :</p>\n<p>(I) $f$ is differentiable at all $x>0$.</p>\n<p>(II) $f$ is increasing in $(0,1)$.</p>\n<p>(III) $f$ is decreasing in $(1, \\infty)$.</p>\n<p>Then.</p>",
