      "q": "If $\\alpha=1$ and $\\beta=1+i \\sqrt{2}$, where $i=\\sqrt{-1}$ are two roots of the equation\n\n$x^3+a x^2+b x+c=0, a, b, \\in \\mathbb{R}$, then $\\int_{-1}^1\\left(x^3+a x^2+b x+c\\right) d x$ is equal to:",
      "qHtml": "<p>If $\\alpha=1$ and $\\beta=1+i \\sqrt{2}$, where $i=\\sqrt{-1}$ are two roots of the equation</p>\n<p>$x^3+a x^2+b x+c=0, a, b, \\in \\mathbb{R}$, then $\\int_{-1}^1\\left(x^3+a x^2+b x+c\\right) d x$ is equal to:</p>",
