      "a": 0,
      "s": "JEE Main 2026 (Online) 2nd April Evening Shift. Correct option: A. The least count is the smallest distance the screw moves when the circular scale is rotated by one division. It is defined as:\n\n$$ \\text { Least Count }=\\frac{\\text { Pitch }}{\\text { Number of divisions on circular scale }} $$\n\nThe pitch is linear distance moved in one complete rotation. The pitch of screw gauge is given as 0.1 mm and there are 100 divisions:\n\nSo, the least count is $\\mathrm{LC}=\\frac{0.1 \\mathrm{~mm}}{100}=0.001 \\mathrm{~mm}$\n\nWhen the studs are in contact, the 5th division of the circular scale coincides with the reference line. Since the zero of the circular scale has passed the reference line, the error is positive.\n\nZero Error $=+($ Coinciding division $\\times$ LC $)$\n\n$$\\Rightarrow $$ Zero Error $=+(5 \\times 0.001 \\mathrm{~mm})=+0.005 \\mathrm{~mm}$\n\nThe total observed reading is the sum of the Main Scale Reading (MSR) and the Circular Scale Reading (CSR).\n\n$\\mathrm{MSR}=5 \\mathrm{~mm}$\n\nCSR $=$ Coinciding circular division × LC $=50 \\times 0.001 \\mathrm{~mm}=0.05 \\mathrm{~mm}$\n\nSo, observed reading $=5 \\mathrm{~mm}+0.05 \\mathrm{~mm}=5.05 \\mathrm{~mm}$\n\nThe true diameter is obtained by subtracting the zero error from the observed reading:\n\nSo, the true diameter $=$ Observed Reading - Zero Error\n\nTrue Diameter $=5.05 \\mathrm{~mm}-0.005 \\mathrm{~mm}=5.045 \\mathrm{~mm}$\n\nTherefore, the correct option is (A).",
      "source": "JEE Main 2026 (Online) 2nd April Evening Shift | Units and Dimensions | mnrqtn1n",
