      "a": 1,
      "s": "JEE Main 2026 (Online) 2nd April Morning Shift. Correct option: B. The expression given is $\\frac{1}{2}\\varepsilon_0 E^2$, which represents the energy density ($U_d$) of an electric field in a vacuum.\n\nEnergy density is defined as the energy stored per unit volume.\n\n$$U_d = \\frac{\\text{Energy }(U)}{\\text{Volume }(V)}$$\n\nEnergy is equivalent to work done, which is Force $\\times$ Displacement.\n\nThe dimensions of force is $[F] = [ma] = [M\\ L\\ T^{-2}]$\n\nSo, the dimensions of energy is $[U] = [M\\ L\\ T^{-2}] \\times [L] = [M\\ L^2 T^{-2}]$\n\nThe dimensions of volume is $[V] = [L] \\times [L] \\times [L] = [L^3]$\n\nSince energy density is $\\frac{U}{V}$, its dimensions are:\n\n$$[U_d] = \\frac{[M\\ L^2 T^{-2}]}{[L^3]} = [M\\ L^{-1} T^{-2}]$$\n\nThe dimensional formula of energy density due to electric field is is $M^a L^b T^c$.\n\nBy comparing this with derived dimensional formula $[M^1 L^{-1} T^{-2}]$, we get:\n\n$$a = 1,\\ b = -1,\\ c = -2$$\n\nSo, the value of $2a - b + c = 2(1) - (-1) + (-2) = 2 + 1 - 2 = 1$\n\nTherefore, the value of $2a - b + c$ is 1. Thus, the correct options is (B).",
      "source": "JEE Main 2026 (Online) 2nd April Morning Shift | Units and Dimensions | mnrjpxca",
      "pyq": true,
