      "q": "The energy of a system is given as $\\mathrm{E}(\\mathrm{t})=\\alpha^3 \\mathrm{e}^{-\\beta t}$, where t is the time and $\\beta=0.3 \\mathrm{~s}^{-1}$. The errors in the measurement of $\\alpha$ and $t$ are $1.2 \\%$ and $1.6 \\%$, respectively. At $t=5 \\mathrm{~s}$, maximum percentage error in the energy is :",
      "qHtml": "The energy of a system is given as $\\mathrm{E}(\\mathrm{t})=\\alpha^3 \\mathrm{e}^{-\\beta t}$, where t is the time and $\\beta=0.3 \\mathrm{~s}^{-1}$. The errors in the measurement of $\\alpha$ and $t$ are $1.2 \\%$ and $1.6 \\%$, respectively. At $t=5 \\mathrm{~s}$, maximum percentage error in the energy is :",
