      "a": 0,
      "s": "JEE Main 2026 (Online) 5th April Morning Shift. Correct option: A. Let the acceleration of wedge along horizontal is $\\mathrm{a}_{\\mathrm{w}}$ and whole system will accelerate to the right.\n\n[Diagram: JEE Main 2026 (Online) 5th April Morning Shift Physics - Laws of Motion Question 3 English Explanation 1]\n\nTotal mass of the system is $\\mathrm{M}=\\mathrm{m}_{\\mathrm{X}}+\\mathrm{m}_{\\mathrm{Y}}=(10+2) \\mathrm{kg}=12 \\mathrm{~kg}$\n\nThe applied force along horizontal is $\\mathrm{f}=24 \\mathrm{~N}$\n\nUsing Newton's second law of motion for the system, acceleration of wedge,\n\n$$ \\mathrm{a}_{\\mathrm{w}}=\\frac{\\mathrm{f}}{\\mathrm{M}}=\\frac{24}{12}=2 \\mathrm{~m} / \\mathrm{s}^2 $$\n\nThe block X will be at rest along normal to the incline when motion is observed with respect to wedge Y . So, in the non-inertial frame of the wedge, a pseudo-force $\\left(\\mathrm{ma}_{\\mathrm{w}}\\right)$ acts on block X toward the left. Components of forces acting along the incline for block X :\n\n[Diagram: JEE Main 2026 (Online) 5th April Morning Shift Physics - Laws of Motion Question 3 English Explanation 2]\n\nComponent of gravity is $\\mathrm{mg} \\sin \\left(37^{\\circ}\\right)$ (down the incline).\n\nComponent of pseudo-force is $\\mathrm{ma}_{\\mathrm{w}} \\cos \\left(37^{\\circ}\\right)$ (up the incline)\n\nSo, the acceleration of block X down the incline with relative to wedge is;\n\n$$ a_{\\mathrm{X}}=g \\sin \\left(37^{\\circ}\\right)-a_{\\mathrm{w}} \\cos \\left(37^{\\circ}\\right) $$\n\n$$\\Rightarrow $$ $a_{\\mathrm{X}}=(10)\\left(\\frac{3}{5}\\right)-(2)\\left(\\frac{4}{5}\\right)$\n\n$$\\Rightarrow $$ $$ \\mathrm{a}_{\\mathrm{x}}=6-1.6=4.4 \\mathrm{~m} / \\mathrm{s}^2 $$\n\nDistance to slide along the incline is $\\mathrm{s}=8.8 \\mathrm{~m}$.\n\nInitial relative velocity of block X is $\\mathrm{u}=0$.\n\nUsing equation of motion;\n\n$$ \\mathrm{s}=\\mathrm{ut}+\\frac{1}{2} \\mathrm{a}_{\\mathrm{X}} \\mathrm{t}^2 $$\n\n$$\\Rightarrow $$ $8.8=0+\\frac{1}{2}(4.4) \\mathrm{t}^2$\n\n$$\\Rightarrow $$ $\\mathrm{t}^2=\\frac{8.8 \\times 2}{4.4}$\n\n$$\\Rightarrow $$ $$ t^2=4 \\Rightarrow t=2 s $$\n\nTherefore, the block X will take 2 s to slide 8.8 m down the inline of wedge Y .\n\nHence, the correct option is (A).",
      "source": "JEE Main 2026 (Online) 5th April Morning Shift | Laws of Motion | mnswhtdg",
