      "qHtml": "<img class=\"quiz-question-image\" src=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/image/1l91dzva8/32a61b53-56bd-4d0a-b3d8-bf03d4828714/152ee910-47d7-11ed-9a0e-8f7a98995d79/file-1l91dzva9.png\" alt=\"JEE Main 2015 (Offline) Physics - Laws of Motion Question 130 English\" loading=\"lazy\"><br>Given in the figure are two blocks $$A$$ and $$B$$ of weight 20 N and 100 N, respectively. These are being pressed against a wall by a force $$F$$ as shown. If the coefficient of friction between the blocks is 0.1 and between block $$B$$ and the wall is 0.15, the frictional force applied by the wall on block $$B$$ is :",
