      "a": 0,
      "s": "JEE Main 2026 (Online) 5th April Evening Shift. Correct option: A. When the block is at rest on the incline, the forces acting on it are :\n\n[Diagram: JEE Main 2026 (Online) 5th April Evening Shift Physics - Work Power & Energy Question 4 English Explanation]\n\n$\\mathrm{F}_{\\mathrm{g}}=\\mathrm{mg}$ is weight acting vertically downward.\n\n$\\mathrm{N}=$ Normal force acting perpendicular to the incline.\n\n$\\mathrm{f}_{\\mathrm{s}}=$ Static friction acting up the incline, preventing the block from sliding down.\n\nSince the block is at rest relative to the incline, the frictional force must balance the component of gravity acting down the slope :\n\n$$ \\mathrm{f}_{\\mathrm{s}}=\\mathrm{mg} \\sin \\theta $$\n\nThe mass of block is $\\mathrm{m}=1 \\mathrm{~kg}$, acceleration due to gravity is $\\mathrm{g}=10 \\mathrm{~m} / \\mathrm{s}^2$ and $\\theta=30^{\\circ}$\n\nSo, value of static friction is\n\n$$ \\mathrm{f}_{\\mathrm{s}}=1 \\times 10 \\times \\sin 30^{\\circ}=10 \\times 0.5=5 \\mathrm{~N} $$\n\nThe friction force is 5 N directed up along the incline.\n\nAs the entire assembly moves vertically upward with a constant velocity $\\mathrm{v}=4 \\mathrm{~m} / \\mathrm{s}$, so in time $\\mathrm{t}=2 \\mathrm{~s}$, the vertical displacement $S$ is:\n\n$$ S=v \\times t=4 \\times 2=8 \\mathrm{~m} $$\n\nWork done is defined as $W=\\vec{F} \\cdot \\vec{d}=F d \\cos \\phi$, where $\\phi$ is the angle between the force and the displacement.\n\nThe angle between the friction force and the vertical is $90^{\\circ}-30^{\\circ}=60^{\\circ}=\\phi$.\n\nSo, work done by frictional force is,\n\n$$ \\mathrm{W}=\\mathrm{f}_{\\mathrm{s}} \\times \\mathrm{S} \\times \\cos 60^{\\circ} $$\n\n$$\\Rightarrow $$ $\\mathrm{W}=5 \\times 8 \\times 0.5 \\mathrm{~J}$\n\n$$\\Rightarrow $$ $$ \\mathrm{W}=5 \\times 4=20 \\mathrm{~J} $$\n\nTherefore, the work done by the frictional force is 20 J .\n\nHence, the correct option is (A).",
