      "a": 0,
      "s": "JEE Main 2026 (Online) 21st January Morning Shift. Correct option: A. The force (F) acting on a particle is defined as the negative gradient of its potential energy (V) with respect to position (x) :\n\n$$ \\mathrm{F}=-\\frac{\\mathrm{dV}}{\\mathrm{dx}} $$\n\nHere, $\\frac{d V}{d x}$ is the slope of the $V$ versus $x$ graph. So, the magnitude of the force $(|F|)$ is the absolute value of the slope in each region :\n\n$$ |\\mathrm{F}|=\\mid \\text { slope of the } \\mathrm{V}-\\mathrm{x} \\text { graph } \\mid $$\n\nUsing the formula of slope\n\n$$ \\text { Slope }=m=\\frac{V_2-V_1}{x_2-x_1} $$\n\nFor region AB (from $\\mathrm{x}=0$ to $\\mathrm{x}=1$ ) :\n\nPoints are ( 0,0 ) and ( 1,1 )\n\n$$ \\left|\\mathrm{F}_{\\mathrm{AB}}\\right|=\\left|\\frac{1-0}{1-0}\\right|=1 \\text { unit } $$\n\nFor region BC (from $\\mathrm{x}=1$ to $\\mathrm{x}=2$ ) :\n\nPoints are $(1,1)$ and $(2,4)$\n\n$$ \\left|\\mathrm{F}_{\\mathrm{BC}}\\right|=\\left|\\frac{4-1}{2-1}\\right|=3 \\text { unit } $$\n\nFor region CD (from $\\mathrm{x}=2$ to $\\mathrm{x}=4$ ) :\n\nPoints are (2,4) and (4,4)\n\n$$ \\left|\\mathrm{F}_{\\mathrm{CD}}\\right|=\\left|\\frac{4-4}{4-2}\\right|=0 \\text { unit } $$\n\nFor region DE (from $\\mathrm{x}=4$ to $\\mathrm{x}=6$ ):\n\nPoints are $(4,4)$ and $(6,3)$\n\n$$ \\left|\\mathrm{F}_{\\mathrm{DE}}\\right|=\\left|\\frac{3-4}{6-4}\\right|=0.5 \\text { unit } $$\n\nThe descending order of the magnitude of forces is,\n\n$$ 3>1>0.5>0 \\Rightarrow \\mathrm{~F}_{\\mathrm{BC}}>\\mathrm{F}_{\\mathrm{AB}}>\\mathrm{F}_{\\mathrm{DE}}>\\mathrm{F}_{\\mathrm{CD}} $$\n\nTherefore, region $B C$ has the greatest slope and thus the strongest force, while region CD has no slope and zero force.\n\nHence, the correct option is (A).",
      "source": "JEE Main 2026 (Online) 21st January Morning Shift | Work, Power and Energy | ml89h6ux",
      "pyq": true,
