      "a": 1,
      "s": "JEE Main 2026 (Online) 6th April Morning Shift. Correct option: B. Since the cube is accelerating at $\\mathrm{a}=\\frac{\\mathrm{g}}{2}$ to the right, when analysing the blocks from the cube's non-inertial frame, we must apply a pseudo-force ( $\\mathrm{F}_{\\mathrm{p}}=\\mathrm{m} \\times \\mathrm{a}$ ) on both blocks in the opposite direction to the acceleration of block S.\n\n[Diagram: JEE Main 2026 (Online) 6th April Morning Shift Physics - Laws of Motion Question 1 English Explanation]\n\nFor block P (Mass $\\mathrm{m}_{\\mathrm{P}}=2 \\mathrm{~kg}$ )\n\nAlong horizontal the tension (T) in the thread pulls it to the right. The pseudo-force ( $\\mathrm{m}_{\\mathrm{P}} \\cdot \\mathrm{a}$ ) pulls it to the left. Along vertical direction gravity ( $\\mathrm{m}_{\\mathrm{P}} \\mathrm{g}$ ) acts downward and normal force ( $\\mathrm{N}_{\\mathrm{P}}$ ) from the top surface acts upward. Since the block is stationary relative to the cube :\n\n$$ \\mathrm{T}=\\mathrm{m}_{\\mathrm{P}} \\cdot \\mathrm{a}=\\mathrm{m}_{\\mathrm{P}} \\cdot \\frac{\\mathrm{~g}}{2} $$\n\n$$\\Rightarrow $$ $$ \\mathrm{T}=2 \\times \\frac{10}{2}=10 \\mathrm{~N} $$\n\nFor block Q (Mass $\\mathrm{m}_{\\mathrm{Q}}=1.5 \\mathrm{~kg}$ )\n\nAlong horizontal direction the cube pushes against the block with a normal force $\\left(\\mathrm{N}_{\\mathrm{Q}}\\right)$ to the right. The pseudoforce $\\left(\\mathrm{m}_{\\mathrm{Q}} \\cdot \\mathrm{a}\\right)$ acts to the left.\n\n$$ \\mathrm{N}_{\\mathrm{Q}}=\\mathrm{m}_{\\mathrm{Q}} \\cdot \\mathrm{a}=1.5 \\times \\frac{\\mathrm{g}}{2} $$\n\nAlong vertical direction, gravity ( $\\mathrm{m}_{\\mathrm{Q}} \\mathrm{g}$ ) acts downward.\n\n$$ \\mathrm{F}_{\\mathrm{gQ}}=1.5 \\times 10=15 \\mathrm{~N} $$\n\nTension (T) in the thread acts upward, $\\mathrm{T}=10 \\mathrm{~N}$ [as the string is massless and inextensible]\n\nFriction (f) acts upward to prevent the block from falling.\n\nFor equilibrium in the vertical direction:\n\n$$ \\mathrm{T}+\\mathrm{f}=\\mathrm{m}_{\\mathrm{Q}} \\mathrm{~g} $$\n\n$$\\Rightarrow $$ $$ 10+\\mathrm{f}=15 \\Rightarrow \\mathrm{f}=5 \\mathrm{~N} $$\n\nThe friction force is given by $\\mathrm{f}=\\mu \\mathrm{N}_{\\mathrm{Q}}$.\n\n$$ 5=\\mu \\times\\left(1.5 \\times \\frac{10}{2}\\right) $$\n\n$$\\Rightarrow $$ $5=\\mu \\times(1.5 \\times 5)$\n\n$$\\Rightarrow $$ $5=\\mu \\times 7.5$\n\n$$\\Rightarrow $$ $$ \\mu=\\frac{5}{7.5}=\\frac{2}{3} \\approx 0.67 $$\n\nTherefore, the value of coefficient of friction between the block Q and S is $\\mu=0.67$.\n\nThus, the correct option is (B).",
      "source": "JEE Main 2026 (Online) 6th April Morning Shift | Center of Mass, Momentum and Collision | mnswhy9a",
      "pyq": true,
      "exactPaperText": true,
      "pyqSourceSlug": "laws-of-motion"
