      "q": "A uniform circular disc of radius ' $\\mathrm{R}^{\\prime}$ and mass ' $\\mathrm{M}^{\\prime}$ is rotating about an axis perpendicular to its plane and passing through its centre. A small circular part of radius $R / 2$ is removed from the original disc as shown in the figure. Find the moment of inertia of the remaining part of the original disc about the axis as given above.\n\n[Diagram: JEE Main 2025 (Online) 22nd January Morning Shift Physics - Rotational Motion Question 50 English]",
      "qHtml": "<p>A uniform circular disc of radius ' $\\mathrm{R}^{\\prime}$ and mass ' $\\mathrm{M}^{\\prime}$ is rotating about an axis perpendicular to its plane and passing through its centre. A small circular part of radius $R / 2$ is removed from the original disc as shown in the figure. Find the moment of inertia of the remaining part of the original disc about the axis as given above.</p>\n<p><img class=\"quiz-question-image\" src=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/image/jaoe38c1m6qnsgoo/7758b425-b0e8-44d9-9b4b-31ea7c179344/1e45af80-e310-11ef-8161-69fc95b6cece/file-jaoe38c1m6qnsgop.png\" alt=\"JEE Main 2025 (Online) 22nd January Morning Shift Physics - Rotational Motion Question 50 English\" loading=\"lazy\"></p>",
