      "q": "Initially a satellite of 100 kg is in a circular orbit of radius $1.5 \\mathrm{R}_{\\mathrm{E}}$. This satellite can be moved to a circular orbit of radius $3 R_E$ by supplying $\\alpha \\times 10^6 \\mathrm{~J}$ of energy The value of $\\alpha$ is $\\_\\_\\_\\_$ .\n\n(Take Radius of Earth $R_E=6 \\times 10^6 \\mathrm{~m}$ and $\\mathrm{g}=10 \\mathrm{~m} / \\mathrm{s}^2$ )",
