      "oHtml": [
        "<p>$100 \\mathrm{~m} / \\mathrm{s}$</p>",
        "<p>$10 \\mathrm{~m} / \\mathrm{s}$</p>",
        "<p>$1000 \\mathrm{~m} / \\mathrm{s}$</p>",
        "<p>$15 \\times 10^2 \\mathrm{~m} / \\mathrm{s}$</p>"
      ],
      "a": 1,
      "s": "JEE Main 2026 (Online) 4th April Evening Shift. Correct option: B. For an incompressible fluid, the volume of fluid entering a pipe per unit time must equal the volume of fluid leaving the pipe per unit time.\n\nVolume Flow Rate (In) = Volume Flow Rate (Out)\n\n$$ A_1 v_1=A_2 v_2 $$\n\nWhere A is the area and v is the velocity of the fluid.\n\nThe area of hose is $\\mathrm{A}_1=30 \\mathrm{~cm}^2=30 \\times 10^{-4} \\mathrm{~m}^2$.\n\nThe speed in hose is $\\mathrm{v}_1=50 \\mathrm{~cm} / \\mathrm{s}=0.5 \\mathrm{~m} / \\mathrm{s}$.\n\nNumber of perforations is $\\mathrm{n}=10$.\n\nThe area of one perforation is $\\mathrm{a}=15 \\mathrm{~mm}^2=15 \\times\\left(10^{-3} \\mathrm{~m}\\right)^2=15 \\times 10^{-6} \\mathrm{~m}^2$\n\nSo, total area of exit is, $\\mathrm{A}_2=\\mathrm{n} \\times \\mathrm{a}=10 \\times 15 \\times 10^{-6}=150 \\times 10^{-6} \\mathrm{~m}^2$\n\nUsing the equation of continuity:\n\n$$ A_1 v_1=A_2 v_2 $$\n\n$$\\Rightarrow $$ $$ v_2=\\frac{A_1 v_1}{A_2} $$\n\nSubstituting the values :\n\n$$ v_2=\\frac{\\left(30 \\times 10^{-4}\\right) \\times 0.5}{150 \\times 10^{-6}} $$\n\n$$\\Rightarrow $$ $v_2=\\frac{15 \\times 10^{-4}}{150 \\times 10^{-6}}$\n\n$$\\Rightarrow $$ $$ \\mathrm{v}_2=10 \\mathrm{~m} / \\mathrm{s} $$\n\nTherefore, the speed at which the water flows out from each perforation is $10 \\mathrm{~m} / \\mathrm{s}$.\n\nThus, the correct option is (B).",
      "source": "JEE Main 2026 (Online) 4th April Evening Shift | Mechanical Properties of Solids | mnswhqqb",
