      "a": 1,
      "s": "JEE Main 2026 (Online) 5th April Evening Shift. Correct option: B. When 8 small drops of radius $r$ combine to form one large drop of radius $R$, the total volume remains constant.\n\nVolume of 8 small drops $=$ Volume of 1 large drop\n\n$$ 8 \\times\\left(\\frac{4}{3} \\pi r^3\\right)=\\frac{4}{3} \\pi R^3 $$\n\n$$\\Rightarrow $$ $8 r^3=R^3$\n\n$$ \\Rightarrow R=2 r $$\n\nThe surface energy of a single drop is $E=S A$ where $S$ is the surface tension and $A$ is the surface area.\n\nTotal initial area for 8 drops $=8 \\times\\left(4 \\pi \\mathrm{r}^2\\right)=32 \\pi \\mathrm{r}^2$.\n\nSo, total initial surface energy is $\\mathrm{U}_{\\mathrm{i}}=32 \\pi \\mathrm{r}^2 \\mathrm{~S}$\n\nThe final drop has radius $\\mathrm{R}=2 \\mathrm{r}$.\n\nSo, final surface area $=4 \\pi R^2=4 \\pi(2 r)^2=4 \\pi\\left(4 r^2\\right)=16 \\pi r^2$.\n\nSo, the final surface energy is $U_f=16 \\pi r^2 S$\n\nThe energy released is the decrease in surface energy :\n\n$$ \\Delta U=U_i-U_f $$\n\n$$\\Rightarrow $$ $\\Delta U=32 \\pi r^2 S-16 \\pi r^2 S$\n\n$$\\Rightarrow $$ $$ \\Delta U=16 \\pi r^2 S $$\n\nTherefore, the surface energy released in this process is $16 \\pi r^2 S$.\n\nHence, the correct option is (B).",
      "source": "JEE Main 2026 (Online) 5th April Evening Shift | Mechanical Properties of Fluids | mnswhvpz",
