      "q": "Rods $x$ and $y$ of equal dimensions but of different materials are joined as shown in figure. Temperatures of end points $A$ and $F$ are maintained at $100^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C}$ and $40^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C}$ respectively. Given the thermal conductivity of $\\operatorname{rod} x$ is three times of that of $\\operatorname{rod} y$, the temperature at junction points $B$ and $E$ are (close to):\n\n[Diagram: JEE Main 2026 (Online) 22nd January Morning Shift Physics - Heat and Thermodynamics Question 30 English]",
      "qHtml": "<p>Rods $x$ and $y$ of equal dimensions but of different materials are joined as shown in figure. Temperatures of end points $A$ and $F$ are maintained at $100^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C}$ and $40^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C}$ respectively. Given the thermal conductivity of $\\operatorname{rod} x$ is three times of that of $\\operatorname{rod} y$, the temperature at junction points $B$ and $E$ are (close to):</p><img class=\"quiz-question-image\" src=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/image/6y3zli1ml8u6shs/acc6c08c-4a51-424e-b46e-650de2447e66/467de310-023a-11f1-88dd-c7214e4b90e3/file-6y3zli1ml8u6sht.png\" alt=\"JEE Main 2026 (Online) 22nd January Morning Shift Physics - Heat and Thermodynamics Question 30 English\" loading=\"lazy\">",
