      "a": 2,
      "s": "JEE Main 2026 (Online) 4th April Evening Shift. Correct option: C. According to the kinetic theory of gases, the average translational kinetic energy ( $\\mathrm{K}_{\\text {avg }}$ ) of a gas molecule is directly proportional to its absolute temperature (T).\n\n$$ \\mathrm{K}_{\\mathrm{avg}}=\\frac{3}{2} \\mathrm{k}_{\\mathrm{B}} \\mathrm{~T} $$\n\nWhere $\\mathrm{k}_{\\mathrm{B}}$ is the Boltzmann constant.\n\nSo, the average kinetic energy depends only on the temperature and not on the mass of the molecule or the size/volume of the container.\n\nSince $\\mathrm{K}_{\\mathrm{avg}}$ is the same for both $\\mathrm{H}_2$ and $\\mathrm{O}_2$, their temperatures (T) must be identical.\n\nTherefore, Assertion A is true.\n\nThe root mean square (r. m. s.) speed ( $\\mathrm{v}_{\\text {rms }}$ ) of a gas molecule is given by the formula:\n\n$$ v_{r m s}=\\sqrt{\\frac{3 R T}{M}} $$\n\nWhere R is the universal gas constant, T is the absolute temperature, and M is the molar mass of the gas.\n\nAt the same temperature (T), $\\mathrm{v}_{\\mathrm{rms}}$ is inversely proportional to the square root of the molar mass (M).\n\nSince the molar mass of $\\mathrm{H}_2(2 \\mathrm{~g} / \\mathrm{mol})$ is different from $\\mathrm{O}_2(32 \\mathrm{~g} / \\mathrm{mol})$, their r.m.s. speeds will be different even at the same temperature.\n\nTherefore, Reason R is false.\n\nHence, Assertion A is true, but Reason R is false.\n\nSo, the correct option is (C).",
