      "a": 2,
      "s": "JEE Main 2026 (Online) 2nd April Evening Shift. Correct option: C. Using the ideal gas equation $\\mathrm{PV}=\\mathrm{nRT}$\n\nThe pressure of gas is given as $\\mathrm{P}=100 \\mathrm{kPa}=10^5 \\mathrm{~Pa}$.\n\nThe volume of gas is $\\mathrm{V}=8310 \\mathrm{~cm}^3=8310 \\times 10^{-6} \\mathrm{~m}^3=8.31 \\times 10^{-3} \\mathrm{~m}^3$\n\nThe temperature of gas is $\\mathrm{T}=300 \\mathrm{~K}$\n\nThe universal gas constant is $\\mathrm{R}=8.31 \\mathrm{~J} / \\mathrm{mol} . \\mathrm{K}$\n\nSo, the number of moles of gas is,\n\n$$ \\mathrm{n}_{\\text {total }}=\\frac{\\mathrm{PV}}{\\mathrm{RT}}=\\frac{10^5 \\times 8.31 \\times 10^{-3}}{8.31 \\times 300} $$\n\n$$\\Rightarrow $$ $$ \\mathrm{n}_{\\text {total }}=\\frac{831}{2493}=\\frac{1}{3} \\approx 0.333 \\mathrm{moles} $$\n\nLet $\\mathrm{n}_1$ be the moles of $\\mathrm{CO}_2$ and $\\mathrm{n}_2$ be the moles of $\\mathrm{O}_2, \\mathrm{n}_1+\\mathrm{n}_2=0.333$ .......(i)\n\nMolar mass of $\\mathrm{CO}_2$ is $\\mathrm{M}_1=12+(2 \\times 16)=44 \\mathrm{~g} / \\mathrm{mol}$\n\nMolar mass of $\\mathrm{O}_2$ is $\\mathrm{M}_2=2 \\times 16=32 \\mathrm{~g} / \\mathrm{mol}$\n\nAs the total mass of the mixture is 13.2 g :\n\n$$ \\mathrm{n}_1 \\mathrm{M}_1+\\mathrm{n}_2 \\mathrm{M}_2=13.2 $$\n\n$$ 44 n_1+32 n_2=13.2 \\ldots ......(ii) $$\n\nFrom equation (i), $\\mathrm{n}_2=0.333-\\mathrm{n}_1$.\n\nSubstituting this into (ii) :\n\n$$ 44 \\mathrm{n}_1+32\\left(0.333-\\mathrm{n}_1\\right)=13.2 $$\n\n$$\\Rightarrow $$ $44 n_1+10.66-32 n_1=13.2$\n\n$$\\Rightarrow $$ $12 n_1=2.54$\n\n$$\\Rightarrow $$ $$ \\mathrm{n}_1 \\approx 0.21 \\text { moles } $$\n\nSo, $\\mathrm{n}_2=0.333-0.21=0.12$ moles\n\nTherefore, the number of moles of carbon dioxide and oxygen gases in the mixture respectively are $0.21,0.12$.\n\nHence, the correct option is (C).",
