      "q": "The equation for real gas is given by $\\left(\\mathrm{P}+\\frac{\\mathrm{a}}{\\mathrm{V}^2}\\right)(\\mathrm{V}-\\mathrm{b})=\\mathrm{RT}$, where $\\mathrm{P}, \\mathrm{V}, \\mathrm{T}$ and R are the pressure, volume, temperature and gas constant, respectively. The dimension of $\\mathrm{ab}^{-2}$ is equivalent to that of :",
      "qHtml": "<p>The equation for real gas is given by $\\left(\\mathrm{P}+\\frac{\\mathrm{a}}{\\mathrm{V}^2}\\right)(\\mathrm{V}-\\mathrm{b})=\\mathrm{RT}$, where $\\mathrm{P}, \\mathrm{V}, \\mathrm{T}$ and R are the pressure, volume, temperature and gas constant, respectively. The dimension of $\\mathrm{ab}^{-2}$ is equivalent to that of :\n</p>",
