      "s": "JEE Main 2017 (Online) 8th April Morning Slot. Correct option: B. Work done by engine = area under closed curve = P 0 V 0\n\nAccording to the principle of calorimetry,\n\nHeat given to the system,\n\nQ = Q AB + Q BC\n\n= nC v $$\\Delta $$T AB + nC p $$\\Delta $$T BC\n\n= $${3 \\over 2}$$ (nR T B $$-$$ nRT A ) + $${5 \\over 2}$$ (nRT c + nRT B )\n\n= $${3 \\over 2}$$ (2P 0 V 0 $$-$$ P 0 V 0 ) + $${5 \\over 2}$$ (4P 0 V 0 $$-$$ 2P 0 V 0 )\n\n= $${13 \\over 2}$$ P 0 V 0\n\n$$\\therefore\\,\\,\\,$$ Thermal efficiency\n\n= $${W \\over Q}$$ = $${{{P_0}\\,{V_0}} \\over {{{13} \\over 2}{P_0}{V_0}}}$$ = $${2 \\over {13}}$$ = 0.15",
      "source": "JEE Main 2017 (Online) 8th April Morning Slot | Thermodynamics | fzKtUzu87ZcX2uYIKV73y",
