      "a": 1,
      "s": "JEE Main 2026 (Online) 21st January Evening Shift. Correct option: B. In simple harmonic motion, the kinetic energy oscillates with angular frequency $2\\omega$, where $\\omega$ is the angular frequency of the oscillator.\n\nGiven:\n\n$$ 2\\omega = 176 \\ \\text{rad/s} $$\n\nSo,\n\n$$ \\omega = \\frac{176}{2} = 88 \\ \\text{rad/s} $$\n\nNow, frequency is related to angular frequency by:\n\n$$ \\omega = 2\\pi f $$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$ f = \\frac{\\omega}{2\\pi} = \\frac{88}{2 \\times \\frac{22}{7}} $$\n\n$$ f = \\frac{88}{\\frac{44}{7}} = 88 \\times \\frac{7}{44} $$\n\n$$ f = 2 \\times 7 = 14 \\ \\text{Hz} $$\n\nSo, the correct answer is:\n\n$$ \\boxed{14} $$\n\nOption B.",
      "source": "JEE Main 2026 (Online) 21st January Evening Shift | Oscillations | ml7sec83",
