      "q": "If $\\epsilon_0$ denotes the permittivity of free space and $\\Phi_E$ is the flux of the electric field through the area bounded by the closed surface, then dimensions of $\\left(\\epsilon_0 \\frac{d \\phi_E}{d t}\\right)$ are that of :",
      "qHtml": "<p>If $\\epsilon_0$ denotes the permittivity of free space and $\\Phi_E$ is the flux of the electric field through the area bounded by the closed surface, then dimensions of $\\left(\\epsilon_0 \\frac{d \\phi_E}{d t}\\right)$ are that of :</p>",
