      "s": "JEE Main 2025 (Online) 2nd April Evening Shift. Correct option: D. [Diagram: JEE Main 2025 (Online) 2nd April Evening Shift Physics - Electrostatics Question 35 English Explanation]\n\nStep 1: Formula for Potential Difference\n\nThe potential difference ($$\\Delta V$$) between two points in a uniform electric field is found by multiplying the electric field ($$E$$) by the distance ($$\\Delta d$$) between the points:\n\n$$\\Delta V = E \\times \\Delta d$$\n\nStep 2: Find the Electric Field\n\nThe total potential difference between the two plates is $$V$$, and they are 10 cm apart.\n\nSo, the electric field between the plates is:\n\n$$E = \\frac{V}{10}$$\n\nHere, distance is in centimeters.\n\nStep 3: Calculate Potential Difference Between A and B\n\nPoints A and B are 4 cm apart.\n\nSo, the potential difference between A and B will be:\n\n$$V_{AB} = E \\times 4 = \\frac{V}{10} \\times 4 = \\frac{4V}{10} = \\frac{2V}{5}$$",
