      "s": "JEE Main 2025 (Online) 29th January Evening Shift. Correct option: B. Given an electric flux $\\phi = -2 \\times 10^4 \\, \\text{Nm}^2\\text{C}^{-1}$ through a spherical Gaussian surface with a radius of 8.0 cm (r = 0.08 m), we are to find the value of the point charge $Q$. According to Gauss's Law:\n\n$ \\phi = \\frac{Q}{\\varepsilon_0} $\n\nWhere $\\varepsilon_0 = 8.85 \\times 10^{-12} \\, \\text{C}^2\\text{N}^{-1}\\text{m}^{-2}$.\n\nRearranging the equation to solve for $Q$, we have:\n\n$ Q = \\phi \\varepsilon_0 $\n\nSubstituting the given values:\n\n$ Q = -2 \\times 10^4 \\times 8.85 \\times 10^{-12} $\n\nCalculating this yields:\n\n$ Q = -17.7 \\times 10^{-8} \\, \\text{C} $\n\nThus, the value of the point charge is $Q = -17.7 \\times 10^{-8} \\, \\text{C}$.",
