      "q": "Two point charges $-4 \\mu \\mathrm{c}$ and $4 \\mu \\mathrm{c}$, constituting an electric dipole, are placed at $(-9,0,0) \\mathrm{cm}$ and $(9,0,0) \\mathrm{cm}$ in a uniform electric field of strength $10^4 \\mathrm{NC}^{-1}$. The work done on the dipole in rotating it from the equilibrium through $180^{\\circ}$ is :",
      "qHtml": "<p>Two point charges $-4 \\mu \\mathrm{c}$ and $4 \\mu \\mathrm{c}$, constituting an electric dipole, are placed at $(-9,0,0) \\mathrm{cm}$ and $(9,0,0) \\mathrm{cm}$ in a uniform electric field of strength $10^4 \\mathrm{NC}^{-1}$. The work done on the dipole in rotating it from the equilibrium through $180^{\\circ}$ is :</p>",
