      "q": "Five positive charges each having charge $q$ are placed at the vertices of a pentagon as shown in the figure. The electric potential $(V)$ and the electric field $(\\vec{E})$ at the center $O$ of the pentagon due to these five positive charges are :\n\n[Diagram: JEE Main 2026 (Online) 22nd January Evening Shift Physics - Electrostatics Question 19 English]",
      "qHtml": "<p>Five positive charges each having charge $q$ are placed at the vertices of a pentagon as shown in the figure. The electric potential $(V)$ and the electric field $(\\vec{E})$ at the center $O$ of the pentagon due to these five positive charges are :</p>\n<img class=\"quiz-question-image\" src=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/image/6y3zli1mlwd6kfa/16606f49-5fb3-4d26-bd5e-9e0b57e9ec0e/94a5e860-0f2a-11f1-bd0d-b1da3324815a/file-6y3zli1mlwd6kfb.png\" alt=\"JEE Main 2026 (Online) 22nd January Evening Shift Physics - Electrostatics Question 19 English\" loading=\"lazy\">",
