      "s": "JEE Main 2026 (Online) 5th April Morning Shift. Correct option: B. We have three identical branches in parallel. Each branch has an emf $\\mathrm{E}=5 \\mathrm{~V}$ and an internal resistance $\\mathrm{r}= 3 \\Omega$.\n\nWhen cells are connected in series with their polarity in order, the equivalent emf is given as,\n\n$$ \\mathrm{E}_{\\mathrm{eq}(\\mathrm{~s})}=\\mathrm{E}_1+\\mathrm{E}_2+\\cdots+\\mathrm{E}_{\\mathrm{n}} $$\n\nThe equivalent internal resistance is given as $\\mathrm{r}_{\\mathrm{eq}(\\mathrm{s})}=\\mathrm{r}_1+\\mathrm{r}_2+\\cdots+\\mathrm{r}_{\\mathrm{n}}$.\n\nWhen cells are connected in parallel with their polarity in order, the equivalent emf is given as\n\n$$ \\mathrm{E}_{\\mathrm{eq}(\\mathrm{p})}=\\frac{\\frac{\\mathrm{E}_1}{\\mathrm{r}_1}+\\frac{\\mathrm{E}_2}{\\mathrm{r}_2}+\\cdots+\\frac{\\mathrm{E}_{\\mathrm{n}}}{\\mathrm{r}_{\\mathrm{n}}}}{\\frac{1}{\\mathrm{r}_1}+\\frac{1}{\\mathrm{r}_2}+\\cdots+\\frac{1}{\\mathrm{r}_{\\mathrm{n}}}} $$\n\nThe equivalent internal resistance is given as $\\frac{1}{r_{e q(p)}}=\\frac{1}{r_1}+\\frac{1}{r_2}+\\cdots+\\frac{1}{r_n}$.\n\nFor each branch, total emf is, $\\mathrm{E}_{\\mathrm{eq}}=(5+5+5+) \\mathrm{V}=15 \\mathrm{~V}$\n\nTotal internal resistance is, $\\mathrm{r}_{\\mathrm{eq}}=(3+3+3) \\Omega=9 \\Omega$\n\nSo, the circuit simplifies to;\n\n[Diagram: JEE Main 2026 (Online) 5th April Morning Shift Physics - Current Electricity Question 4 English Explanation 1]\n\nNow all three branches containing cell are in parallel.\n\nUsing the parallel combination of cells;\n\n$$ \\mathrm{E}_{\\text {total }}=\\frac{\\frac{15}{9}+\\frac{15}{9}+\\frac{15}{9}}{\\frac{1}{9}+\\frac{1}{9}+\\frac{1}{9}}=\\frac{45}{3}=15 \\mathrm{~V} $$\n\nThe total internal resistance is,\n\n$$ \\frac{1}{\\mathrm{r}_{\\text {total }}}=\\frac{1}{9}+\\frac{1}{9}+\\frac{1}{9}=\\frac{1}{3} \\Rightarrow \\mathrm{r}_{\\text {total }}=3 \\Omega $$\n\nAnd the total external resistance between A and B is $\\mathrm{R}_{\\text {total }}=(3+3+3) \\Omega=9 \\Omega$\n\nSo, the circuit simplifies to,\n\n[Diagram: JEE Main 2026 (Online) 5th April Morning Shift Physics - Current Electricity Question 4 English Explanation 2]\n\nUsing Ohm's Law $\\left(I=\\frac{V}{R}\\right)$ for the entire circuit, the current through $A$ and $B$ will be\n\n$i=\\frac{E_{\\text {total }}}{R_{\\text {net }}}=\\frac{15}{(3+9)}=\\frac{15}{12} A=$ 1.25 A\n\nThus, the correct option is (B).",
