      "q": "For designing a voltmeter of range $50 \\mathrm{~V}$ and an ammeter of range $10 \\mathrm{~mA}$ using a galvanometer which has a coil of resistance $54 \\Omega$ showing a full scale deflection for $1 \\mathrm{~mA}$ as in figure.\n\n[Diagram: JEE Main 2023 (Online) 15th April Morning Shift Physics - Current Electricity Question 118 English]\n\n(A) for voltmeter $R \\approx 50 \\mathrm{k} \\Omega$\n\n(B) for ammeter $\\mathrm{r} \\approx 0.2 \\Omega$\n\n(C) for ammeter $\\mathrm{r}=6 \\Omega$\n\n(D) for voltmeter $R \\approx 5 \\mathrm{k} \\Omega$\n\n(E) for voltmeter $R \\approx 500 \\Omega$\n\nChoose the correct answer from the options given below:",
