      "qHtml": "A conducting square loop of side $$L$$ and resistance $$R$$ moves in its plane with a uniform velocity $$v$$ perpendicular to one of its sides. A magnetic induction $$B$$ constant in time and space, pointing perpendicular and into the plane at the loop exists everywhere with half the loop outside the field, as shown in figure. The induced $$emf$$ is \n<img class=\"quiz-question-image\" src=\"https://imagex.cdn.examgoal.net/FLYaMRa4u35666zrE/b9LjT1N9L63i9wR19iOsAL4jOrOeG/C5ZCznjxxFfpWGPtsJ4WVb/image.png\" alt=\"AIEEE 2002 Physics - Electromagnetic Induction Question 139 English\" loading=\"lazy\">",
