      "a": 0,
      "s": "JEE Main 2025 (Online) 22nd January Evening Shift. Correct option: A. At resonance in a series LCR circuit, the reactive components (inductive and capacitive) cancel each other out, leaving only the resistance. Therefore, the amplitude of the current is given by:\n\n$$ I_0 = \\frac{E}{R} $$\n\nNow, if the resistance is doubled, the new resistance becomes $2R$. The current amplitude at resonance then becomes:\n\n$$ I = \\frac{E}{2R} = \\frac{1}{2}\\left(\\frac{E}{R}\\right) = \\frac{I_0}{2} $$\n\nThus, the amplitude of current at resonance when the resistance is doubled is $ \\frac{I_0}{2} $.\n\nThe correct option is A.",
