      "a": 2,
      "s": "JEE Main 2026 (Online) 4th April Evening Shift. Correct option: C. When polarized light of intensity $\\mathrm{I}_{\\text {in }}$ passes through a polarizer, the intensity of the transmitted light $\\left(\\mathrm{I}_{\\text {out }}\\right)$ is given by Malus's Law\n\n$$ I_{\\text {out }}=I_{\\text {in }} \\cos ^2 \\theta $$\n\nWhere $\\theta$ is the angle between the polarization direction of the incident light and the transmission axis of the polarizer.\n\nThe initial intensity of unpolarised light $=\\mathrm{I}_0$.\n\nAfter the first polarizer (at $30^{\\circ}$ ), the light becomes polarized with intensity $\\mathrm{I}_1=\\frac{1}{2} \\mathrm{I}_0$.\n\nThis light then hits the second polarizer (at $90^{\\circ}$ ). The angle between them is $\\theta=90^{\\circ}-30^{\\circ}=60^{\\circ}$.\n\nSo, the final intensity without third polarizer is,\n\n$$ I_{\\text {withoud }}=I_2=I_1 \\cos ^2 60^{\\circ}=\\left(\\frac{1}{2} I_0\\right)\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)^2=\\frac{1}{2} I_0 \\times \\frac{1}{4}=\\frac{I_0}{8} $$\n\nThe intensity after the first polarizer (at $30^{\\circ}$ ) is $\\mathrm{I}_1=\\frac{1}{2} \\mathrm{I}_0$.\n\nThis light hits the middle polarizer (at $60^{\\circ}$ ). The angle is $\\theta_{12}=60^{\\circ}-30^{\\circ}=30^{\\circ}$.\n\nSo, intensity after middle polarizer $\\left(\\mathrm{I}_3\\right)$ :\n\n$$ I_3=I_1 \\cos ^2 30^{\\circ}=\\left(\\frac{1}{2} I_0\\right)\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\right)^2=\\frac{1}{2} I_0 \\times \\frac{3}{4}=\\frac{3 I_0}{8} $$\n\nThis light hits the final polarizer (at $90^{\\circ}$ ). The angle is $\\theta_{23}=90^{\\circ}-60^{\\circ}=30^{\\circ}$.\n\nSo, final intensity after the final polarizer is\n\n$$ \\mathrm{I}_{\\text {with }}=\\mathrm{I}_3 \\cos ^2 30^{\\circ}=\\left(\\frac{3 \\mathrm{I}_0}{8}\\right)\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\right)^2=\\frac{3 \\mathrm{I}_0}{8} \\times \\frac{3}{4}=\\frac{9 \\mathrm{I}_0}{32} $$\n\nSo, the ratio of the output intensities with and without the third polarizer is,\n\n$$ \\frac{\\mathrm{I}_{\\text {with }}}{\\mathrm{I}_{\\text {without }}}=\\frac{\\left(\\frac{9 \\mathrm{I}_0}{32}\\right)}{\\left(\\frac{\\mathrm{I}_0}{8}\\right)}=\\frac{9}{4} $$\n\nTherefore, the ratio of the output intensities with and without the third polarizer is $9 / 4$.\n\nThus, the correct option is (C).",
      "source": "JEE Main 2026 (Online) 4th April Evening Shift | Electromagnetic Waves | mnswhqr7",
      "pyq": true,
      "exactPaperText": true,
