      "a": 3,
      "s": "JEE Main 2026 (Online) 4th April Evening Shift. Correct option: D. For a thin lens with two curved surfaces, the focal length ( $f$ ) is related to the refractive index ( $n$ ) and the radii of curvature $\\left(\\mathrm{R}_1\\right.$ and $\\left.\\mathrm{R}_2\\right)$ by Lens Makers' formula,\n\n[Diagram: JEE Main 2026 (Online) 4th April Evening Shift Physics - Geometrical Optics Question 5 English Explanation]\n\n$$ \\frac{1}{\\mathrm{f}}=(\\mathrm{n}-1)\\left(\\frac{1}{\\mathrm{R}_1}-\\frac{1}{\\mathrm{R}_2}\\right) $$\n\nThe refractive index of the material, $\\mathrm{n}=1.4$.\n\nThe lens is convex with the same radius of curvature on both sides (R).\n\nAccording to the Cartesian sign convention:\n\nThe first surface is convex towards the incident light, so $\\mathrm{R}_1=+\\mathrm{R}$.\n\nThe second surface is concave towards the incident light, so $R_2=-R$.\n\nSubstituting the values into the formula :\n\n$$ \\frac{1}{\\mathrm{f}}=(1.4-1)\\left(\\frac{1}{\\mathrm{R}}-\\frac{1}{-\\mathrm{R}}\\right) $$\n\n$$\\Rightarrow $$ $\\frac{1}{\\mathrm{f}}=(0.4)\\left(\\frac{1}{\\mathrm{R}}+\\frac{1}{\\mathrm{R}}\\right)$\n\n$$\\Rightarrow $$ $\\frac{1}{\\mathrm{f}}=0.4 \\times \\frac{2}{\\mathrm{R}}$\n\n$$\\Rightarrow $$ $\\frac{1}{f}=\\frac{0.8}{R}$\n\n$$\\Rightarrow $$ $\\mathrm{f}=\\frac{\\mathrm{R}}{0.8}$\n\n$$\\Rightarrow $$ $$ \\frac{\\mathrm{f}}{\\mathrm{R}}=\\frac{1}{0.8}=1.25 $$\n\nTherefore, the ratio of its focal length and radius of curvature is 1.25 .\n\nThus, the correct option is (D).",
