      "a": 3,
      "s": "JEE Main 2026 (Online) 22nd January Evening Shift. Correct option: D. For photoelectrons to have zero kinetic energy, the incident light must have the threshold frequency .\n\nUsing Einstein’s photoelectric equation:\n\n$$ h \\nu = \\phi $$\n\nwhere\n\n$\\phi = 110 \\times 10^{-20}\\ \\text{J} = 1.10 \\times 10^{-18}\\ \\text{J}$\n\nand\n\n$$ \\nu = \\frac{\\phi}{h} = \\frac{1.10 \\times 10^{-18}}{6.63 \\times 10^{-34}} $$\n\n$$ \\nu \\approx 1.66 \\times 10^{15}\\ \\text{Hz} $$\n\nNow angular frequency is:\n\n$$ \\omega = 2\\pi \\nu $$\n\n$$ \\omega = 2\\pi \\times 1.66 \\times 10^{15} \\approx 10.43 \\times 10^{15} = 1.04 \\times 10^{16}\\ \\text{rad/s} $$\n\nSo, the correct answer is:\n\n$$ \\boxed{1.04 \\times 10^{16}\\ \\text{rad/s}} $$\n\nHence, Option D is correct.",
