      "q": "A photoemissive substance is illuminated with a radiation of wavelength $\\lambda_i$ so that it releases electrons with de-Broglie wavelength $\\lambda_e$. The longest wavelength of radiation that can emit photoelectron is $\\lambda_o$. Expression for de-Broglie wavelength is given by:\n(m: mass of the electron, h: Planck's constant and c: speed of light)",
      "qHtml": "<p>A photoemissive substance is illuminated with a radiation of wavelength $\\lambda_i$ so that it releases electrons with de-Broglie wavelength $\\lambda_e$. The longest wavelength of radiation that can emit photoelectron is $\\lambda_o$. Expression for de-Broglie wavelength is given by:</p> <p>(m: mass of the electron, h: Planck's constant and c: speed of light)</p>",
