      "a": 2,
      "s": "JEE Main 2026 (Online) 2nd April Morning Shift. Correct option: C. According to Bohr's second postulate, the angular momentum (L) of an electron in a stationary orbit is quantized and given by :\n\n$$L = \\frac{nh}{2\\pi}$$\n\nThe angular momentum is $L = \\frac{3h}{\\pi}$.\n\n$$\\Rightarrow \\frac{nh}{2\\pi} = \\frac{3h}{\\pi}$$\n\n$$\\Rightarrow \\frac{n}{2} = 3$$\n\n$$\\Rightarrow n = 6$$\n\nIn the Bohr model, the total energy ($E_n$) of an electron in the $n^{\\text{th}}$ orbit of a hydrogen atom is the sum of its kinetic and potential energies. The energy in electron volts (eV) is derived as :\n\n$$E_n = -13.6n^2\\ \\text{eV}$$\n\nFor $n = 6$:\n\n$$E_6 = -\\frac{13.6}{6^2}$$\n\n$$E_6 = -\\frac{13.6}{36}$$\n\n$$E_6 \\approx -0.3777\\ldots\\ \\text{eV}$$\n\nTherefore, the energy of the electron is $-0.38\\ \\text{eV}$. Therefore, the correct option is (C).",
      "source": "JEE Main 2026 (Online) 2nd April Morning Shift | Atomic Physics | mnrl0173",
