      "s": "JEE Main 2016 (Online) 9th April Morning Slot. Correct option: C. Energy released when hydrogen atom makes transition from n = 2 to n = 1 is,\n\nE 1 = 13.6 $$ \\times $$ $$\\left( {{1 \\over {{1^2}}} - {1 \\over {{z^2}}}} \\right)$$\n\n= $${3 \\over 4} \\times 13.6\\,\\,\\,$$ eV\n\nEnergy required to remove a electron from n th excited state of doubly ionized lithium,\n\nE 2 = $${{13.6{z^2}} \\over {{n^2}}}$$ = $${{13.6 \\times {3^2}} \\over {{n^2}}}$$ eV\n\nThis energy is provided by the photon when it strike with the lithium atom.\n\n$$ \\therefore $$ E 1 $$ \\ge $$ E 2\n\n$$ \\Rightarrow $$ $${3 \\over 4} \\times 13.6 \\ge {{13.6 \\times 9} \\over {{n^2}}}$$\n\n$$ \\Rightarrow $$ n 2 $$ \\ge $$ 3$$ \\times $$4\n\n$$ \\Rightarrow $$ n $$ \\ge $$ $$\\sqrt {12} $$\n\n$$ \\Rightarrow $$ n $$ \\ge $$ 3.5\n\n$$ \\therefore $$ Least possible excited state = 4",
