      "q": "The maximum rated power of the LED is 2 mW and it is used in the circuit with input voltage of 5 V as shown in the figure below. The current through resistance $R_S$ is 0.5 mA .\n\nThe minimum value of the resistance of $R_S$, to ensure that the LED is not damaged is $\\_\\_\\_\\_$ $\\mathrm{k} \\Omega$.\n\n[Diagram: JEE Main 2026 (Online) 6th April Morning Shift Physics - Semiconductor Question 2 English]",
      "qHtml": "<p>The maximum rated power of the LED is 2 mW and it is used in the circuit with input voltage of 5 V as shown in the figure below. The current through resistance $R_S$ is 0.5 mA .</p>\n<p>The minimum value of the resistance of $R_S$, to ensure that the LED is not damaged is $\\_\\_\\_\\_$ $\\mathrm{k} \\Omega$.</p><img class=\"quiz-question-image\" src=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/image/6y3zli1mo5o9w11/70b9de56-1036-4030-b152-bd2e1ded389a/72100950-3be1-11f1-aafb-6f2b8ad54979/file-6y3zli1mo5o9w12.png\" alt=\"JEE Main 2026 (Online) 6th April Morning Shift Physics - Semiconductor Question 2 English\" loading=\"lazy\">",
