      "a": 2,
      "s": "JEE Main 2026 (Online) 5th April Evening Shift. Correct option: C. The reaction is:\n\n$$ \\mathrm{Zn} + \\mathrm{H_2SO_4} \\rightarrow \\mathrm{ZnSO_4} + \\mathrm{H_2} $$\n\nFrom the balanced equation,\n\n$$ 1 \\text{ mol Zn } \\text{ reacts with } 1 \\text{ mol } \\mathrm{H_2SO_4} \\text{ and gives } 1 \\text{ mol } \\mathrm{H_2} $$\n\nNow let us find the number of moles of each reactant.\n\n1. Amount of $\\mathrm{H_2SO_4}$ present\n\nVolume of acid solution $= 50 \\, \\mathrm{mL}$\n\nDensity $= 1.3 \\, \\mathrm{g\\,mL^{-1}}$\n\nSo, mass of acid solution is\n\n$$ \\text{Mass} = \\text{Volume} \\times \\text{Density} = 50 \\times 1.3 = 65 \\, \\mathrm{g} $$\n\nPurity $= 50\\%$\n\nHence, mass of pure $\\mathrm{H_2SO_4}$ is\n\n$$ \\frac{50}{100} \\times 65 = 32.5 \\, \\mathrm{g} $$\n\nMolar mass of $\\mathrm{H_2SO_4}$:\n\n$$ 2(1) + 32 + 4(16) = 98 \\, \\mathrm{g\\,mol^{-1}} $$\n\nSo, moles of $\\mathrm{H_2SO_4}$ are\n\n$$ \\frac{32.5}{98} = 0.3316 \\text{ mol} $$\n\n2. Amount of zinc\n\nMass of Zn $= 20 \\, \\mathrm{g}$\n\nMolar mass of Zn $= 65 \\, \\mathrm{g\\,mol^{-1}}$\n\nSo, moles of Zn are\n\n$$ \\frac{20}{65} = 0.3077 \\text{ mol} $$\n\n3. Limiting reagent\n\nSince the reaction ratio is $1:1$:\n\n$\\mathrm{H_2SO_4}$ available $= 0.3316$ mol\n\nZn available $= 0.3077$ mol\n\nZn is smaller in amount, so zinc is the limiting reagent .\n\nTherefore, moles of $\\mathrm{H_2}$ formed are\n\n$$ 0.3077 \\text{ mol} $$\n\n4. Volume of hydrogen at STP\n\nAt STP, $1$ mol gas occupies $22.4 \\, \\mathrm{L}$.\n\nSo, volume of $\\mathrm{H_2}$ is\n\n$$ 0.3077 \\times 22.4 = 6.892 \\, \\mathrm{L} $$\n\n$$ \\boxed{6.892 \\, \\mathrm{L}} $$\n\nSo, the correct option is:\n\n$$ \\boxed{\\text{Option C}} $$",
      "source": "JEE Main 2026 (Online) 5th April Evening Shift | Some Basic Concepts of Chemistry | mnswhslh",
