      "s": "JEE Main 2026 (Online) 2nd April Evening Shift. Correct option: B. Let the hydrocarbon be $C_2H_x$ since it has two carbon atoms.\n\nGiven, the mass percentage ratio of $C:H$ is $12:1$.\n\nSo, in the hydrocarbon,\n\nmass of carbon $= 2 \\times 12 = 24$\n\nmass of hydrogen $= x \\times 1 = x$\n\nNow,\n\n$$ 24 : x = 12 : 1 $$\n\nSo,\n\n$$ \\frac{24}{x} = \\frac{12}{1} $$\n\n$$ 24 = 12x $$\n\n$$ x = 2 $$\n\nHence, the hydrocarbon is\n\n$$ C_2H_2 $$\n\nIts molar mass is\n\n$$ (2 \\times 12) + (2 \\times 1) = 24 + 2 = 26 \\text{ g mol}^{-1} $$\n\nNumber of moles of $C_2H_2$ in $3.38$ g:\n\n$$ \\text{moles of } C_2H_2 = \\frac{3.38}{26} = 0.13 \\text{ mol} $$\n\nComplete combustion of acetylene:\n\n$$ 2C_2H_2 + 5O_2 \\rightarrow 4CO_2 + 2H_2O $$\n\nFrom the equation,\n\n$$ 1 \\text{ mol } C_2H_2 \\rightarrow 2 \\text{ mol } CO_2 $$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$ 0.13 \\text{ mol } C_2H_2 \\rightarrow 0.26 \\text{ mol } CO_2 $$\n\nMolar mass of $CO_2$:\n\n$$ 12 + (2 \\times 16) = 44 \\text{ g mol}^{-1} $$\n\nMass of $CO_2$ formed:\n\n$$ 0.26 \\times 44 = 11.44 \\text{ g} $$\n\nSo, the correct answer is\n\n$$ \\boxed{11.44 \\text{ g}} $$\n\nOption B.",
