      "s": "JEE Main 2026 (Online) 2nd April Morning Shift. Correct option: D. The reaction of iron with steam is:\n\n$$ 3Fe + 4H_2O \\rightarrow Fe_3O_4 + 4H_2 $$\n\nWe are given:\n\n$$ \\text{Mass of steam} = 18 \\text{ g} $$\n\nMolar mass of water:\n\n$$ H_2O = 2(1) + 16 = 18 \\text{ g mol}^{-1} $$\n\nSo, moles of steam are:\n\n$$ \\text{Moles of } H_2O = \\frac{18}{18} = 1 \\text{ mol} $$\n\nFrom the balanced equation:\n\n$$ 4 \\text{ mol } H_2O \\text{ react with } 3 \\text{ mol } Fe $$\n\nTherefore, for $1$ mol $H_2O$:\n\n$$ \\text{Moles of Fe required} = \\frac{3}{4} $$\n\nNow, molar mass of iron is:\n\n$$ 56 \\text{ g mol}^{-1} $$\n\nSo, mass of iron reacted:\n\n$$ \\text{Mass of Fe} = \\frac{3}{4} \\times 56 = 42 \\text{ g} $$\n\nHence, the mass of iron converted into $Fe_3O_4$ is:\n\n$$ \\boxed{42 \\text{ g}} $$\n\nSo, the correct option is:\n\n$$ \\boxed{\\text{Option D}} $$",
