      "s": "JEE Main 2026 (Online) 2nd April Morning Shift. Correct option: C. For the process\n\n$$ \\text{Li}^{2+}(g) \\rightarrow \\text{Li}^{3+}(g) + e^- $$\n\nwe have to remove the only electron present in $\\text{Li}^{2+}$.\n\n$\\text{Li}^{2+}$ is a hydrogen-like species because it has only one electron.\n\nFor a hydrogen-like species, ionization energy is given by\n\n$$ E = Z^2 \\times 2.18 \\times 10^{-18}\\ \\text{J atom}^{-1} $$\n\nwhere $Z$ is the atomic number.\n\nFor lithium, $Z = 3$.\n\nSo,\n\n$$ E = 3^2 \\times 2.18 \\times 10^{-18} $$\n\n$$ E = 9 \\times 2.18 \\times 10^{-18} $$\n\n$$ E = 19.62 \\times 10^{-18} $$\n\n$$ E = 1.962 \\times 10^{-17}\\ \\text{J atom}^{-1} $$\n\nHence, the required energy is\n\n$$ \\boxed{1.962 \\times 10^{-17}\\ \\text{J atom}^{-1}} $$\n\nSo, the correct option is:\n\n$$ \\boxed{\\text{Option C}} $$",
