      "q": "Which of the following statements are true?\n\n(A) The subsidiary quantum number $l$ describes the shape of the orbital occupied by the electron.\n\n(B)\n[Diagram: JEE Main 2025 (Online) 2nd April Evening Shift Chemistry - Structure of Atom Question 33 English]\nis the boundary surface diagram of the $2 \\mathrm{p}_x$ orbital.\n\n(C) The + and - signs in the wave function of the $2 p_x$ orbital refer to charge.\n\n(D) The wave function of $2 \\mathrm{p}_x$ orbital is zero everywhere in the $x y$ plane.\n\nChoose the correct answer from the options given below :",
      "qHtml": "<p>Which of the following statements are true?</p>\n<p>(A) The subsidiary quantum number $l$ describes the shape of the orbital occupied by the electron.</p>\n<p>(B) <img class=\"quiz-question-image\" src=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/image/jaoe38c1mbatxjsz/f28ff2a8-0908-4b9b-9561-26fd0ef43be9/ad01ad30-3d58-11f0-9ada-d3921be4ce16/file-jaoe38c1mbatxjt0.png\" alt=\"JEE Main 2025 (Online) 2nd April Evening Shift Chemistry - Structure of Atom Question 33 English\" loading=\"lazy\"> is the boundary surface diagram of the $2 \\mathrm{p}_x$ orbital.</p>\n<p>(C) The + and - signs in the wave function of the $2 p_x$ orbital refer to charge.</p>\n<p>(D) The wave function of $2 \\mathrm{p}_x$ orbital is zero everywhere in the $x y$ plane.</p>\n<p>Choose the correct answer from the options given below :</p>",
