      "q": "Given below are statements about some molecules/ions.\n\nIdentify the CORRECT statements.\n\nA. The dipole moment value of $\\mathrm{NF}_3$ is higher than that of $\\mathrm{NH}_3$.\n\nB. The dipole moment value of $\\mathrm{BeH}_2$ is zero.\n\nC. The bond order of $\\mathrm{O}_2{ }^{2-}$ and $\\mathrm{F}_2$ is same.\n\nD. The formal charge on the central oxygen atom of ozone is -1 .\n\nE. In $\\mathrm{NO}_2$, all the three atoms satisfy the octet rule, hence it is very stable.\n\nChoose the correct answer from the options given below:",
      "qHtml": "<p>Given below are statements about some molecules/ions.</p>\n<p>Identify the CORRECT statements.</p>\n<p>A. The dipole moment value of $\\mathrm{NF}_3$ is higher than that of $\\mathrm{NH}_3$.</p>\n<p>B. The dipole moment value of $\\mathrm{BeH}_2$ is zero.</p>\n<p>C. The bond order of $\\mathrm{O}_2{ }^{2-}$ and $\\mathrm{F}_2$ is same.</p>\n<p>D. The formal charge on the central oxygen atom of ozone is -1 .</p>\n<p>E. In $\\mathrm{NO}_2$, all the three atoms satisfy the octet rule, hence it is very stable.</p>\n<p>Choose the correct answer from the options given below:</p>",
