      "a": 3,
      "s": "JEE Main 2026 (Online) 21st January Evening Shift. Correct option: D. Bond length is inversely related to bond order (as per NCERT idea):\n\ntriple bond $ Also, for single bonds , bond length increases when the bonded atom is larger (so $C{-}O$ is longer than $C{-}H$).\n\nNow compare:\n\n$C{-}H$ (A): single bond, but H is very small $\\Rightarrow$ short\n\n$C{\\equiv}N$ (D): triple bond $\\Rightarrow$ very short\n\n$C{=}O$ (C): double bond $\\Rightarrow$ short, but longer than triple\n\n$C{-}O$ (B): single bond with larger O $\\Rightarrow$ longest\n\nSo increasing order of bond length is:\n\n$$A Correct option: D",
