      "s": "JEE Main 2026 (Online) 5th April Morning Shift. Correct option: C. Mixture A:\n\nThe acid is $\\mathrm{HCl}$, which furnishes 1 $\\mathrm{H}^+$ ion per molecule.\n\n$$ \\text{Millimoles of } \\mathrm{H}^+ = \\text{Molarity} \\times \\text{Volume in mL} \\times 1 = 0.1 \\times 25 \\times 1 = 2.5 \\text{ mmol} $$\n\nThe base is $\\mathrm{Ca}(\\mathrm{OH})_2$, which furnishes 2 $\\mathrm{OH}^-$ ions per molecule.\n\n$$ \\text{Millimoles of } \\mathrm{OH}^- = \\text{Molarity} \\times \\text{Volume in mL} \\times 2 = 0.2 \\times 10 \\times 2 = 4.0 \\text{ mmol} $$\n\nSince the amount of $\\mathrm{OH}^-$ ions is greater than $\\mathrm{H}^+$ ions ($4.0 > 2.5$), the remaining solution has an excess of $\\mathrm{OH}^-$ ions. Therefore, mixture A is basic , which means its pH will be greater than 7.\n\nMixture B:\n\nThe acid is $\\mathrm{H}_2\\mathrm{SO}_4$, which furnishes 2 $\\mathrm{H}^+$ ions per molecule.\n\n$$ \\text{Millimoles of } \\mathrm{H}^+ = 0.01 \\times 10 \\times 2 = 0.2 \\text{ mmol} $$\n\nThe base is $\\mathrm{Ca}(\\mathrm{OH})_2$, which furnishes 2 $\\mathrm{OH}^-$ ions per molecule.\n\n$$ \\text{Millimoles of } \\mathrm{OH}^- = 0.01 \\times 10 \\times 2 = 0.2 \\text{ mmol} $$\n\nHere, the amount of $\\mathrm{H}^+$ ions exactly equals the amount of $\\mathrm{OH}^-$ ions ($0.2 = 0.2$). This results in complete neutralization. Thus, mixture B is neutral , meaning its pH will be exactly equal to 7.\n\nMixture C:\n\nThe acid is $\\mathrm{H}_2\\mathrm{SO}_4$, furnishing 2 $\\mathrm{H}^+$ ions per molecule.\n\n$$ \\text{Millimoles of } \\mathrm{H}^+ = 0.1 \\times 10 \\times 2 = 2.0 \\text{ mmol} $$\n\nThe base is $\\mathrm{KOH}$, which furnishes 1 $\\mathrm{OH}^-$ ion per molecule.\n\n$$ \\text{Millimoles of } \\mathrm{OH}^- = 0.1 \\times 10 \\times 1 = 1.0 \\text{ mmol} $$\n\nSince the amount of $\\mathrm{H}^+$ ions is greater than $\\mathrm{OH}^-$ ions ($2.0 > 1.0$), there is an excess of $\\mathrm{H}^+$ ions in the solution. Therefore, mixture C is acidic , meaning its pH will be down, specifically less than 7.\n\nFinal Conclusion:\n\nNow, let us bring it all together and arrange them in increasing order of their pH values (from most acidic to most basic):\n\nMixture C is acidic ($\\mathrm{pH} Mixture B is neutral ($\\mathrm{pH} = 7$)\n\nMixture A is basic ($\\mathrm{pH} > 7$)\n\nThe increasing order of their pH values is $\\mathrm{C} Therefore, the correct answer is Option C .",
