      "qHtml": "<p>Consider the following chemical equilibrium of the gas phase reaction at a constant temperature : $\\mathrm{A}(\\mathrm{g}) \\rightleftharpoons \\mathrm{B}(\\mathrm{g})+\\mathrm{C}(\\mathrm{g})$</p>\n<p>If $p$ being the total pressure, $K_p$ is the pressure equilibrium constant and $\\alpha$ is the degree of dissociation, then which of the following is true at equilibrium?</p>",
