      "s": "JEE Main 2026 (Online) 2nd April Evening Shift. Correct option: A. Carbocation ($C^+$) has a deficiency of electrons, so it becomes more stable when a group donates electron density towards it.\n\nTherefore, carbocations are stabilised by electron donating groups (EDGs) due to $+R,+T,+H$ effect whereas, carbanions ($C^-$) are stabilised by electron withdrawing groups (EWGs) due to $-R,-I,-H$ effect.\n[Diagram: JEE Main 2026 (Online) 2nd April Evening Shift Chemistry - Basics of Organic Chemistry Question 11 English Explanation 1]\n\nSo, in Statement I, the $-OCH_3$ group shows $+R$ effect (lone pair donation), which stabilises the carbocation by resonance.\n\n[Diagram: JEE Main 2026 (Online) 2nd April Evening Shift Chemistry - Basics of Organic Chemistry Question 11 English Explanation 2]\n\nIn Statement II, the $-NO_2$ group shows $-R$ effect (it withdraws electron density), which stabilises the carbanion by resonance.",
