      "s": "JEE Main 2026 (Online) 6th April Evening Shift. Correct option: D. In chamber (I), the concentration of solute is calculated as:\n\n$$C_1 = \\frac{18/180}{0.1} = 1\\, \\text{M}$$\n\nIn chamber (II), the concentration is given by:\n\n$$C_2 = \\frac{30/180}{250/1000} = \\frac{2}{3}\\, \\text{M}$$\n\nSince osmotic pressure depends on concentration and $\\pi_1 > \\pi_2$, water will move from the side having lower osmotic pressure (chamber II) to the side having higher osmotic pressure (chamber I).\n\nOsmotic pressure is calculated using the formula:\n\n$$\\pi = iCRT$$\n\nFor potassium sulfate $(\\mathrm{K_2SO_4})$, the van’t Hoff factor is $i = 3$.\n\nSo,\n\n$$\\pi = 3 \\times \\left(\\frac{50 \\times 10^{-3}/174}{2}\\right) \\times 0.083 \\times 300$$\n\nOn solving,\n\n$$\\pi = 0.0107\\, \\text{bar}$$",
