      "a": 3,
      "s": "JEE Main 2026 (Online) 6th April Morning Shift. Correct option: D. Let the mole fraction of the solvent be $ x_1 $ and that of the solute be $ x_2 $.\n\nGiven:\n\nMoles of solute $ n_2 = 0.25 $\n\nMoles of solvent $ n_1 = 1 $\n\n$ x_1 = \\frac{n_1}{n_1 + n_2} = \\frac{1}{1 + 0.25} = \\frac{1}{1.25} = 0.8 $\n\n$ x_2 = 1 - x_1 = 1 - 0.8 = 0.2 $\n\nFor a non-volatile solute, the vapor pressure of the solution is given by:\n\n$ P_{\\text{solution}} = x_1 P^0 $\n\nwhere $ P^0 $ is the vapor pressure of the pure solvent.\n\n$ \\frac{P_{\\text{solution}}}{P^0} \\times 100 = x_1 \\times 100 = 0.8 \\times 100 = 80\\% $\n\nFinal Answer:\n\n$ x = 80\\% $\n\nOption D: 80%",
