      "a": 1,
      "s": "JEE Main 2026 (Online) 6th April Morning Shift. Correct option: B. Let the oxide of iron contain 100 g of the compound.\n\nThen,\n\nMass of Fe = 69.9 g\n\nMass of O = 100 − 69.9 = 30.1 g\n\nCalculate moles of each element\n\n$ \\text{Moles of Fe} = \\frac{69.9}{56} = 1.248 $\n\n$ \\text{Moles of O} = \\frac{30.1}{16} = 1.881 $\n\nFind the simplest whole-number ratio\n\nDivide each by the smaller number (1.248):\n\n$ \\text{Ratio of Fe:O} = \\frac{1.248}{1.248} : \\frac{1.881}{1.248} = 1 : 1.51 $\n\nThis ratio is approximately 1 : 1.5 .\n\nTo remove the fraction, multiply both by 2 : $ \\text{Fe}_2\\text{O}_3 $\n\nIn $\\mathrm{Fe_2O_3}$,\n\nMass of Fe = $2 \\times 56 = 112$ g\n\nMass of O = $3 \\times 16 = 48$ g\n\nTotal mass = 160 g\n\nPercentage of Fe = $\\dfrac{112}{160} \\times 100 = 70\\%$ (approximately 69.9%)\n\nTherefore, the empirical formula of the oxide is\n\n$ \\boxed{\\mathrm{Fe_2O_3}} $\n\nCorrect Option: B.",
