      "s": "JEE Main 2025 (Online) 3rd April Morning Shift. Correct option: B. The limiting molar conductivities of ions are important in determining how well they conduct electricity in solution. Here are the values for some common cations at 298 K:\n\nH⁺: 349.8 S cm² mol⁻¹\n\nNa⁺: 50.11 S cm² mol⁻¹\n\nK⁺: 73.52 S cm² mol⁻¹\n\nCa²⁺: 119 S cm² mol⁻¹\n\nMg²⁺: 106.12 S cm² mol⁻¹\n\nBased on these values, the correct order of limiting molar conductivity for these cations is:\n\n$ \\stackrel{\\oplus}{\\text{H}}^+ > \\text{Ca}^{2+} > \\text{Mg}^{2+} > \\text{K}^+ > \\text{Na}^+ $\n\nThis order reflects the decreasing ability of each ion to conduct electricity in water under the given conditions.",
