      "s": "JEE Main 2026 (Online) 8th April Evening Shift. Correct option: B. The first-row transition metals use both their 3d and 4s electrons to form bonds with reactant molecules on the surface of the catalyst.\n\n∴ Statement I is incorrect.\n\nWhen reactants are adsorbed on the catalytic surface, their concentration on the surface increases, but this adsorption actually weakens the bonds within the reactant molecules. This helps in forming an activated complex and reduces the activation energy of the reaction.\n\n∴ Statement II is incorrect.",
