      "a": 1,
      "s": "JEE Main 2026 (Online) 5th April Morning Shift. Correct option: B. The main physical and chemical properties of interstitial compounds are :\n\n(1) They have very high melting points, even higher than the pure metals from which they are formed.\n\n(2) They are extremely hard. For example, some borides can be almost as hard as diamond.\n\n(3) They continue to show metallic conductivity, meaning they can conduct electricity like metals.\n\n(4) They are chemically inactive (inert) and often do not have a fixed composition, which is called being non-stoichiometric.",
      "source": "JEE Main 2026 (Online) 5th April Morning Shift | d & f Block | mnswhrr3",
