      "a": 0,
      "s": "JEE Main 2026 (Online) 2nd April Morning Shift. Correct option: A. In acidic medium, $\\mathrm{K_2Cr_2O_7}$ acts as a strong oxidising agent.\n\nIts orange colour is due to $\\mathrm{Cr_2O_7^{2-}}$, which gets reduced to green $\\mathrm{Cr^{3+}}$:\n\n$$ \\mathrm{Cr_2O_7^{2-} + 14H^+ + 6e^- \\rightarrow 2Cr^{3+} + 7H_2O} $$\n\nSo, the species that will change the orange colour must be reducing agents , because they will reduce dichromate to $\\mathrm{Cr^{3+}}$.\n\nNow check each option.\n\nOption A: $\\mathrm{Fe^{2+},\\ Sn^{2+},\\ I^-,\\ S^{2-}}$\n\n$\\mathrm{Fe^{2+} \\rightarrow Fe^{3+}}$ : reducing agent\n\n$\\mathrm{Sn^{2+} \\rightarrow Sn^{4+}}$ : reducing agent\n\n$\\mathrm{I^- \\rightarrow I_2}$ : reducing agent\n\n$\\mathrm{S^{2-}}$ : strong reducing agent\n\nAll these can reduce acidified dichromate, so all will change the orange colour.\n\nOption B: $\\mathrm{S^{2-},\\ Fe^{3+},\\ I^-,\\ C_2O_4^{2-}}$\n\n$\\mathrm{S^{2-}}$ : reducing agent\n\n$\\mathrm{Fe^{3+}}$ : not a reducing agent here\n\n$\\mathrm{I^-}$ : reducing agent\n\n$\\mathrm{C_2O_4^{2-}}$ : reducing agent\n\nSince $\\mathrm{Fe^{3+}}$ will not reduce dichromate, this option is incorrect.\n\nOption C: $\\mathrm{Fe^{2+},\\ NO_2^-,\\ SO_2,\\ Sn^{4+}}$\n\n$\\mathrm{Fe^{2+}}$ : reducing agent\n\n$\\mathrm{NO_2^-}$ : can act as reducing agent\n\n$\\mathrm{SO_2}$ : reducing agent\n\n$\\mathrm{Sn^{4+}}$ : already in higher oxidation state, not a reducing agent\n\nSo this option is incorrect.\n\nOption D: $\\mathrm{Fe^{3+},\\ SO_4^{2-},\\ S^{2-},\\ Sn^{4+}}$\n\n$\\mathrm{Fe^{3+}}$ : not reducing\n\n$\\mathrm{SO_4^{2-}}$ : not reducing\n\n$\\mathrm{S^{2-}}$ : reducing\n\n$\\mathrm{Sn^{4+}}$ : not reducing\n\nSo this is also incorrect.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is:\n\n$$ \\boxed{\\text{Option A}} $$",
      "source": "JEE Main 2026 (Online) 2nd April Morning Shift | d & f Block | mnrlrv1q",
