      "s": "JEE Main 2026 (Online) 2nd April Morning Shift. Correct option: D. The crystal field splitting energy (CFSE), represented by Δ₀, depends on how strong the ligands are and also on chelation (when a ligand forms a ring with the metal ion).\n\nThe stronger the ligand, the higher the value of Δ₀. Chelating ligands like ethylenediamine (en) also increase stability and splitting energy.\n\nAmong the given ligands, their strength follows this order:\n\n$$ \\mathrm{CN}^{-} > \\text{en} > \\mathrm{H_2O} > \\mathrm{F}^{-} $$\n\nThis order means complexes with CN⁻ have the largest Δ₀, and those with F⁻ have the smallest Δ₀.",
