      "q": "Identify the homoleptic complexes with odd number of $d$ electrons in the central metal :\n\n(A) $\\left[\\mathrm{FeO}_4\\right]^{2-}$\n\n(B) $\\left[\\mathrm{Fe}(\\mathrm{CN})_6\\right]^{3-}$\n\n(C) $\\left[\\mathrm{Fe}(\\mathrm{CN})_5 \\mathrm{NO}\\right]^{2-}$\n\n(D) $\\left[\\mathrm{CoCl}_4\\right]^{2-}$\n\n(E) $\\left[\\mathrm{Co}\\left(\\mathrm{H}_2 \\mathrm{O}\\right)_3 \\mathrm{~F}_3\\right]$\n\nChoose the correct answer from the options given below :",
      "qHtml": "<p>Identify the homoleptic complexes with odd number of $d$ electrons in the central metal :</p>\n<p>(A) $\\left[\\mathrm{FeO}_4\\right]^{2-}$</p>\n<p>(B) $\\left[\\mathrm{Fe}(\\mathrm{CN})_6\\right]^{3-}$</p>\n<p>(C) $\\left[\\mathrm{Fe}(\\mathrm{CN})_5 \\mathrm{NO}\\right]^{2-}$</p>\n<p>(D) $\\left[\\mathrm{CoCl}_4\\right]^{2-}$</p>\n<p>(E) $\\left[\\mathrm{Co}\\left(\\mathrm{H}_2 \\mathrm{O}\\right)_3 \\mathrm{~F}_3\\right]$</p>\n<p>Choose the <b>correct </b>answer from the options given below :</p>",
