      "s": "JEE Main 2025 (Online) 29th January Evening Shift. Correct option: A. Relation with HBr to give phenol\n\n(1)\n[Diagram: JEE Main 2025 (Online) 29th January Evening Shift Chemistry - Alcohols, Phenols and Ethers Question 21 English Explanation 1]\n\nThe reaction involves two steps,\n\n$\\star$) The lone pair of oxygen atom attacks on the hydrogen of HBr.\n\n$\\star$) The nucleophile Br$^-$ attacks on the methyl group which lead to the formation of phenol along with methyl bromide.\n\nPhenol is formed from this compound on reaction with HBr.\n\n(2)\n[Diagram: JEE Main 2025 (Online) 29th January Evening Shift Chemistry - Alcohols, Phenols and Ethers Question 21 English Explanation 2]\n\nNo phenol formation in this case because alkyl chain is attached to the benzene ring and on addition of H-Br, either H$^+$ or Br$^-$ get attached to this chain and no $-$OH group is formed as it is directly bonded to the benzene ring.\n\n(3)\n[Diagram: JEE Main 2025 (Online) 29th January Evening Shift Chemistry - Alcohols, Phenols and Ethers Question 21 English Explanation 3]\n\nNo phenol formation in this case. $-$OH group is formed as\n\n[Diagram: JEE Main 2025 (Online) 29th January Evening Shift Chemistry - Alcohols, Phenols and Ethers Question 21 English Explanation 4]\n\nSo, phenol product is formed in case of option (1) compound only.",
