      "a": 0,
      "s": "JEE Main 2023 (Online) 13th April Evening Shift. Correct option: A. Acidic strength $\\alpha-\\mathrm{I}$ effect\n\n$$\n\\alpha \\frac{1}{+\\mathrm{I}} \\text { effect }\n$$\n\n$\\mathrm{F}, \\mathrm{Cl}$ exerts $-\\mathrm{I}$ effect, Methyl exerts $+\\mathrm{I}$ effect, $\\mathrm{C}$ is least acidic.\n\nAmong $\\mathrm{A}$ and $\\mathrm{B}$; since inductive effect is distance dependent, Extent of $-\\mathrm{I}$ effect is higher in $\\mathrm{A}$ followed by $\\mathrm{B}$ even though $\\mathrm{F}$ is stronger electron withdrawing group than $\\mathrm{Cl}$. Thus, $\\mathrm{A}$ is more acidic than $\\mathrm{B}$.",
      "source": "JEE Main 2023 (Online) 13th April Evening Shift | Alcohols, Phenols & Ethers | 1lgp38f1x",
