      "s": "JEE Main 2025 (Online) 3rd April Morning Shift. Correct option: A. For the iodoform reaction, the compound must contain either:\n\na methyl ketone group:\n\n$$\\mathrm{R{-}CO{-}CH_3}$$\n\nor\n\nan alcohol which can be oxidised to a methyl ketone, that is:\n\n$$\\mathrm{CH_3{-}CH(OH){-}R}$$\n\nAlso, ethanol gives iodoform reaction because it gets oxidised to ethanal, and ethanal also gives the test.\n\nNow let us check each compound one by one.\n\n1. Ethanol\n\nStructure:\n\n$$\\mathrm{CH_3CH_2OH}$$\n\nIt gives iodoform reaction.\n\n2. Isopropyl alcohol\n\nStructure:\n\n$$\\mathrm{CH_3{-}CH(OH){-}CH_3}$$\n\nThis is a secondary alcohol of type\n\n$$\\mathrm{CH_3{-}CH(OH){-}R}$$\n\nSo it gives iodoform reaction.\n\n3. Bromoacetone\n\nStructure:\n\n$$\\mathrm{CH_3{-}CO{-}CH_2Br}$$\n\nIt contains the methyl ketone group\n\n$$\\mathrm{CH_3{-}CO{-}}$$\n\nSo it gives iodoform reaction.\n\n4. 2-Butanol\n\nStructure:\n\n$$\\mathrm{CH_3{-}CH(OH){-}CH_2CH_3}$$\n\nThis is of type\n\n$$\\mathrm{CH_3{-}CH(OH){-}R}$$\n\nSo it gives iodoform reaction.\n\n5. 2-Butanone\n\nStructure:\n\n$$\\mathrm{CH_3{-}CO{-}CH_2CH_3}$$\n\nThis is a methyl ketone.\n\nSo it gives iodoform reaction.\n\n6. Butanal\n\nStructure:\n\n$$\\mathrm{CH_3CH_2CH_2CHO}$$\n\nThis is an aldehyde, but not ethanal.\n\nSo it does not give iodoform reaction.\n\n7. 2-Pentanone\n\nStructure:\n\n$$\\mathrm{CH_3{-}CO{-}CH_2CH_2CH_3}$$\n\nThis is a methyl ketone.\n\nSo it gives iodoform reaction.\n\n8. 3-Pentanone\n\nStructure:\n\n$$\\mathrm{CH_3CH_2{-}CO{-}CH_2CH_3}$$\n\nThere is no\n\n$$\\mathrm{CH_3{-}CO{-}}$$\n\ngroup directly attached to carbonyl carbon.\n\nSo it does not give iodoform reaction.\n\n9. Pentanal\n\nStructure:\n\n$$\\mathrm{CH_3CH_2CH_2CH_2CHO}$$\n\nThis is an aldehyde, but not ethanal.\n\nSo it does not give iodoform reaction.\n\n10. 3-Pentanol\n\nStructure:\n\n$$\\mathrm{CH_3CH_2{-}CH(OH){-}CH_2CH_3}$$\n\nThe carbon having $-OH$ is not attached to a $CH_3$ group in the required way. On oxidation it forms 3-pentanone, which is not a methyl ketone.\n\nSo it does not give iodoform reaction.\n\nCompounds which do not give iodoform reaction:\n\nButanal\n\n3-Pentanone\n\nPentanal\n\n3-Pentanol\n\nTotal number:\n\n$$4$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is:\n\n$$\\boxed{4}$$\n\nSo, Option A is correct.",
