      "a": 3,
      "s": "JEE Main 2026 (Online) 4th April Morning Shift. Correct option: D. Maltose and lactose are both disaccharides .\n\nIn each of these structures, one anomeric carbon is used to form the glycosidic linkage , but the other anomeric carbon remains free as a hemiacetal (–OH at anomeric carbon) .\n\nIf a disaccharide has a free hemiacetal group , it can open up to the open-chain form and can reduce mild oxidising agents (like Tollens’ reagent or Fehling’s solution).\n\nTherefore, both maltose and lactose are reducing sugars because both contain a hemiacetal linkage (free anomeric carbon) .",
