      "s": "JEE Main 2026 (Online) 2nd April Morning Shift. Correct option: C. Vitamin B$_1$ : The chemical name for Vitamin B$_1$ is Thiamine. Its deficiency in the human body can lead to a disease known as Beri-Beri.\n\nTherefore, A matches with III.\n\nVitamin B$_2$ : The chemical name for Vitamin B$_2$ is Riboflavin. A deficiency in this vitamin leads to cheilosis, which is the fissuring at the corners of the mouth and lips.\n\nTherefore, B matches with IV.\n\nVitamin B$_6$ : The chemical name for Vitamin B$_6$ is Pyridoxine. Its deficiency can cause convulsions.\n\nTherefore, C matches with I.\n\nVitamin C : The chemical name for Vitamin C is Ascorbic acid. It is a water-soluble vitamin found in citrus fruits, and its deficiency causes Scurvy (bleeding gums).\n\nTherefore, D matches with II.\n\nNow, let us combine our findings:\n\nA $\\rightarrow$ III\n\nB $\\rightarrow$ IV\n\nC $\\rightarrow$ I\n\nD $\\rightarrow$ II\n\nLooking at the options provided, the sequence A-III, B-IV, C-I, D-II perfectly matches Option C.\n\nOption C is the correct answer.",
