      "a": 0,
      "s": "JEE Main 2023 (Online) 13th April Evening Shift. Correct option: A. Among the given options, arginine, histidine, and lysine are all basic amino acids because they contain amino (-NH 2 ) and imino (-NH=) functional groups that can accept a proton (H + ) to become positively charged.\n\nAsparagine, on the other hand, contains an amide (-CONH 2 ) functional group instead of an imino group. This functional group is not basic because it does not have a proton that can be easily removed. Therefore, the answer is: asparagine.",
