      "s": "JEE Main 2026 (Online) 5th April Evening Shift. Correct option: C. (A) The stability of a complex increases when the ligand is stronger (i.e., stronger field/stronger bonding ligand gives more stable complex).\n\nThe ligand strength order given is:\n\n$$ \\mathrm{SCN}^{-}<\\mathrm{OH}^{-}<\\mathrm{C}_2 \\mathrm{OH}_4^{-2} $$\n\nAlso, $\\mathrm{C}_2 \\mathrm{O}_4^{-2}$ (oxalate) is a bidentate ligand. Because of the chelate effect , complexes with bidentate ligands are generally more stable.\n\nSo, $\\left[\\mathrm{Fe}\\left(\\mathrm{C}_2 \\mathrm{O}_4\\right)_3\\right]^{3-}$ is the most stable among the given complexes. Hence, statement (A) is true.\n\n(B) en (ethylenediamine) is also a chelating (bidentate) ligand, while $\\mathrm{NH}_3$ is monodentate (non-chelating).\n\nDue to the chelate effect, $\\left[\\mathrm{Cu}(\\mathrm{en})_2\\right]^{2+}$ is more stable than $\\left[\\mathrm{Cu}\\left(\\mathrm{NH}_3\\right)_4\\right]^{2+}$.\n\nSo, statement (B) is false.\n\n$$ \\begin{aligned}(c)\\,\\,\\, & {\\left[\\mathrm{Fe}(\\mathrm{CN})_6\\right]^{-4}} \\\\ & \\mathrm{Fe}^{+2}=4 \\mathrm{~s}^{\\circ} \\text { 3d }{ }^6 \\end{aligned} $$\n\n$C N^{-}=$ strong field ligand, so it forms a low spin complex.\n\n[Diagram: JEE Main 2026 (Online) 5th April Evening Shift Chemistry - Coordination Compounds Question 7 English Explanation 1]\n\nBecause $\\mathrm{CN^-}$ is a strong field ligand, electrons pair up in the $3d$ orbitals. This leads to an inner orbital complex with $d^2sp^3$ hybridisation for Fe.\n\nSo, statement (C) is true.\n\n(D) $\\left[\\mathrm{Fe}\\left(\\mathrm{NO}_2\\right)_3 \\mathrm{Cl}_3\\right]^{-2}$ and $\\left[\\mathrm{Fe}(0 \\mathrm{NO})_3 \\mathrm{Cl}_3\\right]^{-2}$\n\nLinkage isomerism is shown when an ambidentate ligand can donate electrons through two different atoms.\n\n[Diagram: JEE Main 2026 (Online) 5th April Evening Shift Chemistry - Coordination Compounds Question 7 English Explanation 2]\n\nHere, $\\mathrm{NO_2^-}$ can coordinate through N (nitro) or through O (nitrito). Therefore, the complex shows linkage isomerism.\n\nSo, statement (D) is true.\n\n(E) $\\mathrm{NO}_2^{-}$ and $\\mathrm{SCN}^{-}$ are ambidentate ligands (they can attach through different atoms).\n\n$S$-donor $\\leftarrow S=C=N^{\\ominus} \\rightarrow N$-donor\n\n[Diagram: JEE Main 2026 (Online) 5th April Evening Shift Chemistry - Coordination Compounds Question 7 English Explanation 3]\n\nSo, the statement “$\\mathrm{NO}_2^{-}$ and $\\mathrm{SCN}^{-}$ ligands are NOT ambidentate ligands” is incorrect.\n\nHence, statement (E) is false.",
      "source": "JEE Main 2026 (Online) 5th April Evening Shift | Practical Chemistry | mnswhrpf",
      "pyq": true,
      "exactPaperText": true,
      "pyqSourceSlug": "coordination-compounds"
