      "s": "JEE Main 2026 (Online) 5th April Evening Shift. Correct option: D. Since there are $39$ arithmetic means between $59$ and $159$, the full arithmetic progression has\n\n$$ 59, A_1, A_2, A_3, \\ldots, A_{39}, 159 $$\n\nSo total number of terms is\n\n$$ 39+2=41 $$\n\nHence, the number of intervals is\n\n$$ 41-1=40 $$\n\nTherefore, the common difference is\n\n$$ d=\\frac{159-59}{40}=\\frac{100}{40}=2.5 $$\n\nNow the terms are:\n\n$$ A_1=59+2.5=61.5 $$\n\nIn general,\n\n$$ A_n=59+n(2.5) $$\n\nNow find the required terms:\n\n$$ A_{25}=59+25(2.5)=59+62.5=121.5 $$\n\n$$ A_{28}=59+28(2.5)=59+70=129 $$\n\n$$ A_{31}=59+31(2.5)=59+77.5=136.5 $$\n\n$$ A_{36}=59+36(2.5)=59+90=149 $$\n\nNow their mean is\n\n$$ \\frac{A_{25}+A_{28}+A_{31}+A_{36}}{4} = \\frac{121.5+129+136.5+149}{4} $$\n\n$$ = \\frac{536}{4}=134 $$\n\nSo the correct answer is:\n\n$$ \\boxed{134} $$\n\nHence, Option D is correct.",
