      "s": "JEE Main 2026 (Online) 8th April Evening Shift. Correct option: C. $\\boldsymbol{S}_{\\boldsymbol{r}}=26\\left[\\left(\\frac{2^3}{3}\\right) \\cdot\\left({ }^{12} \\boldsymbol{C}_2\\right)+\\left(\\frac{2^5}{5}\\right) \\cdot\\left({ }^{12} \\boldsymbol{C}_4\\right)+\\left(\\frac{2^7}{7}\\right) \\cdot\\left({ }^{12} \\boldsymbol{C}_6\\right)+\\left(\\frac{2^9}{9}\\right) \\cdot\\left({ }^{12} \\boldsymbol{C}_8\\right)+\\ldots .+\\left(\\frac{2^{13}}{13}\\right) \\cdot\\left({ }^{12} \\boldsymbol{C}_{12}\\right)\\right]$\n\n$=26\\left[\\sum\\limits_{r=1}^6\\left(\\frac{2^{2 r+1}}{2 r+1}\\right) \\cdot\\left({ }^{12} \\boldsymbol{C}_{2 r}\\right)\\right]$.\n\n$\\boldsymbol{S}_{\\boldsymbol{r}}=\\frac{26}{13}\\left[\\sum\\limits_{r=1}^6\\left(2^{2 r+1}\\right) \\cdot\\left({ }^{13} \\boldsymbol{C}_{2 r+1}\\right)\\right]$\n\n$=2\\left[\\sum\\limits_{r=0}^6\\left(2^{2 r+1}\\right) \\cdot\\left({ }^{13} \\boldsymbol{C}_{2 r+1}\\right)-\\left({ }^{13} \\boldsymbol{C}_1\\right) \\cdot 2^1\\right]$\n\n$=2\\left[\\sum\\limits_{r=0}^6\\left(2^{2 r+1}\\right) \\cdot\\left({ }^{13} C_{2 r+1}\\right)\\right]-52$\n\n$\\begin{aligned} \\boldsymbol{S}_{\\boldsymbol{r}} & =2\\left[\\left({ }^{13} \\boldsymbol{C}_1\\right) \\cdot 2^1+\\left({ }^{13} \\boldsymbol{C}_3\\right) \\cdot 2^3+\\left({ }^{13} \\boldsymbol{C}_5\\right) \\cdot 2^5+\\left({ }^{13} \\boldsymbol{C}_7\\right) \\cdot 2^7+\\ldots . .+\\left({ }^{13} \\boldsymbol{C}_{13}\\right) \\cdot 2^{13}\\right]-52 \\\\ & =(1+2)^{13}-(1-2)^{13}-52 \\\\ & =3^{13}+1-52 \\\\ & =3^{13}-51.....(i)\\end{aligned}$\n\n$$ \\boldsymbol{S}_r=26\\left[\\left(\\frac{2^3}{3}\\right) \\cdot\\left({ }^{12} \\boldsymbol{C}_2\\right)+\\left(\\frac{2^5}{5}\\right) \\cdot\\left({ }^{12} \\boldsymbol{C}_4\\right)+\\left(\\frac{2^7}{7}\\right) \\cdot\\left({ }^{12} \\boldsymbol{C}_6\\right)+\\left(\\frac{2^9}{9}\\right) \\cdot\\left({ }^{12} \\boldsymbol{C}_8\\right)+\\ldots .+\\left(\\frac{2^{13}}{13}\\right) \\cdot\\left({ }^{12} \\boldsymbol{C}_{12}\\right)\\right]=3^{13}-\\boldsymbol{\\alpha} \\ldots . (ii)$$\n\nFrom the equivalence relationship between equation $(\\boldsymbol{i})$ and $(\\boldsymbol{i i})$ we conclude $\\alpha=51$",
