      "q": "Let the smallest value of $k \\in \\mathbb{N}$, for which the coefficient of $x^3$ in $(1+x)^3+(1+x)^4+(1+x)^5+\\ldots+(1+x)^{99}+(1+k x)^{100}, x \\neq 0$, is $\\left(43 n+\\frac{101}{4}\\right)\\left({ }^{100} \\mathrm{C}_3\\right)$ for some $n \\in \\mathrm{~N}$, be $p$. Then the value of $p+n$ is :",
      "qHtml": "<p>Let the smallest value of $k \\in \\mathbb{N}$, for which the coefficient of $x^3$ in $(1+x)^3+(1+x)^4+(1+x)^5+\\ldots+(1+x)^{99}+(1+k x)^{100}, x \\neq 0$, is $\\left(43 n+\\frac{101}{4}\\right)\\left({ }^{100} \\mathrm{C}_3\\right)$ for some $n \\in \\mathrm{~N}$, be $p$. Then the value of $p+n$ is :</p>",
