      "q": "For the function $f:[1, \\infty) \\rightarrow[1, \\infty)$ defined by $f(x)=(x-1)^4+1$, among the two statements:\n\n(I) The set $\\mathrm{S}=\\left\\{x \\in[1, \\infty): f(x)=f^{-1}(x)\\right\\}$ contains exactly two elements, and\n\n(II) The set $\\mathrm{S}=\\left\\{x \\in[1, \\infty): f(x)=f^{-1}(x+1)\\right\\}$ is an empty set,",
      "qHtml": "<p>For the function $f:[1, \\infty) \\rightarrow[1, \\infty)$ defined by $f(x)=(x-1)^4+1$, among the two statements:</p>\n<p>(I) The set $\\mathrm{S}=\\left\\{x \\in[1, \\infty): f(x)=f^{-1}(x)\\right\\}$ contains exactly two elements, and</p>\n<p>(II) The set $\\mathrm{S}=\\left\\{x \\in[1, \\infty): f(x)=f^{-1}(x+1)\\right\\}$ is an empty set,</p>",
