      "a": 1,
      "s": "JEE Main 2026 (Online) 4th April Morning Shift. Correct option: B. Total number of functions from $\\{1,2,3,4\\}$ to $\\{a,b,c\\}$ is\n\n$$ 3^4=81 $$\n\nNow we find the number of onto functions.\n\nFor a function to be onto, all the three elements $a,b,c$ must appear as images of elements of $\\{1,2,3,4\\}$.\n\nUsing inclusion-exclusion principle:\n\nTotal functions: $3^4=81$\n\nLet\n\n$A$ = functions missing $a$\n\n$B$ = functions missing $b$\n\n$C$ = functions missing $c$\n\nIf one element is missing, then the function goes into only $2$ elements.\n\nSo,\n\n$$ |A|=|B|=|C|=2^4=16 $$\n\nHence,\n\n$$ |A|+|B|+|C|=3\\times 16=48 $$\n\nIf two elements are missing, then all $4$ elements of domain must go to only one element of codomain.\n\nSo,\n\n$$ |A\\cap B|=|B\\cap C|=|C\\cap A|=1^4=1 $$\n\nThus,\n\n$$ |A\\cap B|+|B\\cap C|+|C\\cap A|=3 $$\n\nIf all three are missing, that is impossible, so\n\n$$ |A\\cap B\\cap C|=0 $$\n\nTherefore, number of functions which are not onto is\n\n$$ |A\\cup B\\cup C|=48-3=45 $$\n\nSo the correct answer is\n\n$$ \\boxed{45} $$\n\nHence, Option B is correct.",
