      "a": 1,
      "s": "JEE Main 2026 (Online) 6th April Morning Shift. Correct option: B. For the function\n\n$$ f(x)=\\sin^{-1}\\left(\\frac{x+[x]}{3}\\right), $$\n\nthe expression inside $\\sin^{-1}$ must lie between $-1$ and $1$.\n\nSo, we need\n\n$$ -1 \\le \\frac{x+[x]}{3} \\le 1 $$\n\nMultiplying throughout by $3$,\n\n$$ -3 \\le x+[x] \\le 3 $$\n\nNow let\n\n$$ [x]=n $$\n\nThen by definition of greatest integer function,\n\n$$ n \\le x and so\n\n$$ x+[x]=x+n $$\n\nHence the condition becomes\n\n$$ -3 \\le x+n \\le 3 $$\n\nBut since $x \\in [n,n+1)$, let us check possible integer values of $n$.\n\nCase 1: $n=-2$\n\nThen\n\n$$ x \\in [-2,-1) $$\n\nand\n\n$$ x+[x]=x-2 $$\n\nSince $x \\in [-2,-1)$,\n\n$$ x-2 \\in [-4,-3) $$\n\nThis does not satisfy $-3 \\le x+[x]$ except at $x=-1$, but $-1 \\notin [-2,-1)$.\n\nSo no value from this interval is allowed.\n\nCase 2: $n=-1$\n\nThen\n\n$$ x \\in [-1,0) $$\n\nand\n\n$$ x+[x]=x-1 $$\n\nSo\n\n$$ x-1 \\in [-2,-1) $$\n\nThis lies completely within $[-3,3]$.\n\nHence all $x \\in [-1,0)$ are allowed.\n\nCase 3: $n=0$\n\nThen\n\n$$ x \\in [0,1) $$\n\nand\n\n$$ x+[x]=x $$\n\nSo\n\n$$ x \\in [0,1) $$\n\nThis also lies within $[-3,3]$.\n\nHence all $x \\in [0,1)$ are allowed.\n\nCase 4: $n=1$\n\nThen\n\n$$ x \\in [1,2) $$\n\nand\n\n$$ x+[x]=x+1 $$\n\nSo\n\n$$ x+1 \\in [2,3) $$\n\nThis lies within $[-3,3]$.\n\nHence all $x \\in [1,2)$ are allowed.\n\nCase 5: $n=2$\n\nThen\n\n$$ x \\in [2,3) $$\n\nand\n\n$$ x+[x]=x+2 $$\n\nSo\n\n$$ x+2 \\in [4,5) $$\n\nThis exceeds $3$, so no value is allowed.\n\nNow let us also check the boundary points:\n\nAt $x=-\\dfrac{3}{2}$, actually $[x]=-2$, so this does not help.\n\nBetter to solve more carefully near the ends.\n\nWe want the full set of $x$ satisfying\n\n$$ -3 \\le x+[x] \\le 3 $$\n\nLet $x \\in [n,n+1)$, so $[x]=n$.\n\nThen\n\n$$ -3 \\le x+n \\le 3 $$\n\nwhich gives\n\n$$ -3-n \\le x \\le 3-n $$\n\nTogether with $n \\le x $$ [n,n+1) \\cap [-3-n,\\,3-n]. $$\n\nNow check relevant integers:\n\nFor $n=-2$\n\n$$ x \\in [-2,-1) \\cap [-1,5] = \\{-1\\} $$\n\nbut $-1$ is not included in $[-2,-1)$, so no solution.\n\nFor $n=-1$\n\n$$ x \\in [-1,0) \\cap [-2,4] = [-1,0) $$\n\nFor $n=0$\n\n$$ x \\in [0,1) \\cap [-3,3] = [0,1) $$\n\nFor $n=1$\n\n$$ x \\in [1,2) \\cap [-4,2] = [1,2) $$\n\nFor $n=2$\n\n$$ x \\in [2,3) \\cap [-5,1] = \\varnothing $$\n\nThus domain is\n\n$$ [-1,0)\\cup [0,1)\\cup [1,2)=[-1,2) $$\n\nSo,\n\n$$ \\alpha=-1,\\qquad \\beta=2 $$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$ \\alpha^2+\\beta^2=(-1)^2+2^2=1+4=5 $$\n\nHence the correct answer is\n\n$$ \\boxed{5} $$\n\nSo, Option B is correct.",
      "source": "JEE Main 2026 (Online) 6th April Morning Shift | Functions | mnswhq5g",
      "pyq": true,
