      "s": "JEE Main 2026 (Online) 5th April Evening Shift. Correct option: D. Given the quadratic equation\n\n$$ z^2+4z-(1+12i)=0 $$\n\nlet its roots be $z_1$ and $z_2$.\n\nWe need to find\n\n$$ |z_1|^2+|z_2|^2 $$\n\nUsing Vieta’s formulas for\n\n$$ az^2+bz+c=0, $$\n\nwe have\n\n$$ z_1+z_2=-\\frac{b}{a}=-4 $$\n\nand\n\n$$ z_1z_2=\\frac{c}{a}=-(1+12i)=-1-12i $$\n\nNow solve the equation to identify the roots.\n\n$$ z^2+4z-(1+12i)=0 $$\n\nUsing the quadratic formula,\n\n$$ z=\\frac{-4\\pm\\sqrt{16+4(1+12i)}}{2} $$\n\n$$ z=\\frac{-4\\pm\\sqrt{20+48i}}{2} $$\n\nNow observe that\n\n$$ (6+4i)^2=36+48i-16=20+48i $$\n\nSo,\n\n$$ \\sqrt{20+48i}=6+4i $$\n\nHence the roots are\n\n$$ z_1=\\frac{-4+(6+4i)}{2}=1+2i $$\n\nand\n\n$$ z_2=\\frac{-4-(6+4i)}{2}=-5-2i $$\n\nNow compute their moduli squared:\n\n$$ |z_1|^2=|1+2i|^2=1^2+2^2=5 $$\n\n$$ |z_2|^2=|-5-2i|^2=(-5)^2+(-2)^2=25+4=29 $$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$ |z_1|^2+|z_2|^2=5+29=34 $$\n\nSo the correct answer is\n\n$$ \\boxed{34} $$\n\nHence, Option D is correct.",
