      "s": "JEE Main 2026 (Online) 4th April Morning Shift. Correct option: A. Let\n\n$$ z = x + iy $$\n\nwhere $x, y \\in \\mathbb{R}$.\n\nWe are given:\n\n$$ |z+2| = |z-2| $$\n\nand\n\n$$ \\arg\\left(\\frac{z+3}{z-i}\\right)=\\frac{\\pi}{4} $$\n\nWe will use these one by one.\n\n1. Using $|z+2| = |z-2|$\n\nSubstitute $z = x+iy$:\n\n$$ |x+iy+2| = |x+iy-2| $$\n\nSo,\n\n$$ \\sqrt{(x+2)^2+y^2} = \\sqrt{(x-2)^2+y^2} $$\n\nSquaring both sides:\n\n$$ (x+2)^2 + y^2 = (x-2)^2 + y^2 $$\n\n$$ x^2+4x+4 = x^2-4x+4 $$\n\n$$ 8x = 0 $$\n\n$$ x = 0 $$\n\nHence,\n\n$$ z = iy $$\n\nSo the point lies on the imaginary axis.\n\n2. Using the argument condition\n\nNow,\n\n$$ \\frac{z+3}{z-i} = \\frac{3+iy}{i(y-1)} $$\n\nWe are given that its argument is $\\dfrac{\\pi}{4}$.\n\nA complex number has argument $\\dfrac{\\pi}{4}$ when its real and imaginary parts are equal and positive in sign together.\n\nLet us simplify:\n\n$$ \\frac{3+iy}{i(y-1)} $$\n\nSince $\\dfrac{1}{i} = -i$, we get\n\n$$ \\frac{3+iy}{i(y-1)} = \\frac{-i(3+iy)}{y-1} $$\n\nNow expand:\n\n$$ -i(3+iy) = -3i - i^2y = y - 3i $$\n\nSo,\n\n$$ \\frac{z+3}{z-i} = \\frac{y-3i}{y-1} = \\frac{y}{y-1} - i\\frac{3}{y-1} $$\n\nThus real part is\n\n$$ \\frac{y}{y-1} $$\n\nand imaginary part is\n\n$$ -\\frac{3}{y-1} $$\n\nSince argument is $\\dfrac{\\pi}{4}$, we need\n\n$$ \\frac{\\text{imaginary part}}{\\text{real part}} = \\tan\\frac{\\pi}{4} = 1 $$\n\nSo,\n\n$$ \\frac{-\\frac{3}{y-1}}{\\frac{y}{y-1}} = 1 $$\n\n$$ -\\frac{3}{y} = 1 $$\n\n$$ y = -3 $$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$ z = -3i $$\n\n3. Find $|z|^2$\n\n$$ |z|^2 = 0^2 + (-3)^2 = 9 $$\n\nSo,\n\n$$ \\boxed{9} $$\n\nHence, the correct option is Option A .",
