      "s": "JEE Main 2026 (Online) 2nd April Evening Shift. Correct option: C. [Diagram: JEE Main 2026 (Online) 2nd April Evening Shift Mathematics - Complex Numbers Question 8 English Explanation]\n\n$$ \\begin{aligned} & |z|=r \\\\ & O A=r \\end{aligned} $$\n\nStep 1: Circle $C_1:|z|=r$ has centre $O(0,0)$ and radius $r$ (so $OA=r$).\n\nStep 2: Circle $C_2:|z-3-4i|=5$ has centre at the point $(3,4)$ and radius $5$.\n\nStep 3: Distance between the centres is\n\n$$OC=\\sqrt{3^2+4^2}=5$$\n\nStep 4: Since $C_2$ lies completely inside $C_1$, the minimum distance between a point $z_1$ on $C_1$ and a point $z_2$ on $C_2$ happens when the two points are on the same line through the centres, on the nearest sides.\n\nSo,\n\nminimum $\\left|\\mathrm{z}_1-\\mathrm{z}_2\\right|= r-(OC+5)=r-(5+5)=r-10$\n\nGiven minimum $\\left|\\mathrm{z}_1-\\mathrm{z}_2\\right|=2$, we get\n\n$$ \\Rightarrow r-10=2 \\Rightarrow r=12 $$\n\nStep 5: The maximum distance $\\left|z_1-z_2\\right|$ happens when $z_1$ and $z_2$ are on opposite sides along the same line through the centres.\n\nThen the farthest distance is\n\n$$ \\left|z_1-z_2\\right|= r+(OC+5)=r+10 $$\n\nSubstituting $r=12$,\n\n$$ \\left|z_1-z_2\\right|=12+10=22 $$",
