      "s": "JEE Main 2026 (Online) 8th April Evening Shift. Correct option: A. 1. A series sum is defined : $\\boldsymbol{\\alpha}=3+4+8+9+13+14+\\ldots . . \\boldsymbol{t}_{40}$\n\n2. $(\\tan \\boldsymbol{\\beta})^{\\frac{\\alpha}{1020}}$ is a root of the quadratic equation $\\boldsymbol{x}^2+\\boldsymbol{x}-2=0$ where $\\boldsymbol{\\beta} \\in\\left(0, \\frac{\\boldsymbol{\\pi}}{2}\\right)$\n\n3. To evaluate the expression $\\sin ^2 \\beta+3 \\cos ^2 \\beta$\n\n$$\\therefore $$ $\\boldsymbol{\\alpha}=3+4+8+9+13+14+\\ldots . . \\boldsymbol{t}_{40}$\n\n$=7+17+27+\\ldots . .+\\boldsymbol{T}_{20}$\n\n$=\\frac{20}{2}\\{(2) \\cdot(7)+(20-1) \\cdot(10)\\}$\n\n$=(10) \\cdot(14+190)=2,040 \\ldots \\ldots(\\boldsymbol{i})$\n\nEquation (i) gives the value of $\\alpha=2,040$ :\n\n$$ (\\tan \\beta)^{\\frac{\\alpha}{1020}}=(\\tan \\beta)^{\\frac{2040}{1020}}=\\tan ^2 \\beta \\ldots \\ldots(i i) $$\n\nNow let us solve the quadratic equation $x^2+x-2=0$ :\n\n$x^2+x-2=0 \\Rightarrow x^2+2 x-x-2=0 \\Rightarrow(x+2)(x-1)=0$\n\n$$ \\Rightarrow \\begin{array}{|l|l|} \\hline p & q \\\\ \\hline-2 & 1 \\\\ \\hline \\end{array} $$\n\nwhere $\\boldsymbol{p}$ and $\\boldsymbol{q}$ are the roots\n\nWe have derived in equation $(i i)(\\tan \\beta)^{\\frac{\\alpha}{1020}}=\\tan ^2 \\beta$ which is also a root of the equation $x^2+x-2=0$ :\n\nFrom the pair of roots we get $\\tan ^2 \\beta$ =1$ \\Rightarrow \\tan \\beta= \\pm 1 $ As $ \\tan ^2 \\beta \\geqslant 0$ always\n\n$\\boldsymbol{\\beta} \\in\\left(0, \\frac{\\pi}{2}\\right) \\Rightarrow \\tan \\boldsymbol{\\beta}=1 \\Rightarrow \\boldsymbol{\\beta}=\\frac{\\pi}{4}$\n\n$\\Rightarrow \\sin ^2 \\beta+3 \\cos ^2 \\beta=\\sin ^2 \\frac{\\pi}{4}+3 \\cos ^2 \\frac{\\pi}{4}=\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)+\\left(\\frac{3}{2}\\right)=2$",
