      "s": "JEE Main 2026 (Online) 6th April Morning Shift. Correct option: B. We need to find\n\n$$ 1^3-2^3+3^3-4^3+\\cdots+15^3 $$\n\nThis is an alternating sum of cubes.\n\nLet us group the terms in pairs:\n\n$$ (1^3-2^3)+(3^3-4^3)+(5^3-6^3)+\\cdots+(13^3-14^3)+15^3 $$\n\nNow calculate each pair:\n\n$$ 1^3-2^3=1-8=-7 $$\n\n$$ 3^3-4^3=27-64=-37 $$\n\n$$ 5^3-6^3=125-216=-91 $$\n\n$$ 7^3-8^3=343-512=-169 $$\n\n$$ 9^3-10^3=729-1000=-271 $$\n\n$$ 11^3-12^3=1331-1728=-397 $$\n\n$$ 13^3-14^3=2197-2744=-547 $$\n\nAlso,\n\n$$ 15^3=3375 $$\n\nNow add all these:\n\n$$ -7-37-91-169-271-397-547+3375 $$\n\nFirst add the negative terms:\n\n$$ 7+37+91+169+271+397+547=1519 $$\n\nSo,\n\n$$ 3375-1519=1856 $$\n\nHence, the value is\n\n$$ \\boxed{1856} $$\n\nSo, the correct option is B .",
