      "s": "JEE Main 2026 (Online) 5th April Morning Shift. Correct option: C. Given that the sum of the first $n$ terms of the A.P. is\n\n$$ S_n = 3n^2 + 5n $$\n\nWe know that the $n$th term of the A.P. is\n\n$$ a_n = S_n - S_{n-1} $$\n\nSo first find $S_{n-1}$:\n\n$$ S_{n-1} = 3(n-1)^2 + 5(n-1) $$\n\nNow expand:\n\n$$ S_{n-1} = 3(n^2 - 2n + 1) + 5n - 5 $$\n\n$$ S_{n-1} = 3n^2 - 6n + 3 + 5n - 5 $$\n\n$$ S_{n-1} = 3n^2 - n - 2 $$\n\nNow,\n\n$$ a_n = S_n - S_{n-1} $$\n\n$$ a_n = (3n^2 + 5n) - (3n^2 - n - 2) $$\n\n$$ a_n = 6n + 2 $$\n\nSo the A.P. has terms:\n\n$$ a_1 = 6(1) + 2 = 8 $$\n\nand common difference\n\n$$ d = 6 $$\n\nThus the first 10 terms are:\n\n$$ 8,\\ 14,\\ 20,\\ 26,\\ 32,\\ 38,\\ 44,\\ 50,\\ 56,\\ 62 $$\n\nNow we need the sum of their squares:\n\n$$ 8^2 + 14^2 + 20^2 + 26^2 + 32^2 + 38^2 + 44^2 + 50^2 + 56^2 + 62^2 $$\n\nCalculate one by one:\n\n$$ 8^2 = 64 $$\n\n$$ 14^2 = 196 $$\n\n$$ 20^2 = 400 $$\n\n$$ 26^2 = 676 $$\n\n$$ 32^2 = 1024 $$\n\n$$ 38^2 = 1444 $$\n\n$$ 44^2 = 1936 $$\n\n$$ 50^2 = 2500 $$\n\n$$ 56^2 = 3136 $$\n\n$$ 62^2 = 3844 $$\n\nNow add:\n\n$$ 64 + 196 = 260 $$\n\n$$ 260 + 400 = 660 $$\n\n$$ 660 + 676 = 1336 $$\n\n$$ 1336 + 1024 = 2360 $$\n\n$$ 2360 + 1444 = 3804 $$\n\n$$ 3804 + 1936 = 5740 $$\n\n$$ 5740 + 2500 = 8240 $$\n\n$$ 8240 + 3136 = 11376 $$\n\n$$ 11376 + 3844 = 15220 $$\n\nTherefore, the sum of squares of the first 10 terms is\n\n$$ \\boxed{15220} $$\n\nSo, the correct option is Option C .",
