      "a": 2,
      "s": "JEE Main 2026 (Online) 2nd April Evening Shift. Correct option: C. Given\n\n$$ {^{30}C_{30-r}} + 3{^{30}C_{31-r}} + 3{^{30}C_{32-r}} + {^{30}C_{33-r}} = {^mC_r} $$\n\nfor $3 \\le r \\le 30$.\n\nWe have to find $m$.\n\nFirst, use the symmetry property of combinations:\n\n$$ {^nC_k} = {^nC_{n-k}} $$\n\nSo,\n\n$$ {^{30}C_{30-r}} = {^{30}C_r} $$\n\n$$ {^{30}C_{31-r}} = {^{30}C_{r-1}} $$\n\nbecause\n\n$$ 30-(31-r)=r-1 $$\n\nSimilarly,\n\n$$ {^{30}C_{32-r}} = {^{30}C_{r-2}} $$\n\nand\n\n$$ {^{30}C_{33-r}} = {^{30}C_{r-3}} $$\n\nTherefore the left-hand side becomes\n\n$$ {^{30}C_r} + 3{^{30}C_{r-1}} + 3{^{30}C_{r-2}} + {^{30}C_{r-3}} $$\n\nNow notice the coefficients:\n\n$$ 1,\\ 3,\\ 3,\\ 1 $$\n\nThese are the binomial coefficients in the expansion of\n\n$$ (1+x)^3 $$\n\nAlso, by Vandermonde’s identity,\n\n$$ {^{30}C_r} + 3{^{30}C_{r-1}} + 3{^{30}C_{r-2}} + {^{30}C_{r-3}} = {^{33}C_r} $$\n\nLet us see this through binomial expansion:\n\nCoefficient of $x^r$ in $(1+x)^{33}$ is\n\n$$ {^{33}C_r} $$\n\nBut\n\n$$ (1+x)^{33} = (1+x)^{30}(1+x)^3 $$\n\nand\n\n$$ (1+x)^3 = 1 + 3x + 3x^2 + x^3 $$\n\nSo coefficient of $x^r$ in $(1+x)^{30}(1+3x+3x^2+x^3)$ is\n\n$$ {^{30}C_r} + 3{^{30}C_{r-1}} + 3{^{30}C_{r-2}} + {^{30}C_{r-3}} $$\n\nHence,\n\n$$ {^{30}C_r} + 3{^{30}C_{r-1}} + 3{^{30}C_{r-2}} + {^{30}C_{r-3}} = {^{33}C_r} $$\n\nComparing with\n\n$$ {^mC_r} $$\n\nwe get\n\n$$ m = 33 $$\n\nThe correct answer is:\n\n$$ \\boxed{33} $$\n\nSo, Option C.",
