      "s": "JEE Main 2026 (Online) 5th April Evening Shift. Correct option: B. Using the binomial theorem,\n\n$$ \\left(2x^2+\\frac{1}{x}\\right)^{10} = \\sum_{r=0}^{10} \\binom{10}{r} (2x^2)^{10-r}\\left(\\frac{1}{x}\\right)^r $$\n\nNow simplify the general term:\n\n$$ T_{r+1}=\\binom{10}{r} 2^{10-r} x^{2(10-r)} x^{-r} $$\n\n$$ T_{r+1}=\\binom{10}{r} 2^{10-r} x^{20-2r-r} =\\binom{10}{r} 2^{10-r} x^{20-3r} $$\n\nWe need the coefficient of $x^2$, so set the power of $x$ equal to $2$:\n\n$$ 20-3r=2 $$\n\n$$ 3r=18 $$\n\n$$ r=6 $$\n\nNow substitute $r=6$:\n\n$$ \\text{Required coefficient}=\\binom{10}{6}2^{10-6} $$\n\n$$ =\\binom{10}{6}2^4 $$\n\n$$ =210 \\times 16 $$\n\n$$ =3360 $$\n\nSo, the coefficient of $x^2$ is\n\n$$ \\boxed{3360} $$\n\nHence, the correct option is B .",
