      "a": 1,
      "s": "JEE Main 2026 (Online) 2nd April Morning Shift. Correct option: B. We need to find the number of ordered pairs $(r,k)$ satisfying\n\n$$ {}^{36}C_{r+1}=\\frac{6\\left({}^{35}C_r\\right)}{k^2-3}, $$\n\nwhere $k \\in \\mathbb{Z}$.\n\nLet us simplify the relation using the standard NCERT combination formula.\n\nWe know that\n\n$$ {}^{n}C_{r+1}=\\frac{n!}{(r+1)!(n-r-1)!} $$\n\nand\n\n$$ {}^{n-1}C_r=\\frac{(n-1)!}{r!(n-r-1)!}. $$\n\nSo,\n\n$$ \\frac{{}^{36}C_{r+1}}{{}^{35}C_r} = \\frac{\\dfrac{36!}{(r+1)!(35-r)!}}{\\dfrac{35!}{r!(35-r)!}} = \\frac{36!}{35!}\\cdot \\frac{r!}{(r+1)!} = 36\\cdot \\frac{1}{r+1} = \\frac{36}{r+1}. $$\n\nHence,\n\n$$ {}^{36}C_{r+1} = {}^{35}C_r \\cdot \\frac{36}{r+1}. $$\n\nGiven,\n\n$$ {}^{36}C_{r+1}=\\frac{6\\left({}^{35}C_r\\right)}{k^2-3}. $$\n\nComparing both expressions,\n\n$$ {}^{35}C_r \\cdot \\frac{36}{r+1}=\\frac{6\\left({}^{35}C_r\\right)}{k^2-3}. $$\n\nSince ${}^{35}C_r \\neq 0$, cancel it:\n\n$$ \\frac{36}{r+1}=\\frac{6}{k^2-3}. $$\n\nCross-multiplying,\n\n$$ 36(k^2-3)=6(r+1). $$\n\nDivide by $6$:\n\n$$ 6(k^2-3)=r+1. $$\n\nSo,\n\n$$ r = 6k^2-19. $$\n\nNow $r$ must be valid for the combinations ${}^{35}C_r$ and ${}^{36}C_{r+1}$.\n\nThus,\n\n$$ 0 \\le r \\le 35. $$\n\nSubstitute $r=6k^2-19$:\n\n$$ 0 \\le 6k^2-19 \\le 35. $$\n\nAdd $19$ throughout:\n\n$$ 19 \\le 6k^2 \\le 54. $$\n\nDivide by $6$:\n\n$$ \\frac{19}{6} \\le k^2 \\le 9. $$\n\nNow possible integer square values are\n\n$$ k^2=4 \\quad \\text{or} \\quad k^2=9. $$\n\nSo the integer values of $k$ are:\n\nIf $k^2=4$, then $k=\\pm 2$\n\nIf $k^2=9$, then $k=\\pm 3$\n\nNow find corresponding $r$:\n\nFor $k^2=4$,\n\n$$ r=6(4)-19=24-19=5. $$\n\nSo pairs are\n\n$$ (5,2),\\ (5,-2). $$\n\nFor $k^2=9$,\n\n$$ r=6(9)-19=54-19=35. $$\n\nSo pairs are\n\n$$ (35,3),\\ (35,-3). $$\n\nHence total number of elements in the set $S$ is\n\n$$ 4. $$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is:\n\n$$ \\boxed{4} $$\n\nSo, Option B is correct.",
      "source": "JEE Main 2026 (Online) 2nd April Morning Shift | Permutation and Combination | mnriohx3",
      "pyq": true,
      "exactPaperText": true,
      "pyqSourceSlug": "permutations-and-combinations"
