      "s": "JEE Main 2026 (Online) 5th April Morning Shift. Correct option: C. First, find the vertex of the parabola.\n\nThe parabola is\n\n$$ x^2+6x+y+13=0 $$\n\nRewrite it by completing the square:\n\n$$ x^2+6x+y+13=0 $$\n\n$$ x^2+6x+9+y+13-9=0 $$\n\n$$ (x+3)^2+y+4=0 $$\n\n$$ y=-(x+3)^2-4 $$\n\nSo, the vertex of the parabola is\n\n$$ (-3,-4) $$\n\nNow, find the centre and radius of the circle.\n\nGiven circle:\n\n$$ x^2+y^2-6x-8y+21=0 $$\n\nComplete the squares:\n\n$$ x^2-6x+y^2-8y+21=0 $$\n\n$$ (x^2-6x+9)+(y^2-8y+16)+21-9-16=0 $$\n\n$$ (x-3)^2+(y-4)^2-4=0 $$\n\n$$ (x-3)^2+(y-4)^2=4 $$\n\nHence, centre of the circle is\n\n$$ (3,4) $$\n\nand radius is\n\n$$ r=2 $$\n\nNow we need the maximum distance of a point $P$ on this circle from the vertex $(-3,-4)$.\n\nLet $V=(-3,-4)$ and centre of circle be $C=(3,4)$.\n\nFirst find $VC$:\n\n$$ VC=\\sqrt{(3+3)^2+(4+4)^2} =\\sqrt{6^2+8^2} =\\sqrt{36+64} =\\sqrt{100} =10 $$\n\nFor a point moving on a circle, the maximum distance from an external point is\n\n$$ VC+r $$\n\nSo,\n\n$$ \\text{Maximum distance}=10+2=12 $$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is\n\n$$ \\boxed{12} $$\n\nSo, Option C is correct.",
