      "s": "JEE Main 2026 (Online) 6th April Evening Shift. Correct option: D. For the ellipse $E$, let its equation be\n\n$$ \\frac{x^2}{A^2}+\\frac{y^2}{B^2}=1, \\quad A>B $$\n\nsince its major axis is along the $x$-axis because the directrices are of the form $x=\\text{constant}$.\n\nGiven eccentricity,\n\n$$ e=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} $$\n\nFor an ellipse with major axis along the $x$-axis, the directrices are\n\n$$ x=\\pm \\frac{A}{e} $$\n\nWe are given\n\n$$ x=\\pm \\frac{4\\sqrt{6}}{3} $$\n\nSo,\n\n$$ \\frac{A}{e}=\\frac{4\\sqrt{6}}{3} $$\n\nSubstituting $e=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}$,\n\n$$ A=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\cdot \\frac{4\\sqrt{6}}{3} $$\n\n$$ A=\\frac{4\\sqrt{18}}{6} =\\frac{4\\cdot 3\\sqrt{2}}{6} =2\\sqrt{2} $$\n\nThus the semi-major axis of ellipse $E$ is\n\n$$ A=2\\sqrt{2} $$\n\nNow for the ellipse,\n\n$$ B^2=A^2(1-e^2) $$\n\nSince\n\n$$ A^2=(2\\sqrt{2})^2=8 $$\n\nand\n\n$$ e^2=\\frac{3}{4} $$\n\nwe get\n\n$$ B^2=8\\left(1-\\frac{3}{4}\\right)=8\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}=2 $$\n\nHence\n\n$$ B=\\sqrt{2} $$\n\nSo the length of minor axis of $E$ is\n\n$$ 2B=2\\sqrt{2} $$\n\nNow consider the hyperbola\n\n$$ H:\\frac{x^2}{a^2}-\\frac{y^2}{b^2}=1 $$\n\nIts eccentricity is equal to the length of semi-major axis of $E$, so\n\n$$ e_H=2\\sqrt{2} $$\n\nFor a hyperbola,\n\n$$ e_H^2=1+\\frac{b^2}{a^2} $$\n\nThus,\n\n$$ (2\\sqrt{2})^2=1+\\frac{b^2}{a^2} $$\n\n$$ 8=1+\\frac{b^2}{a^2} $$\n\n$$ \\frac{b^2}{a^2}=7 \\quad \\Rightarrow \\quad b^2=7a^2 $$\n\nAlso, the length of latus rectum of the hyperbola is equal to the length of minor axis of $E$.\n\nFor the hyperbola, length of latus rectum is\n\n$$ \\frac{2b^2}{a} $$\n\nSo,\n\n$$ \\frac{2b^2}{a}=2\\sqrt{2} $$\n\n$$ \\frac{b^2}{a}=\\sqrt{2} $$\n\nUsing $b^2=7a^2$,\n\n$$ \\frac{7a^2}{a}=\\sqrt{2} $$\n\n$$ 7a=\\sqrt{2} $$\n\n$$ a=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{7} $$\n\nNow for the hyperbola,\n\n$$ c=ae_H $$\n\nSo,\n\n$$ c=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{7}\\cdot 2\\sqrt{2} =\\frac{4}{7} $$\n\nDistance between the foci $=2c$,\n\n$$ 2c=\\frac{8}{7} $$\n\nHence, the correct answer is\n\n$$ \\boxed{\\frac{8}{7}} $$\n\nSo, Option D is correct.",
