      "s": "JEE Main 2025 (Online) 2nd April Evening Shift. Correct option: C. The length of the minor axis is equal to one-fourth of the distance between the foci. Mathematically, this can be expressed as:\n\n$ 2b = \\frac{1}{4}(2ae) $\n\nThis simplifies to:\n\n$ b = \\frac{ae}{4} $\n\nGiven that the relationship between $ b $, $ a $, and $ e $ is:\n\n$ \\frac{b^2}{a^2} = 1 - e^2 $\n\nSubstitute $ b = \\frac{ae}{4} $ into the equation:\n\n$ \\left(\\frac{ae}{4}\\right)^2 = a^2 \\cdot \\left(1 - e^2\\right) $\n\nExpanding and simplifying gives:\n\n$ \\frac{a^2 e^2}{16} = a^2(1 - e^2) $\n\nDivide both sides by $ a^2 $:\n\n$ \\frac{e^2}{16} = 1 - e^2 $\n\nRearrange and solve for $ e^2 $:\n\n$ \\frac{e^2}{16} + e^2 = 1 $\n\n$ \\frac{17e^2}{16} = 1 $\n\nSolve for $ e $:\n\n$ e^2 = \\frac{16}{17} $\n\n$ e = \\frac{4}{\\sqrt{17}} $\n\nThus, the eccentricity of the ellipse is:\n\n$\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{17}}$",
