      "s": "JEE Main 2025 (Online) 23rd January Evening Shift. Correct option: A. $$\\begin{aligned}\n&\\begin{aligned}\n& \\mathrm{T}=\\mathrm{S}_1 \\\\\n& \\frac{\\mathrm{x} \\cdot 1}{4}+\\frac{\\mathrm{y} \\cdot 1 / 2}{2}=\\frac{1}{4}+\\frac{1}{8} \\\\\n& \\mathrm{x}+\\mathrm{y}=\\frac{3}{2}\n\\end{aligned}\\\\\n&\\text { solve with ellipse }\\\\\n&\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{PR} & =\\sqrt{\\left(\\mathrm{x}_2-\\mathrm{x}_1\\right)^2+\\left(\\mathrm{y}_2-\\mathrm{y}_1\\right)^2} \\\\\n& =\\sqrt{2}\\left|\\mathrm{x}_2-\\mathrm{x}_1\\right|\n\\end{aligned}\n\\end{aligned}$$\n\n[Diagram: JEE Main 2025 (Online) 23rd January Evening Shift Mathematics - Ellipse Question 29 English Explanation]\n\n$$\\begin{aligned}\n& y_2=\\frac{3}{2}-x_2 \\\\\n& y_1=\\frac{3}{2}-x_1 \\\\\n& y_2-y_1=x_2-x_1 \\\\\n& x^2+2 y^2=4 \\\\\n& x^2+2\\left(\\frac{3}{2}-x\\right)^2=4 \\\\\n& 6 x^2-12 x+1=0 \\\\\n& x_1+x_2=2 \\\\\n& x_1 x_2=1 / 6 \\\\\n& \\left|x_2-x_1\\right|=\\sqrt{\\left(x_2+x_1\\right)^2-4 x_1 x_2} \\\\\n& \\quad=\\sqrt{4-4 / 6} \\\\\n& P R=\\sqrt{2} \\cdot 2 \\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{\\sqrt{2} \\sqrt{3}}=\\frac{2}{3} \\sqrt{15}\n\\end{aligned}$$",
