      "s": "JEE Main 2026 (Online) 5th April Morning Shift. Correct option: C. For the ellipse\n\n$$ E:\\frac{x^2}{a^2}+\\frac{y^2}{b^2}=1 $$\n\na focus is $S(4,0)$ and eccentricity is\n\n$$ e=\\frac{4}{5} $$\n\nWe need the area of $\\triangle POS$, where $P(3,\\alpha)$ lies on the ellipse and $O=(0,0)$.\n\nSince the focus is on the $x$-axis, the ellipse has major axis along the $x$-axis.\n\nFor such an ellipse, focus is at $(\\pm ae,0)$.\n\nGiven one focus is $(4,0)$, so\n\n$$ ae=4 $$\n\nand $e=\\frac{4}{5}$. Therefore,\n\n$$ a\\cdot \\frac{4}{5}=4 $$\n\n$$ a=5 $$\n\nNow,\n\n$$ c=ae=4 $$\n\nand for ellipse,\n\n$$ b^2=a^2-c^2 $$\n\nSo,\n\n$$ b^2=25-16=9 $$\n\nHence the ellipse is\n\n$$ \\frac{x^2}{25}+\\frac{y^2}{9}=1 $$\n\nSince $P(3,\\alpha)$ lies on the ellipse, substitute $x=3$:\n\n$$ \\frac{3^2}{25}+\\frac{\\alpha^2}{9}=1 $$\n\n$$ \\frac{9}{25}+\\frac{\\alpha^2}{9}=1 $$\n\n$$ \\frac{\\alpha^2}{9}=1-\\frac{9}{25} =\\frac{16}{25} $$\n\n$$ \\alpha^2=\\frac{144}{25} $$\n\n$$ \\alpha=\\pm \\frac{12}{5} $$\n\nNow find the area of triangle with vertices\n\n$$ O(0,0),\\quad P(3,\\alpha),\\quad S(4,0) $$\n\nUsing base $OS$:\n\n$$ OS=4 $$\n\nSince $OS$ lies on the $x$-axis, the height from $P$ to $OS$ is $|\\alpha|$.\n\nSo area is\n\n$$ \\frac{1}{2}\\times 4\\times |\\alpha| =2|\\alpha| $$\n\n$$ =2\\times \\frac{12}{5} =\\frac{24}{5} $$\n\nTherefore, the area of $\\triangle POS$ is\n\n$$ \\boxed{\\frac{24}{5}} $$\n\nSo, the correct option is:\n\n$$ \\boxed{\\text{Option C}} $$",
