      "q": "The eccentricity of an ellipse $E$ with centre at the origin $O$ is $\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}$ and its directrices are $x= \\pm \\frac{4 \\sqrt{6}}{3}$. Let $\\mathrm{H}: \\frac{x^2}{\\mathrm{a}^2}-\\frac{y^2}{\\mathrm{~b}^2}=1$ be a hyperbola whose eccentricity is equal to the length of semi-major axis of E , and whose length of latus rectum is equal to the length of minor axis of E . Then the distance between the foci of H is :",
      "qHtml": "<p>The eccentricity of an ellipse $E$ with centre at the origin $O$ is $\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}$ and its directrices are $x= \\pm \\frac{4 \\sqrt{6}}{3}$. Let $\\mathrm{H}: \\frac{x^2}{\\mathrm{a}^2}-\\frac{y^2}{\\mathrm{~b}^2}=1$ be a hyperbola whose eccentricity is equal to the length of semi-major axis of E , and whose length of latus rectum is equal to the length of minor axis of E . Then the distance between the foci of H is :</p>",
