      "s": "JEE Main 2026 (Online) 2nd April Evening Shift. Correct option: C. Let\n\n$$ P(x_1,y_1), \\qquad Q(x_2,y_2) $$\n\nbe two points on the rectangular hyperbola\n\n$$ xy=12 $$\n\nSo, both points satisfy\n\n$$ x_1y_1=12 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad x_2y_2=12 $$\n\nAlso, the midpoint of $PQ$ is given as\n\n$$ \\left(\\frac{1}{2},-\\frac{1}{2}\\right) $$\n\nUsing the midpoint formula,\n\n$$ \\frac{x_1+x_2}{2}=\\frac{1}{2}, \\qquad \\frac{y_1+y_2}{2}=-\\frac{1}{2} $$\n\nHence,\n\n$$ x_1+x_2=1, \\qquad y_1+y_2=-1 $$\n\nNow we need the area of triangle $OPQ$, where $O=(0,0)$.\n\nThe area of triangle formed by points $O(0,0)$, $P(x_1,y_1)$, $Q(x_2,y_2)$ is\n\n$$ \\text{Area}=\\frac{1}{2}\\left|x_1y_2-x_2y_1\\right| $$\n\nSo our aim is to find $\\left|x_1y_2-x_2y_1\\right|$.\n\nSince $x_1$ and $x_2$ are the $x$-coordinates of points on the hyperbola, and their sum is $1$, let us use\n\n$$ y_1=\\frac{12}{x_1}, \\qquad y_2=\\frac{12}{x_2} $$\n\nNow using\n\n$$ y_1+y_2=-1 $$\n\nwe get\n\n$$ \\frac{12}{x_1}+\\frac{12}{x_2}=-1 $$\n\n$$ 12\\left(\\frac{x_1+x_2}{x_1x_2}\\right)=-1 $$\n\nSince $x_1+x_2=1$,\n\n$$ 12\\left(\\frac{1}{x_1x_2}\\right)=-1 $$\n\nSo,\n\n$$ x_1x_2=-12 $$\n\nThus $x_1$ and $x_2$ are roots of the quadratic equation\n\n$$ t^2-(x_1+x_2)t+x_1x_2=0 $$\n\n$$ t^2-t-12=0 $$\n\n$$ (t-4)(t+3)=0 $$\n\nHence,\n\n$$ x_1=4,\\quad x_2=-3 $$\n\nor vice versa.\n\nThen corresponding $y$-coordinates are\n\n$$ y_1=\\frac{12}{4}=3, \\qquad y_2=\\frac{12}{-3}=-4 $$\n\nSo the points are\n\n$$ P(4,3), \\qquad Q(-3,-4) $$\n\nNow area of triangle $OPQ$ is\n\n$$ \\text{Area}=\\frac{1}{2}\\left|4(-4)-(-3)(3)\\right| $$\n\n$$ =\\frac{1}{2}\\left|-16+9\\right| $$\n\n$$ =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 7 $$\n\n$$ =\\frac{7}{2} $$\n\nTherefore, the required area is\n\n$$ \\boxed{\\frac{7}{2}} $$\n\nSo, the correct option is:\n\n$$ \\boxed{\\text{Option C}} $$",
