      "s": "JEE Main 2024 (Online) 27th January Morning Shift. Correct option: C. $$(2 k, 3 k)$$ will lie on circle whose diameter is $$A B$$.\n\n[Diagram: JEE Main 2024 (Online) 27th January Morning Shift Mathematics - Circle Question 43 English Explanation]\n\n$$\\begin{aligned}\n& (x-1)(x)+(y-1)(y)=0 \\\\\n& x^2+y^2-x-y=0 \\quad \\text{.... (i)}\n\\end{aligned}$$\n\nSatisfy (2k, 3k) in (i)\n\n$$\\begin{aligned}\n& (2 k)^2+(3 k)^2-2 k-3 k=0 \\\\\n& 13 k^2-5 k=0 \\\\\n& k=0, k=\\frac{5}{13} \\\\\n& \\text { hence } k=\\frac{5}{13}\n\\end{aligned}$$",
