      "a": 1,
      "s": "JEE Main 2026 (Online) 4th April Evening Shift. Correct option: B. Given\n\n$$ f(x+y)=f(x)+2y^2+y+\\alpha xy \\quad \\text{for all } x,y\\in \\mathbb{R} $$\n\nwith\n\n$$ f(0)=-1,\\qquad f(1)=2. $$\n\nWe have to find\n\n$$ \\sum_{n=1}^5 (\\alpha+f(n)). $$\n\nStep 1: Use the given relation to find $\\alpha$\n\nPut $x=0$ in\n\n$$ f(x+y)=f(x)+2y^2+y+\\alpha xy. $$\n\nThen\n\n$$ f(y)=f(0)+2y^2+y+\\alpha\\cdot 0\\cdot y $$\n\nso\n\n$$ f(y)=-1+2y^2+y. $$\n\nThus, for every real $y$,\n\n$$ f(y)=2y^2+y-1. $$\n\nNow use $f(1)=2$:\n\n$$ f(1)=2(1)^2+1-1=2. $$\n\nThis is already satisfied, so now we must use the original equation to determine $\\alpha$.\n\nSubstitute\n\n$$ f(x+y)=2(x+y)^2+(x+y)-1 $$\n\nand\n\n$$ f(x)=2x^2+x-1 $$\n\ninto the given equation:\n\n$$ 2(x+y)^2+(x+y)-1 = 2x^2+x-1+2y^2+y+\\alpha xy. $$\n\nExpand the left side:\n\n$$ 2x^2+4xy+2y^2+x+y-1. $$\n\nRight side is:\n\n$$ 2x^2+x-1+2y^2+y+\\alpha xy. $$\n\nComparing both sides,\n\n$$ 4xy=\\alpha xy. $$\n\nHence,\n\n$$ \\alpha=4. $$\n\nStep 2: Find $f(n)$ for $n=1$ to $5$\n\nSince\n\n$$ f(n)=2n^2+n-1, $$\n\nwe get:\n\n$$ f(1)=2(1)^2+1-1=2 $$\n\n$$ f(2)=2(2)^2+2-1=8+2-1=9 $$\n\n$$ f(3)=2(3)^2+3-1=18+3-1=20 $$\n\n$$ f(4)=2(4)^2+4-1=32+4-1=35 $$\n\n$$ f(5)=2(5)^2+5-1=50+5-1=54 $$\n\nStep 3: Compute the required sum\n\nWe need\n\n$$ \\sum_{n=1}^5 (\\alpha+f(n)). $$\n\nSince $\\alpha=4$,\n\n$$ \\alpha+f(1)=4+2=6 $$\n\n$$ \\alpha+f(2)=4+9=13 $$\n\n$$ \\alpha+f(3)=4+20=24 $$\n\n$$ \\alpha+f(4)=4+35=39 $$\n\n$$ \\alpha+f(5)=4+54=58 $$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$ 6+13+24+39+58=140. $$\n\nSo the required value is\n\n$$ \\boxed{140}. $$\n\nHence, the correct option is B .",
