      "s": "JEE Main 2026 (Online) 6th April Morning Shift. Correct option: B. Let the mean of the 20 observations be $\\bar{x}$ and the standard deviation be $\\sigma$.\n\nWe are given:\n\n$$ \\sum_{i=1}^{20}(x_i+5)^2 = 2500 $$\n\nand\n\n$$ \\sum_{i=1}^{20}(x_i-5)^2 = 100 $$\n\nWe will expand both expressions.\n\nFirst,\n\n$$ \\sum_{i=1}^{20}(x_i+5)^2 = \\sum_{i=1}^{20}(x_i^2+10x_i+25) $$\n\n$$ = \\sum x_i^2 + 10\\sum x_i + 20\\cdot 25 $$\n\n$$ = \\sum x_i^2 + 10\\sum x_i + 500 $$\n\nSo,\n\n$$ \\sum x_i^2 + 10\\sum x_i + 500 = 2500 $$\n\n$$ \\sum x_i^2 + 10\\sum x_i = 2000 \\qquad ...(1) $$\n\nNow expand the second one:\n\n$$ \\sum_{i=1}^{20}(x_i-5)^2 = \\sum_{i=1}^{20}(x_i^2-10x_i+25) $$\n\n$$ = \\sum x_i^2 - 10\\sum x_i + 500 $$\n\nSo,\n\n$$ \\sum x_i^2 - 10\\sum x_i + 500 = 100 $$\n\n$$ \\sum x_i^2 - 10\\sum x_i = -400 \\qquad ...(2) $$\n\nNow add (1) and (2):\n\n$$ 2\\sum x_i^2 = 1600 $$\n\n$$ \\sum x_i^2 = 800 $$\n\nNow subtract (2) from (1):\n\n$$ 20\\sum x_i = 2400 $$\n\n$$ \\sum x_i = 120 $$\n\nHence mean:\n\n$$ \\bar{x}=\\frac{\\sum x_i}{20}=\\frac{120}{20}=6 $$\n\nNow use the formula for standard deviation:\n\n$$ \\sigma = \\sqrt{\\frac{\\sum x_i^2}{20} - \\bar{x}^2} $$\n\n$$ = \\sqrt{\\frac{800}{20} - 6^2} $$\n\n$$ = \\sqrt{40-36} $$\n\n$$ = \\sqrt{4}=2 $$\n\nTherefore, the ratio of mean to standard deviation is\n\n$$ \\bar{x} : \\sigma = 6:2 = 3:1 $$\n\nSo, the correct option is:\n\n$$ \\boxed{3:1} $$\n\nOption B",
