      "s": "JEE Main 2026 (Online) 4th April Morning Shift. Correct option: D. The given data set has $n = 9$ observations: $21, 8, 17, a, 51, 103, b, 13, 67$.\n\nThe mean ($\\bar{x}$) of these numbers is given as $40$.\n\nThe formula for the mean is:\n\n$$ \\text{Mean} = \\frac{\\text{Sum of all observations}}{n} $$\n\nSubstitute the given values into the formula:\n\n$$ 40 = \\frac{21 + 8 + 17 + a + 51 + 103 + b + 13 + 67}{9} $$\n\nMultiply both sides by 9:\n\n$$ 360 = 280 + a + b $$\n\n$$ a + b = 360 - 280 $$\n\n$$ a + b = 80 \\quad \\text{--- (Equation 1)} $$\n\nThe median ($M$) of the data is $21$. For $n = 9$ (an odd number), the median is the $\\left(\\frac{9 + 1}{2}\\right)^{\\text{th}} = 5^{\\text{th}}$ observation when aligned in ascending order.\n\nLet's arrange the known numbers in ascending order:\n\n$8, 13, 17, 21, 51, 67, 103$\n\nHere, there are exactly three numbers less than $21$ ($8, 13, 17$) and three numbers greater than $21$ ($51, 67, 103$).\n\nFor $21$ to remain the middle (5th) observation among all 9 numbers, one of the unknown variables ($a$ or $b$) must be less than or equal to $21$, and the other must be greater than or equal to $21$.\n\nSince it is given that $a > b$, we can conclude:\n\n$a \\ge 21$ and $b \\le 21$\n\nThe formula for mean deviation about the median is:\n\n$$ \\text{M.D. (M)} = \\frac{\\sum_{i=1}^{n} |x_i - M|}{n} $$\n\nWe are given that $\\text{M.D. (M)} = 26$.\n\nSubstitute the values:\n\n$$ 26 = \\frac{|21 - 21| + |8 - 21| + |17 - 21| + |a - 21| + |51 - 21| + |103 - 21| + |b - 21| + |13 - 21| + |67 - 21|}{9} $$\n\nMultiply by 9 and simplify the absolute values for the known numbers:\n\n$$ 234 = 0 + 13 + 4 + |a - 21| + 30 + 82 + |b - 21| + 8 + 46 $$\n\n$$ 234 = 183 + |a - 21| + |b - 21| $$\n\n$$ |a - 21| + |b - 21| = 234 - 183 $$\n\n$$ |a - 21| + |b - 21| = 51 $$\n\nFrom Step 2, we know that $a \\ge 21 \\implies |a - 21| = a - 21$ and $b \\le 21 \\implies |b - 21| = 21 - b$. Replacing these in the equation:\n\n$$ (a - 21) + (21 - b) = 51 $$\n\n$$ a - b = 51 \\quad \\text{--- (Equation 2)} $$\n\nNow we have a system of two linear equations:\n\n1) $a + b = 80$\n\n2) $a - b = 51$\n\nTo find $2a$, simply add Equation 1 and Equation 2:\n\n$$ (a + b) + (a - b) = 80 + 51 $$\n\n$$ 2a = 131 $$\n\nTherefore, the value of $2a$ is $131$.\n\nOption D is the correct answer.",
