      "s": "JEE Main 2026 (Online) 2nd April Morning Shift. Correct option: C. For the grouped data, we first find the class marks of each class interval.\n\nThe classes are:\n\n$$5-10,\\; 10-15,\\; 15-20,\\; 20-25,\\; 25-30,\\; 30-35$$\n\nSo their class marks are:\n\n$$7.5,\\; 12.5,\\; 17.5,\\; 22.5,\\; 27.5,\\; 32.5$$\n\nThe frequencies are:\n\n$$2,\\; k,\\; 28,\\; 54,\\; k+1,\\; 5$$\n\nNow use the formula for mean of grouped data:\n\n$$\\bar{x}=\\frac{\\sum f_i x_i}{\\sum f_i}$$\n\nGiven mean $=21$.\n\nNow calculate $\\sum f_i$:\n\n$$\\sum f_i = 2+k+28+54+(k+1)+5$$\n\n$$\\sum f_i = 2k+90$$\n\nNow calculate $\\sum f_i x_i$:\n\n$$\\sum f_i x_i = 2(7.5)+k(12.5)+28(17.5)+54(22.5)+(k+1)(27.5)+5(32.5)$$\n\nNow simplify step by step:\n\n$$2(7.5)=15$$\n\n$$28(17.5)=490$$\n\n$$54(22.5)=1215$$\n\n$$5(32.5)=162.5$$\n\n$$(k+1)(27.5)=27.5k+27.5$$\n\nSo,\n\n$$\\sum f_i x_i = 15+12.5k+490+1215+27.5k+27.5+162.5$$\n\n$$\\sum f_i x_i = 40k+1910$$\n\nNow apply the mean formula:\n\n$$21=\\frac{40k+1910}{2k+90}$$\n\nCross-multiply:\n\n$$21(2k+90)=40k+1910$$\n\n$$42k+1890=40k+1910$$\n\n$$2k=20$$\n\n$$k=10$$\n\nNow we check which equation has $k=10$ as a root.\n\nOption A:\n\n$$2x^2-23x-10=0$$\n\nPut $x=10$:\n\n$$2(10)^2-23(10)-10=200-230-10=-40\\neq 0$$\n\nOption B:\n\n$$4x^2-35x+24=0$$\n\nPut $x=10$:\n\n$$4(10)^2-35(10)+24=400-350+24=74\\neq 0$$\n\nOption C:\n\n$$2x^2-19x-10=0$$\n\nPut $x=10$:\n\n$$2(10)^2-19(10)-10=200-190-10=0$$\n\nSo $10$ is a root.\n\nHence, the correct option is:\n\n$$\\boxed{\\text{Option C } \\; 2x^2-19x-10=0}$$",
