      "qHtml": "<p>Let $x_1, x_2, ..., x_{10}$ be ten observations such that $\\sum\\limits_{i=1}^{10} (x_i - 2) = 30$, $\\sum\\limits_{i=1}^{10} (x_i - \\beta)^2 = 98$, $\\beta > 2$, and their variance is $\\frac{4}{5}$. If $\\mu$ and $\\sigma^2$ are respectively the mean and the variance of $2(x_1 - 1) + 4\\beta, 2(x_2 - 1) + 4\\beta, ..., 2(x_{10} - 1) + 4\\beta$, then $\\frac{\\beta\\mu}{\\sigma^2}$ is equal to :</p>",
