      "a": 1,
      "s": "JEE Main 2026 (Online) 5th April Evening Shift. Correct option: B. Since the images of the standard basis vectors are given, the columns of matrix $M$ are exactly these vectors.\n\nSo,\n\n$$ M= \\begin{pmatrix} 1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 2 & 1 \\end{pmatrix} $$\n\nNow we are given\n\n$$ M\\begin{pmatrix}x\\\\y\\\\z\\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix}1\\\\7\\\\11\\end{pmatrix} $$\n\nSo,\n\n$$ \\begin{pmatrix} 1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 2 & 1 \\end{pmatrix} \\begin{pmatrix}x\\\\y\\\\z\\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix}1\\\\7\\\\11\\end{pmatrix} $$\n\nThis gives the system:\n\n$$ x-z=1 $$\n\n$$ 2x+y+z=7 $$\n\n$$ 3x+2y+z=11 $$\n\nNow solve step by step.\n\nFrom the first equation,\n\n$$ x=1+z $$\n\nSubstitute into the second equation:\n\n$$ 2(1+z)+y+z=7 $$\n\n$$ 2+3z+y=7 $$\n\n$$ y+3z=5 \\quad \\Rightarrow \\quad y=5-3z $$\n\nNow substitute $x=1+z$ and $y=5-3z$ into the third equation:\n\n$$ 3(1+z)+2(5-3z)+z=11 $$\n\n$$ 3+3z+10-6z+z=11 $$\n\n$$ 13-2z=11 $$\n\n$$ -2z=-2 $$\n\n$$ z=1 $$\n\nThen,\n\n$$ x=1+z=2 $$\n\nand\n\n$$ y=5-3z=2 $$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$ x+y+z=2+2+1=5 $$\n\nSo the correct answer is:\n\n$$ \\boxed{5} $$\n\nOption B",
      "source": "JEE Main 2026 (Online) 5th April Evening Shift | Matrices | mnswhxry",
