      "q": "Let $a \\in R$ and $A$ be a matrix of order $3 \\times 3$ such that $\\operatorname{det}(A)=-4$ and $A+I=\\left[\\begin{array}{lll}1 & a & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ a & 1 & 2\\end{array}\\right]$, where $I$ is the identity matrix of order $3 \\times 3$. If $\\operatorname{det}((a+1) \\operatorname{adj}((a-1) A))$ is $2^{\\mathrm{m}} 3^{\\mathrm{n}}, \\mathrm{m}$, $\\mathrm{n} \\in\\{0,1,2, \\ldots, 20\\}$, then $\\mathrm{m}+\\mathrm{n}$ is equal to :",
      "qHtml": "<p>Let $a \\in R$ and $A$ be a matrix of order $3 \\times 3$ such that $\\operatorname{det}(A)=-4$ and $A+I=\\left[\\begin{array}{lll}1 & a & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ a & 1 & 2\\end{array}\\right]$, where $I$ is the identity matrix of order $3 \\times 3$. If $\\operatorname{det}((a+1) \\operatorname{adj}((a-1) A))$ is $2^{\\mathrm{m}} 3^{\\mathrm{n}}, \\mathrm{m}$, $\\mathrm{n} \\in\\{0,1,2, \\ldots, 20\\}$, then $\\mathrm{m}+\\mathrm{n}$ is equal to :</p>",
