      "s": "JEE Main 2023 (Online) 30th January Evening Shift. Correct option: A. $$P = \\left[ {\\matrix{\n{{a_1}} & {{b_1}} & {{c_1}} \\cr\n{{a_2}} & {{b_2}} & {{c_2}} \\cr\n{{a_3}} & {{b_3}} & {{c_3}} \\cr\n\n} } \\right]$$\n\nGiven : $${P^T} = aP + (a - 1)I$$\n\n$$\\left[ {\\matrix{\n{{a_1}} & {{a_2}} & {{a_3}} \\cr\n{{b_1}} & {{b_2}} & {{b_3}} \\cr\n{{c_1}} & {{c_2}} & {{c_3}} \\cr\n\n} } \\right] = \\left[ {\\matrix{\n{a{a_1} + a - 1} & {a{b_1}} & {a{c_1}} \\cr\n{a{a_2}} & {a{b_2} + a - 1} & {a{c_2}} \\cr\n{a{a_3}} & {a{b_3}} & {a{c_3} + a - 1} \\cr\n\n} } \\right]$$\n\n$$ \\Rightarrow {a_1} = a{a_1} + a - 1 \\Rightarrow {a_1}(1 - a) = a - 1 \\Rightarrow {a_1} = - 1$$\n\nSimilarly, $${a_1} = {b_2} = {c_3} = - 1$$\n\nNow, $$\\left. \\matrix{\n{a_2} = a{b_1} \\hfill \\cr\n{b_1} = a{a_2} \\hfill \\cr} \\right] \\to {a_2} = {a^2}{a_2} \\Rightarrow {a_2} = 0 \\Rightarrow {b_1} = 0$$\n\n$${c_1} = a{a_3}$$\n\nSimilarly, all other elements will also be 0\n\n$${a_2} = {a_3} = {b_1} = {b_3} = {c_1} = {c_2} = 0$$\n\n$$\\therefore$$ $$P = \\left[ {\\matrix{\n{ - 1} & 0 & 0 \\cr\n0 & { - 1} & 0 \\cr\n0 & 0 & { - 1} \\cr\n\n} } \\right]$$\n\n$$|P| = - 1$$\n\n$$|Adj(P){|_{n \\times n}} = |A{|^{(n - 1)}}$$\n\n$$ \\Rightarrow |Adj(P)| = {( - 1)^2} = 1$$",
