      "q": "Let M be a $3 \\times 3$ matrix such that $\\mathrm{M}\\left(\\begin{array}{l}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{array}\\right)=\\left(\\begin{array}{l}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 3\\end{array}\\right), \\mathrm{M}\\left(\\begin{array}{l}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{array}\\right)=\\left(\\begin{array}{l}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{array}\\right)$ and $\\mathrm{M}\\left(\\begin{array}{l}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{array}\\right)=\\left(\\begin{array}{c}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{array}\\right)$. If $\\mathrm{M}\\left(\\begin{array}{l}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{array}\\right)=\\left(\\begin{array}{c}1 \\\\ 7 \\\\ 11\\end{array}\\right)$, then $x+y+z$ equals :",
      "qHtml": "<p>Let M be a $3 \\times 3$ matrix such that $\\mathrm{M}\\left(\\begin{array}{l}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{array}\\right)=\\left(\\begin{array}{l}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 3\\end{array}\\right), \\mathrm{M}\\left(\\begin{array}{l}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{array}\\right)=\\left(\\begin{array}{l}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{array}\\right)$ and $\\mathrm{M}\\left(\\begin{array}{l}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{array}\\right)=\\left(\\begin{array}{c}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{array}\\right)$. If $\\mathrm{M}\\left(\\begin{array}{l}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{array}\\right)=\\left(\\begin{array}{c}1 \\\\ 7 \\\\ 11\\end{array}\\right)$, then $x+y+z$ equals :</p>",
