      "q": "Let $A=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc}1 & 2 & 7 \\\\ 4 & -2 & 8 \\\\ 3 & 8 & -7\\end{array}\\right]$ and $\\operatorname{det}(A-\\alpha I)=0$, where $\\alpha$ is a real number. If the largest possible value of $\\alpha$ is $p$, then the circle $(x-p)^2+(y-2 p)^2=320$, intersects the co-ordinate axes at",
      "qHtml": "<p>Let $A=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc}1 & 2 & 7 \\\\ 4 & -2 & 8 \\\\ 3 & 8 & -7\\end{array}\\right]$ and $\\operatorname{det}(A-\\alpha I)=0$, where $\\alpha$ is a real number. If the largest possible value of $\\alpha$ is $p$, then the circle $(x-p)^2+(y-2 p)^2=320$, intersects the co-ordinate axes at</p>",
