      "q": "Let a triangle PQR be such that P and Q lie on the line $\\frac{x+3}{8}=\\frac{y-4}{2}=\\frac{z+1}{2}$ and are at a distance of 6 units from $R(1,2,3)$. If $(\\alpha, \\beta, \\gamma)$ is the centroid of $\\Delta P Q R$, then $\\alpha+\\beta+\\gamma$ is equal to :",
      "qHtml": "<p>Let a triangle PQR be such that P and Q lie on the line $\\frac{x+3}{8}=\\frac{y-4}{2}=\\frac{z+1}{2}$ and are at a distance of 6 units from $R(1,2,3)$. If $(\\alpha, \\beta, \\gamma)$ is the centroid of $\\Delta P Q R$, then $\\alpha+\\beta+\\gamma$ is equal to :</p>",
