      "s": "JEE Main 2026 (Online) 4th April Morning Shift. Correct option: B. [Diagram: JEE Main 2026 (Online) 4th April Morning Shift Mathematics - 3D Geometry Question 8 English Explanation]\n\nP$(2\\lambda, 3\\lambda, 3\\lambda - 1)$ and Q$(-\\mu - 1, \\mu + 2, 4\\mu)$\n\nD.R of PQ $2\\lambda + \\mu + 1$, $3\\lambda - \\mu - 2$, $3\\lambda - 4\\mu - 1$,\n\n$$\\frac{2\\lambda + \\mu + 1}{1} = \\frac{3\\lambda - \\mu - 2}{-1} = \\frac{3\\lambda - 4\\mu - 1}{2}$$\n\nSolving $\\lambda = \\frac{1}{5}$ and $\\mu = -\\frac{8}{15}$\n\nP$\\left(\\frac{2}{5}, \\frac{3}{5}, -\\frac{2}{5}\\right)$ & Q$\\left(-\\frac{7}{15}, \\frac{22}{15}, -\\frac{32}{15}\\right)$\n\n$$\\mathrm{PQ}^2 = \\left(\\frac{13}{15}\\right)^2 + \\left(\\frac{13}{15}\\right)^2 + \\left(\\frac{26}{15}\\right)^2$$\n\n$$\\alpha^2 = \\frac{1014}{225} \\therefore 225\\alpha^2 = 1014$$",
