      "s": "JEE Main 2026 (Online) 2nd April Morning Shift. Correct option: C. Direction vector of line is\n\n$$ =\\left|\\begin{array}{ccc} \\hat{i} & \\hat{j} & \\hat{k} \\\\ 1 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 2 & 1 \\end{array}\\right|=-2 \\hat{i}+3 \\hat{j}-2 \\hat{k} $$\n\n[Diagram: JEE Main 2026 (Online) 2nd April Morning Shift Mathematics - 3D Geometry Question 16 English Explanation]\n\nSo equation of line is\n\n$$ \\frac{x-1}{2}=\\frac{y-1}{-3}=\\frac{z-1}{2}=\\lambda \\text { let } $$\n\nlet ( $2 \\lambda+1,-3 \\lambda+1,2 \\lambda+1$ ) be the foot of perpendicular from $(0,0,0)$ upon given line\n\n$$ \\begin{aligned} & \\Rightarrow \\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{OM}} \\cdot(2 \\hat{\\mathrm{i}}-3 \\mathrm{j}+2 \\hat{\\mathrm{k}})=0 \\\\ & \\Rightarrow 2(2 \\lambda+1)-3(-3 \\lambda+1)+2(2 \\lambda+1)=0 \\\\ & \\Rightarrow \\lambda=-\\frac{1}{17} \\end{aligned} $$\n\nSo $(\\mathrm{a}, \\mathrm{b}, \\mathrm{c}) \\equiv\\left(\\frac{-2}{17}+1, \\frac{3}{17}+1, \\frac{-2}{17}+1\\right)$\n\n$$ \\Rightarrow 34(a+b+c)=100 $$",
