      "s": "JEE Main 2021 (Online) 31st August Evening Shift. Correct option: B. f(0) = 0, f(1) = 1 and f(2) = 2\n\nLet h(x) = f(x) $$-$$ x\n\nClearly h(x) is continuous and twice differentiable on (0, 2)\n\nAlso, h(0) = h(1) = h(2) = 0\n\n$$\\therefore$$ h(x) satisfies all the condition of Rolle's theorem.\n\n$$\\therefore$$ there exist C 1 $$\\in$$(0, 1) such that h'(c 1 ) = 0\n\n$$\\Rightarrow$$ f'( 1 ) $$-$$ 1 = 0 $$\\Rightarrow$$ f'(c 1 ) = 1\n\nalso there exist c 2 $$\\in$$(1, 2) such that h'(c 2 ) = 0\n\n$$\\Rightarrow$$ f'(c 2 ) = 1\n\nNow, using Rolle's theorem on [c 1 , c 2 ] for f'(x)\n\nWe have f''(c) = 0, c$$\\in$$(c 1 , c 2 )\n\nHence, f''(x) = 0 for some x$$\\in$$(0, 2).",
