      "q": "Let $f(x)$ and $g(x)$ be twice differentiable functions satisfying $f^{\\prime \\prime}(x)=g^{\\prime \\prime}(x)$ for all $x \\in \\mathbf{R}, f^{\\prime}(1)=2 g^{\\prime}(1)=4$ and $g(2)=3 f(2)=9$. Then $f(25)-g(25)$ is equal to :",
      "qHtml": "<p>Let $f(x)$ and $g(x)$ be twice differentiable functions satisfying $f^{\\prime \\prime}(x)=g^{\\prime \\prime}(x)$ for all $x \\in \\mathbf{R}, f^{\\prime}(1)=2 g^{\\prime}(1)=4$ and $g(2)=3 f(2)=9$. Then $f(25)-g(25)$ is equal to :</p>",
