      "a": 1,
      "s": "JEE Main 2026 (Online) 5th April Morning Shift. Correct option: B. Given\n\n$$ f\\left(\\frac{x+y}{3}\\right)=\\frac{f(x)+f(y)}{3}\\quad \\text{for all }x,y\\in \\mathbb{R}, $$\n\nand\n\n$$ f'(0)=3. $$\n\nWe have to find the minimum value of\n\n$$ g(x)=3+e^x f(x). $$\n\nStep 1: Find the form of $f(x)$\n\nWe are given a functional equation. We will use it carefully.\n\nLet\n\n$$ \\frac{x+y}{3}=t. $$\n\nThen\n\n$$ x+y=3t. $$\n\nThe relation becomes\n\n$$ f(t)=\\frac{f(x)+f(y)}{3}\\quad \\text{whenever }x+y=3t. $$\n\nWe now choose suitable values.\n\nPut $x=y=0$\n\nThen\n\n$$ f(0)=\\frac{f(0)+f(0)}{3}=\\frac{2f(0)}{3}. $$\n\nSo,\n\n$$ 3f(0)=2f(0)\\implies f(0)=0. $$\n\nPut $y=0$\n\nThen\n\n$$ f\\left(\\frac{x}{3}\\right)=\\frac{f(x)+f(0)}{3}=\\frac{f(x)}{3}. $$\n\nThus,\n\n$$ f(x)=3f\\left(\\frac{x}{3}\\right). $$\n\nNow differentiate both sides with respect to $x$:\n\n$$ f'(x)=3\\cdot f'\\left(\\frac{x}{3}\\right)\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}=f'\\left(\\frac{x}{3}\\right). $$\n\nSo,\n\n$$ f'(x)=f'\\left(\\frac{x}{3}\\right). $$\n\nRepeating this,\n\n$$ f'(x)=f'\\left(\\frac{x}{3}\\right)=f'\\left(\\frac{x}{3^2}\\right)=\\cdots=f'\\left(\\frac{x}{3^n}\\right). $$\n\nAs $n\\to\\infty$,\n\n$$ \\frac{x}{3^n}\\to 0. $$\n\nSince $f$ is differentiable, $f'$ is defined at $0$, so we get\n\n$$ f'(x)=f'(0)=3. $$\n\nHence,\n\n$$ f'(x)=3\\quad \\text{for all }x. $$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$ f(x)=3x+c. $$\n\nBut $f(0)=0$, so\n\n$$ c=0. $$\n\nThus,\n\n$$ f(x)=3x. $$\n\nStep 2: Write $g(x)$\n\nNow\n\n$$ g(x)=3+e^x f(x)=3+e^x(3x)=3+3xe^x. $$\n\nSo,\n\n$$ g(x)=3\\bigl(1+xe^x\\bigr). $$\n\nStep 3: Minimise $xe^x$\n\nLet\n\n$$ h(x)=xe^x. $$\n\nThen\n\n$$ h'(x)=e^x+xe^x=e^x(1+x). $$\n\nSince $e^x>0$ for all $x$, we have\n\n$$ h'(x)=0 \\iff 1+x=0 \\iff x=-1. $$\n\nNow,\n\nfor $x for $x>-1$, $h'(x)>0$, so $h$ is increasing.\n\nHence $h(x)$ has a minimum at $x=-1$.\n\nIts minimum value is\n\n$$ h(-1)=(-1)e^{-1}=-\\frac{1}{e}. $$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$ g_{\\min}=3\\left(1-\\frac{1}{e}\\right)=3\\left(\\frac{e-1}{e}\\right). $$\n\nFinal Answer\n\n$$ \\boxed{3\\left(\\frac{e-1}{e}\\right)} $$\n\nSo the correct option is B .",
