      "s": "JEE Main 2026 (Online) 2nd April Evening Shift. Correct option: D. Given $f(x)$ is a polynomial of degree $5$\n\nAlso, $f'(1)=0$; $f'(-1)=0$.\n\nAlso $\\because\\ \\lim\\limits_{x\\rightarrow 0}\\dfrac{f(x)}{x^3}=-5$ (fixed and finite)\n\n$\\therefore\\ f(0)=0$; $f'(0)=0$; $f''(0)=0$\n\n$$\\dfrac{f'''(0)}{6}=-5 \\rightarrow f'''(0)=-30$$\n\nHence, let\n\n$$f'(x)=(ax+b)(x-0)(x-1)(x+1)$$\n\n$$\\rightarrow f'(x)=ax^4+bx^3-ax^2-bx$$\n\n$$f''(x)=4ax^3+3bx^2-2ax-b$$\n\n$$\\therefore\\ f''(0)=0 \\rightarrow b=0$$\n\n$$f'''(x)=12ax^2+6bx-2a$$\n\n$$\\therefore\\ f'''(0)=-2a=-30$$\n\n$$\\rightarrow a=15$$\n\n$$\\therefore\\ f'(x)=15x.x.(x-1)(x+1)$$\n\n$$\\rightarrow f'(x)=15x^4-15x^2$$\n\n$$\\rightarrow f(x)=3x^5-5x^3+C$$\n\n$$\\therefore\\ f(0)=0 \\rightarrow C=0$$\n\n$$\\therefore\\ f(x)=3x^5-5x^3$$\n\n$$\\therefore\\ f(2)-f(-2)=112$$",
