      "s": "JEE Main 2026 (Online) 6th April Evening Shift. Correct option: B. $ I=\\int_{-1}^{1}\\left(\\frac{x^3+|x|+1}{x^2+2|x|+1}\\right)\\,dx $\n\nWe will use the property of modulus carefully.\n\nSince $|x|$ changes at $x=0$, split the integral into two parts:\n\n$ I=\\int_{-1}^{0}\\left(\\frac{x^3+|x|+1}{x^2+2|x|+1}\\right)\\,dx+\\int_{0}^{1}\\left(\\frac{x^3+|x|+1}{x^2+2|x|+1}\\right)\\,dx $\n\nFor $-1 \\le x Here, $|x|=-x$.\n\nSo,\n\n$ x^3+|x|+1=x^3-x+1 $\n\nand\n\n$ x^2+2|x|+1=x^2-2x+1=(x-1)^2 $\n\nThus,\n\n$ I_1=\\int_{-1}^{0}\\frac{x^3-x+1}{(x-1)^2}\\,dx $\n\nFor $0 \\le x \\le 1$\n\nHere, $|x|=x$.\n\nSo,\n\n$ x^3+|x|+1=x^3+x+1 $\n\nand\n\n$ x^2+2|x|+1=x^2+2x+1=(x+1)^2 $\n\nThus,\n\n$ I_2=\\int_{0}^{1}\\frac{x^3+x+1}{(x+1)^2}\\,dx $\n\nHence,\n\n$ I=I_1+I_2 $\n\nNow simplify both integrands.\n\nSimplifying $I_1$\n\nWe divide:\n\n$ \\frac{x^3-x+1}{(x-1)^2}=\\frac{x^3-x+1}{x^2-2x+1} $\n\nOn division,\n\n$ \\frac{x^3-x+1}{x^2-2x+1}=x+2+\\frac{2x-1}{(x-1)^2} $\n\nAlso,\n\n$ \\frac{2x-1}{(x-1)^2}=\\frac{2(x-1)+1}{(x-1)^2}=\\frac{2}{x-1}+\\frac{1}{(x-1)^2} $\n\nSo,\n\n$ I_1=\\int_{-1}^{0}\\left(x+2+\\frac{2}{x-1}+\\frac{1}{(x-1)^2}\\right)\\,dx $\n\nIntegrating term by term,\n\n$ \\int x\\,dx=\\frac{x^2}{2}, \\qquad \\int 2\\,dx=2x $\n\n$ \\int \\frac{2}{x-1}\\,dx=2\\ln|x-1| $\n\n$ \\int \\frac{1}{(x-1)^2}\\,dx=\\int (x-1)^{-2}\\,dx=-\\frac{1}{x-1} $\n\nTherefore,\n\n$ I_1=\\left[\\frac{x^2}{2}+2x+2\\ln|x-1|-\\frac{1}{x-1}\\right]_{-1}^{0} $\n\nAt $x=0$:\n\n$ \\frac{0}{2}+0+2\\ln 1-\\frac{1}{-1}=1 $\n\nAt $x=-1$:\n\n$ \\frac{1}{2}-2+2\\ln 2-\\frac{1}{-2} =\\frac{1}{2}-2+2\\ln 2+\\frac{1}{2} =-1+2\\ln 2 $\n\nSo,\n\n$ I_1=1-(-1+2\\ln 2)=2-2\\ln 2 $\n\nSimplifying $I_2$\n\nNow,\n\n$ \\frac{x^3+x+1}{(x+1)^2}=\\frac{x^3+x+1}{x^2+2x+1} $\n\nOn division,\n\n$ \\frac{x^3+x+1}{(x+1)^2}=x-2+\\frac{4x+3}{(x+1)^2} $\n\nAlso,\n\n$ \\frac{4x+3}{(x+1)^2}=\\frac{4(x+1)-1}{(x+1)^2}=\\frac{4}{x+1}-\\frac{1}{(x+1)^2} $\n\nSo,\n\n$ I_2=\\int_{0}^{1}\\left(x-2+\\frac{4}{x+1}-\\frac{1}{(x+1)^2}\\right)\\,dx $\n\nIntegrating term by term,\n\n$ I_2=\\left[\\frac{x^2}{2}-2x+4\\ln|x+1|+\\frac{1}{x+1}\\right]_{0}^{1} $\n\nAt $x=1$:\n\n$ \\frac{1}{2}-2+4\\ln 2+\\frac{1}{2}=-1+4\\ln 2 $\n\nAt $x=0$:\n\n$ 0-0+4\\ln 1+1=1 $\n\nSo,\n\n$ I_2=(-1+4\\ln 2)-1=-2+4\\ln 2 $\n\nAdding $I_1$ and $I_2$\n\n$ I=(2-2\\ln 2)+(-2+4\\ln 2)=2\\ln 2 $\n\nTherefore,\n\n$ \\boxed{\\int_{-1}^{1}\\left(\\frac{x^3+|x|+1}{x^2+2|x|+1}\\right)\\,dx=2\\log_e 2} $\n\nSo, the correct option is:\n\n$ \\boxed{\\text{Option B}} $",
