      "s": "JEE Main 2026 (Online) 6th April Morning Shift. Correct option: B. Let\n\n$$ I=\\int_{-\\frac{\\pi}{4}}^{\\frac{\\pi}{4}} \\frac{32\\cos^4 x}{1+e^{\\sin x}}\\,dx $$\n\nWe will use the standard property:\n\nIf\n\n$$ I=\\int_{-a}^{a} f(x)\\,dx, $$\n\nthen\n\n$$ I=\\int_{-a}^{a} f(-x)\\,dx $$\n\nand hence\n\n$$ 2I=\\int_{-a}^{a} \\bigl(f(x)+f(-x)\\bigr)\\,dx $$\n\nNow here,\n\n$$ f(x)=\\frac{32\\cos^4 x}{1+e^{\\sin x}} $$\n\nSo,\n\n$$ f(-x)=\\frac{32\\cos^4(-x)}{1+e^{\\sin(-x)}} $$\n\nUsing $\\cos(-x)=\\cos x$ and $\\sin(-x)=-\\sin x$,\n\n$$ f(-x)=\\frac{32\\cos^4 x}{1+e^{-\\sin x}} $$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$ f(x)+f(-x) = 32\\cos^4 x\\left(\\frac{1}{1+e^{\\sin x}}+\\frac{1}{1+e^{-\\sin x}}\\right) $$\n\nNow simplify the bracket:\n\n$$ \\frac{1}{1+e^{\\sin x}}+\\frac{1}{1+e^{-\\sin x}} $$\n\nLet $t=e^{\\sin x}$. Then $e^{-\\sin x}=\\frac{1}{t}$. So,\n\n$$ \\frac{1}{1+t}+\\frac{1}{1+\\frac{1}{t}} = \\frac{1}{1+t}+\\frac{t}{1+t} = 1 $$\n\nHence,\n\n$$ f(x)+f(-x)=32\\cos^4 x $$\n\nSo,\n\n$$ 2I=\\int_{-\\frac{\\pi}{4}}^{\\frac{\\pi}{4}} 32\\cos^4 x\\,dx $$\n\nThus,\n\n$$ I=16\\int_{-\\frac{\\pi}{4}}^{\\frac{\\pi}{4}} \\cos^4 x\\,dx $$\n\nSince $\\cos^4 x$ is an even function,\n\n$$ I=32\\int_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{4}} \\cos^4 x\\,dx $$\n\nNow use the identity\n\n$$ \\cos^4 x=\\left(\\cos^2 x\\right)^2 =\\left(\\frac{1+\\cos 2x}{2}\\right)^2 $$\n\nwhich gives\n\n$$ \\cos^4 x=\\frac{3+4\\cos 2x+\\cos 4x}{8} $$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$ I=32\\int_0^{\\frac{\\pi}{4}} \\frac{3+4\\cos 2x+\\cos 4x}{8}\\,dx $$\n\n$$ I=4\\int_0^{\\frac{\\pi}{4}} (3+4\\cos 2x+\\cos 4x)\\,dx $$\n\nNow integrate termwise:\n\n$$ \\int 3\\,dx=3x,\\qquad \\int 4\\cos 2x\\,dx=2\\sin 2x,\\qquad \\int \\cos 4x\\,dx=\\frac{\\sin 4x}{4} $$\n\nSo,\n\n$$ I=4\\left[3x+2\\sin 2x+\\frac{\\sin 4x}{4}\\right]_0^{\\frac{\\pi}{4}} $$\n\nAt $x=\\frac{\\pi}{4}$,\n\n$$ 3x=\\frac{3\\pi}{4},\\qquad \\sin 2x=\\sin \\frac{\\pi}{2}=1,\\qquad \\sin 4x=\\sin \\pi=0 $$\n\nAt $x=0$,\n\n$$ 3x=0,\\qquad \\sin 0=0 $$\n\nHence,\n\n$$ I=4\\left(\\frac{3\\pi}{4}+2\\right) $$\n\n$$ I=3\\pi+8 $$\n\nSo the correct answer is:\n\n$$ \\boxed{3\\pi+8} $$\n\nHence, Option B is correct.",
