      "q": "Let f : (a, b) $$\\to$$ R be twice differentiable function such that $$f(x) = \\int_a^x {g(t)dt} $$ for a differentiable function g(x). If f(x) = 0 has exactly five distinct roots in (a, b), then g(x)g'(x) = 0 has at least :",
      "qHtml": "Let f : (a, b) $$\\to$$ R be twice differentiable function such that $$f(x) = \\int_a^x {g(t)dt} $$ for a differentiable function g(x). If f(x) = 0 has exactly five distinct roots in (a, b), then g(x)g'(x) = 0 has at least :",
