      "s": "JEE Main 2026 (Online) 4th April Evening Shift. Correct option: C. Since the coefficients $a,b,c$ are real, complex roots occur in conjugate pairs.\n\nGiven two roots are:\n\n$$ \\alpha=1,\\qquad \\beta=1+i\\sqrt{2} $$\n\nSo the third root must be:\n\n$$ 1-i\\sqrt{2} $$\n\nHence the cubic polynomial is:\n\n$$ x^3+ax^2+bx+c=(x-1)\\bigl(x-(1+i\\sqrt{2})\\bigr)\\bigl(x-(1-i\\sqrt{2})\\bigr) $$\n\nNow first multiply the conjugate factors:\n\n$$ \\bigl(x-(1+i\\sqrt{2})\\bigr)\\bigl(x-(1-i\\sqrt{2})\\bigr) $$\n\nThis is of the form:\n\n$$ (A-iB)(A+iB)=A^2+B^2 $$\n\nwith\n\n$$ A=x-1,\\qquad B=\\sqrt{2} $$\n\nSo,\n\n$$ \\bigl(x-(1+i\\sqrt{2})\\bigr)\\bigl(x-(1-i\\sqrt{2})\\bigr) =(x-1)^2+2 $$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$ x^3+ax^2+bx+c=(x-1)\\bigl((x-1)^2+2\\bigr) $$\n\nLet $y=x-1$. Then:\n\n$$ (x-1)\\bigl((x-1)^2+2\\bigr)=(x-1)^3+2(x-1) $$\n\nNow expand:\n\n$$ (x-1)^3=x^3-3x^2+3x-1 $$\n\nSo,\n\n$$ x^3+ax^2+bx+c=x^3-3x^2+3x-1+2x-2 $$\n\n$$ =x^3-3x^2+5x-3 $$\n\nNow evaluate:\n\n$$ \\int_{-1}^{1}(x^3+ax^2+bx+c)\\,dx = \\int_{-1}^{1}(x^3-3x^2+5x-3)\\,dx $$\n\nUsing symmetry:\n\n$x^3$ is an odd function, so\n\n$$ \\int_{-1}^{1}x^3\\,dx=0 $$\n\n$5x$ is also odd, so\n\n$$ \\int_{-1}^{1}5x\\,dx=0 $$\n\nThus,\n\n$$ \\int_{-1}^{1}(x^3-3x^2+5x-3)\\,dx = \\int_{-1}^{1}(-3x^2-3)\\,dx $$\n\nNow,\n\n$$ \\int_{-1}^{1}x^2\\,dx=\\left[\\frac{x^3}{3}\\right]_{-1}^{1}=\\frac13-\\left(-\\frac13\\right)=\\frac23 $$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$ \\int_{-1}^{1}(-3x^2)\\,dx=-3\\cdot \\frac23=-2 $$\n\nAlso,\n\n$$ \\int_{-1}^{1}(-3)\\,dx=-3(2)=-6 $$\n\nSo total value:\n\n$$ -2-6=-8 $$\n\nHence,\n\n$$ \\int_{-1}^{1}\\left(x^3+ax^2+bx+c\\right)\\,dx=-8 $$\n\nThe correct option is:\n\n$$ \\boxed{-8} $$\n\nSo, Option C is correct.",
