      "q": "Let $\\mathrm{A}=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc}1 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1 & \\alpha \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1\\end{array}\\right]$ be a singular matrix. Let $f(x)=\\int_0^x\\left(\\mathrm{t}^2+2 \\mathrm{t}+3\\right) \\mathrm{dt}, x \\in[1, \\alpha]$. If M and m are respectively the maximum and the minimum values of $f$ in $[1, \\alpha]$, then $3(\\mathrm{M}-\\mathrm{m})$ is equal to :",
      "qHtml": "<p>Let $\\mathrm{A}=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc}1 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1 & \\alpha \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1\\end{array}\\right]$ be a singular matrix. Let $f(x)=\\int_0^x\\left(\\mathrm{t}^2+2 \\mathrm{t}+3\\right) \\mathrm{dt}, x \\in[1, \\alpha]$. If M and m are respectively the maximum and the minimum values of $f$ in $[1, \\alpha]$, then $3(\\mathrm{M}-\\mathrm{m})$ is equal to :</p>",
